The Minister informed the Ambassador that the Ministry is currently working to develop more irrigation infrastructure to meet the water needs of farmers in the context of global climate change. At the same time, the Ministry is preparing to compile various data related to water and meteorology as a technical basis for the research and development of the next generation.
The Minister also requested the Ambassador to examine the possibility of assisting the Ministry of Water Resources and Meteorology, especially on technical work.
The US Ambassador expressed his gratitude to the Minister for giving him the opportunity to pay a courtesy call and discuss work.
In response to the Minister of Water Resources' request, the Ambassador will explore the possibility of cooperating with the Ministry of Water Resources and Meteorology, especially on technical issues.
