Tomorrow, more than 30,000 people will gather at Koh Pich to celebrate the 41st anniversary of Resurrection Day
(Phnom Penh): January 7, 2020 Tomorrow is the 41st anniversary of the January 7 Victory Day, the day that Cambodians across the country were freed from the dead of the Democratic Kampuchea regime led by the genocidal group Pol Pot Khieu Samphan. Eang Sary and Nuon Chea.
Tomorrow, more than 30,000 Cambodians will gather on the grounds of the Koh Pich Center to celebrate their Victory Day and Resurrection Day. Samdech Techo Hun Sen, President of the Cambodian People's Party, and Samdech Ponhea Chakrei Heng Samrin, Honorary President of the Cambodian People's Party, will preside over the celebration of this great day for the nation and the people of Cambodia.
