Kampong Cham Provincial CamControl Officer Inspects Food Products Displayed at the Exhibition of Khmer Products and General Consumer Goods in Kampong Cham City
(Kampong Cham): Officials from Kampong Cham Provincial CamControl Branch, in cooperation with the Provincial Commercial Hospital and local authorities, inspected food items on display at the Cambodian Products and General Commodity Fair on January 6, 2020. Kampong Cham City, Kampong Cham Province, but did not find any defective goods.
According to Kampong Cham Provincial CamControl Branch Officer, CamControl Branch Officer, in cooperation with the Provincial Department of Commerce and local authorities, inspected the goods and searched for expired goods with incorrect labels, deformed packaging and instructed the traders. Vendors should be more aware of food safety and hygiene of the display, but do not find any defective and expired goods.
The official added that on that occasion, officials also distributed posters and disseminated to traders, vendors, consumers to understand the consequences of eating out of date and adding banned chemicals. Into the food as well.
At the same time, CamControl Kampong Cham Branch called on all traders to be careful and pay attention to the distribution and import of goods for resale.
