711 Rescue Team Wants to Expand Rescue Professionals (Video inside) (Phnom Penh): The 711th Rescue Unit of the 70th Brigade is a unit trained in fire, search and other disaster relief skills. Well. In the event of traffic accidents, fires and other disasters, the 711 rescue team is often seen operating to help the victims.
Brigadier General Chap Puth Davy, Commander of the 711th Brigade of the 70th Brigade, said that the 711th Brigade currently has more than 100 members. In addition to local training, the rescue squad also has the opportunity to conduct search and rescue training from friendly countries such as Japan and China.
In both rescue operations for victims of building collapses in Sihanoukville and in Kep, the 711 Rescue Team worked day and night with the utmost determination to rescue the victims, even though they were drowsy and exhausted. Seriously, though.
Brigadier General Chap Puth Davy told Fresh News during a rescue operation in Kep that her heart was the lifeblood of her team, never focusing on fatigue. The key is to help the victim get out of the accident.
Today, Cambodia has a lot of buildings, both low and high, while the population is also growing. With the rise of skyscrapers as well as population growth, social challenges and disasters can inevitably arise. With the challenge of emerging social problems and disasters, Cambodia is seen as responding to these problems still seem limited.
Rescue workers with expertise in rescue operations and disaster response, including fires and building collapses, are currently seen as the only 711 units. The number of rescue workers in this unit is still small, the rescue capacity is still lacking and the rescue equipment is not enough. These problems have led to rescue operations not yet responding effectively.
Colonel Chap Puth Davy agreed on these shortcomings. She wants to increase the number of rescue workers who specialize in disaster relief and increase the training of rescue workers to make the rescue operation more efficient. National Armed Forces Detain Two Men, Send to Court Involved in Checks and Money Laundering
(Phnom Penh): Two suspects were arrested by the National Gendarmerie and sent to the Phnom Penh Municipal Court on January 5 and 6, 2020 in connection with cases of cashless checks and money laundering.
Please note that the two suspects are currently under the action of Mr. Riel Sophin, Deputy Prosecutor of the Phnom Penh Municipal Court to open an investigation and decide to charge.
According to the police report, the first suspect, Chhong Dararith, male, and the second suspect, Sai Set, male, were arrested on the basis of a complaint filed by the victim, Hem Kuntheam, on charges of money laundering and non-compliance with trafficking instruments. Yes (cashless check).
Please be informed that the arrest of the two suspects took place on January 3, 2020, when they testified before the authorities during the preliminary investigation procedure at the National Gendarmerie Headquarters.
(Phnom Penh): Finally! On January 6, 2020, the Ministry of Interior approved the formation of the "Khmer Patriotic Party" by some former leaders of the former Cambodia National Rescue Party who had received political rehabilitation, but the Ministry required the party's representatives to prepare consistent documents. By law to register at once.
The response letter from the Ministry of Interior came after representatives of some former leaders of the former Cambodia National Rescue Party, Mr. Kei Sinoeun, applied to form the "Khmer Patriotic Party" using an acronym CKC on the 30th. December 2019.
Samdech Krala Hom Sar Kheng's letter to Mr. Kher Sinoeun stated as follows: The acronym (KKC) is headquartered at No. 17B10, Lum Road, Toul Roka 1 Village, Sangkat Chak Angre Krom, Khan Meanchey, Phnom Penh, in accordance with the provisions as stated in paragraph 1, Article 9 of the Law on Parties. "Politics."
The Ministry of Interior emphasizes in its letter that in order to be valid and able to act in accordance with the Law on Political Parties, the Khmer Patriotic Party must apply for registration with the Ministry of Interior in accordance with the second paragraph, Article 9, Article 14, new Article New 19 and Article 20 of the Law on Political Parties.
It should be noted that some former leaders of the National Rescue Party, which received political rehabilitation on January 2, 2020, announced the establishment of the "Khmer Patriotic Party" to contest the upcoming election.
