Building collapses have occurred in many countries around the world, killing hundreds of thousands of people, including the United States, Russia and India.
The following are the major building collapses recorded in 2019:
A four-story building collapse in Mumbai, India, killed 14 people and injured dozens in July 2019.
A 7-storey building collapse in Sihanoukville, Cambodia, killed a total of 28 people in June 2019.
A three-story building collapse in central Nigeria's Jos region in July 2019 killed 13 people and rescued seven others from the rubble.
A four-story apartment building collapse in western Ukraine killed eight people and injured dozens in August 2019.
