Armed Forces Crack Down on 71 Stocks of Rosewood Hidden by Traders in Cashew Plantation in Andong Meas District, Ratanakkiri Province
(Ratanakkiri): Under the direct command of Brigadier General Thao Yen, Commander of the Ratanakkiri Provincial Gendarmerie, the Provincial Gendarmerie, in cooperation with the local Armed Forces of Andong Meas District, patrolled their area and found a pile of wood in the plantation. The cashews of the people that the traders transported were hidden, waiting for a good opportunity and transported to Vietnam.
The above patrol operation took place on January 4, 2020 at the standard point (0751170.1546003) in Moy village, Nhang commune, Andong Meas district, Ratanakkiri province.
According to a report from the Provincial Gendarmerie, during the operation, eight Gendarmerie, in cooperation with two Forestry Administration Special Forces led by Lt. Col. Som Sophal, Director of the Security Planning Office, raided and confiscated the first pile of wood. 71 pieces equal to 11,387 cubic meters that traders transported and hidden in people's cashew plantations.
After the crackdown and confiscation of the above timber, the authorities also transported and stored at the security office 787 to proceed with the procedure.
It should be noted that in Ratanakkiri province, despite the efforts of the competent authorities and relevant institutions to crack down, there are still traders smuggling timber without fear of the law.
