The World Cycling Team has arrived at the top of Bokor Mountain!
(Koh Kong): After running the race from the roundabout of Say Phu Thong for about 5 hours, the national-international team and the event organizers arrived at the top of Bokor Mountain, Kampot Province, at a distance of about 172.5 km Meters for the second day of the first World Cycling Event along the Cambodian coast in 2020.
The World Cycling Shooting was held in the presence of Koh Kong Provincial Governor Mithona Phu Thong, Secretary-General of the Olympic Committee of Cambodia (NOCC) Vath Chamroeun at the Say Phu Thong Senior Circle at 11 a.m. today.
After qualifying from yesterday until now, there are about 75 players who still participate in the race.
Upon reaching the top of Bokor Mountain, the players and event organizers will rest there for one night before continuing the competition on the third day, which will start from the gate of Monivong Bokor National Park to Kep, where The end of the first World Cycling Event along the coast of Cambodia for 3 days.
