(Svay Rieng): A girl was bitten by a bee sting and died while being sent to the provincial hospital for treatment, but doctors were unable to save her because of the poison that spread all over her body. This case happened at 12:00 on January 4, 2020 in Thmey village, Sambour commune, Svay Teap district, Svay Rieng province.
According to Veasna, the victim of the girl, the victim, Ream Lina, over 6 years old, was in the second grade and was an excellent student in the class. Prior to the incident, the victim was riding a bicycle to buy cakes in the village. When she arrived at the stall, she stopped her bicycle near the beehive nest. Land.
The girl's family immediately sent her to Svay Teap District Referral Hospital for treatment. Due to the doctor's inability to treat, he was sent to the provincial hospital at 1:00 AM on January 5, 2020, and died at 3:00 AM.
The source added that the girl had a father named Ream Narin, 35 years old and a mother named Sim Srey Nak, 27 years old, a factory worker, had two children in the family and the girl was the eldest child.
Sources from the girl's relatives revealed that the Svay Teap district referral doctor did not pay much attention to the treatment, leaving the girl until she was seriously injured and sent to the provincial hospital. If sent to the provincial hospital on time, the child may not die.
