(Phnom Penh): The Ministry of Public Works and Transport (MPWT) has announced that a special personal registration number for a car or a registered license plate will be officially launched on January 7, 2020.
Please be reminded that the Head of the Royal Government of Cambodia, Samdech Techo Hun Sen, on June 3, 2019, decided to issue a new sub-decree on the registration of vehicle identification cards and vehicle license plates. The new sub-decree also states that vehicle owners can make special license plates according to their wishes.
This special license plate allows car owners to customize the letters or numbers to their liking and can also use the license plate for life. This was confirmed by Mr. Sun Chanthol, Minister of Public Works and Transport.
Procedures for the collection of revenue from special registration numbers, personal registration numbers and revenue management shall be determined by an inter-ministerial prakas between the Minister of Economy and Finance and the Minister of Public Works and Transport.
Heang Sotheayut, a spokesman for the Ministry of Public Works and Transport, once told Fresh News that the Ministry of Public Works and Transport was working to streamline the techniques and procedures for the special license plate. According to the spokesman, people may order a special license plate in the near future.
It should be noted that Senior Minister Sun Chanthol took the initiative to make this special license plate in order to raise funds for the nation from car users who want a special license plate.
