(Kampong Thom): Derivatives are a new financial instrument in the Cambodia Securities Exchange, or can be said to be a tool to manage various odds in the trading chain, such as exchange rate control, odds, gold and other commodities.
Speaking at the Derivatives Awareness Workshop in Kampong Thom Province on January 4, 2020, Mr. Sou Socheat, Director General of the Securities and Exchange Commission of Cambodia, called on all citizens and traders to find out about derivatives before investing in their cash. .
He said that derivatives trading can be successful only if all citizens and traders have the remaining cash, which means that the remaining cash in addition to other expenses, or in other words, the cash kept in the bank. Take the interest rate. So all this remaining cash can be turned into trading with derivatives, but all you need to do is find out about legitimate companies.
He added that for successful derivatives trading, investors need to find out about legitimate companies licensed or licensed by the Securities and Exchange Commission of Cambodia, as well as other relevant information to avoid investing in unlicensed companies. Legal permission.
The company needs to educate all investors to understand the risks to get long-term value and be able to attract more investment, trust from its customers.
