* Legal work
In the National Assembly session, members of the National Assembly, representatives of the Royal Government, discussed in detail before approving each draft law. Original Voice of the National Assembly Session (Discuss or raise national development)
* Citizen Representation and Monitoring
During this vacation, it is also an important opportunity for the National Assembly's expert committee to study and understand the field of work under its responsibility by meeting with citizens in the community, meeting with provincial and municipal leaders, and local authorities. Meet with ministries, departments, national and sub-national government institutions. Meet civil society organizations, development partners, as well as the private sector.
* Parliamentary Diplomacy
In strengthening parliamentary diplomacy and strengthening cooperation with friendly countries, National Assembly President Samdech Akka Moha Ponhea Chakrei Heng Samrin led a high-level delegation to pay an official visit to the Socialist Republic of Vietnam and the Lao People's Democratic Republic. From May 28 to June 1, 2019.
Dr. Nguon Nhel, First Vice President of the National Assembly, led a high-level delegation to attend the Second Executive Council Meeting and the 12th General Assembly of the Asian Parliament (APA) in Antalya, Turkey from December 12-19, 2019.
At the same time, every month, the leaders of the National Assembly and members of the National Assembly regularly meet with foreign delegations, diplomats and organizations. Samdech Akka Moha Ponhea Chakrei Heng Samrin, on behalf of the President of the institution, has played an active role in strengthening the parliamentary diplomacy. Goodbye after the end of the diplomatic mission from Cambodia.
In strengthening the parliamentary diplomacy, the National Assembly of Cambodia has an expert committee to fulfill this diplomatic mission: the Committee on Foreign Affairs, International Cooperation, Propaganda and Information, chaired by Mr. Chheang Vun. Domestic and foreign. In addition to the National Assembly's expert committee, members of the National Assembly have been involved in promoting parliamentary diplomacy in both multilateral and bilateral frameworks.
