Minister Thong Khon believes that the World Cycling Event will increase the attraction of tourists and investors to the coast of Cambodia.
(Koh Kong): Mr. Thong Khon, Minister of Tourism, expressed optimism that through the first World Cycling Event 2020, which is taking place from January 4 to 6, will help increase the promotion of tourism products, tourism potential. As well as increasing the attraction of tourists and investors to the coast of Cambodia, while the coast of Cambodia is also developing responsibly.
Minister Thong Khon made this statement at a press conference on the first World Cycling Event 2020 at the Darasakor Resort in Koh Kong province on the afternoon of January 3.
He outlined some of the objectives and benefits that Cambodia expects to achieve through the organization of this major world-class sports tourism event, including:
* Objective 1: Starting from the win-win policy of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, which has made Cambodia peaceful, politically stable and prosperous in all areas, including tourism has become a pillar. One of the mainstays of the Cambodian economy.
Today, Cambodia's coastal areas have become a potential and attractive tourist destination for tourism investment and for leisure tourists, full of a wide range of tourism products, especially beaches, islands, underwater resources, ecotourism sites and the region. Culture - Heritage and so on.
Mr. Thong Khon emphasized that "the organization of this World Cycling Event will also contribute to show the progress of Cambodia, which is an achievement of peace."
* Objective 2: To increase the promotion of tourism products, tourism potential, as well as increase the attractiveness of tourists and investors to the coastal areas of Cambodia. The event could also be an effective, innovative mechanism in line with today's modern market.
* The third goal is to train human resources as well as strengthen the capacity of the Cambodian Cycling Federation to prepare to host the 2023 SEA Games and for future events.
Please be informed that on January 4, the world cycling procession will depart from Darasakor resort to Khemarak Phoumin city (Koh Kong provincial town) with a total distance of 153.5 km.
