(Preah Sihanouk): For food safety as well as people's health, this morning, January 3, 2020, CamControl Preah Sihanouk Branch, with Mr. Bun Chamroeun as the Acting Branch Manager, continued to promote the quality of food safety at Stung Hav Market, Preah Sihanouk Province. Sihanouk found a total of 6.72 kilograms of defective beverages and cakes.
According to Preah Sihanouk Provincial CamControl Officer, during the inspection operation at Stung Hav Market, CamControl officers took some food samples for preliminary testing, including shrimp, squid, navy beans and lemongrass to find banned chemicals. May affect people's health.
According to the CamControl official, during the inspection to find the defective goods, as a result, the professional officers did not find the presence of banned chemicals on the food, but the professional officers found the defective goods out of date. 6.72 kg.
After that, the professional officer made a record of confiscating the goods and storing them at the Sihanoukville branch for destruction, and instructed other traders to understand and follow the law on quality control, safety of products, goods and services to avoid causing harm. Impact on people's health will be able to face the law further.
Kampong Chhnang Provincial Traffic Police Fines Illegal Land Trucks
(Kampong Chhnang): On the morning of January 4, 2020, several members of the Road Traffic Police Office, led by Brigadier General Ket Yong, Deputy Commissioner for Land Traffic of Kampong Chhnang Provincial Police, led a traffic police force to conduct a patrol operation. Technical inspections and fines for land trucks and bulky trucks along National Road 5.
The campaign took place after observing the anarchy of transporting land on national roads and bulky trucks without proper license plates and documents. The operation took place along National Road 5 in the territory of Samaki Meanchey district, Kampong Chhnang province. Bordered by Oudong district, Kampong Speu province.
Mr. KET YONG said that the inspection of land trucks at this time is in accordance with the plan of the Road Safety Committee and the order of Major General Khov Ly, Provincial Police Commissioner of Kampong Chhnang in order to prevent and reduce traffic accidents. To maximize the road and to improve the order of the road traffic to improve the participation in the implementation of the law on road traffic from road users.
During the inspection, the police found a car without a license plate, lack of driver's license documents, lack of vehicle identification card, transport business documents and underage drivers, etc. These fines are carried out in accordance with Sub-Decree No. 44 on Transitional penalties for violations of the Road Traffic Law. Throughout this morning, the provincial traffic police stopped nearly 30 trucks to inspect and fine.
