(Kampong Chhnang): A full-term pregnant woman died, both mother and child, while giving birth in a private maternity ward of the provincial obstetrician due to excessive bleeding during childbirth, the doctor created The child refused to send the patient to the provincial hospital in time.
The incident happened at 9 pm on January 2, 2020 at the private hospital of Yim Phalla in the north of Phsar Leu village, Phsar Leu village, Phsar Chhnang commune, Kampong Chhnang city, Kampong Chhnang province.
Mr. Seng Kimheng, the victim's husband, confirmed that his wife, Tuy Chakrya, 31, is a tailor living in Mong Barang village, Sangkat Peer, Kampong Chhnang city, Kampong Chhnang province. Before the incident, his wife was bleeding and she had to give birth every month, so he sent her to see a pregnant woman in a private ward named Yim Phalla, an obstetrician at Kampong Chhnang Provincial Referral Hospital.
At that time, Dr. Khim Phalla confirmed that his sister was fine and could give birth at his place for only one million riel. Upon hearing this, trusting Dr. Yim Phalla, the victim's family and husband decided to leave his wife to give birth there.
The victim's husband said that after giving birth, the baby was hopeless and the mother was getting weaker due to heavy bleeding, so the family urged the doctor. Phalla sent his wife to Kampong Chhnang Provincial Referral Hospital because his wife was not feeling well and was getting weaker.
At that time, Dr. Khim Phalla decided to send the patient to the Provincial Referral Hospital, but sadly, when the mother and baby were sent to the Kampong Chhnang Provincial Referral Hospital, it was too late and the provincial doctor could not save her. No, his wife was very weak and both mother and child died after being sent to the provincial referral hospital.
Immediately, the doctors of Kampong Chhnang Provincial Referral Hospital arranged to send the bodies of the mother and child by ambulance to the residence in Mong Barang village, Sangkat P'er, Kampong Chhnang city all night without issuing any letter.
At 9 am on January 3, 2020, Mr. Sorin Ravuthy, Director of Kampong Chhnang Provincial Referral Hospital, confirmed by telephone that at 9 pm last night, the provincial hospital received the above-mentioned maternity patients. She died at 9:30 pm due to excessive bleeding due to excessive bleeding.
The provincial doctors are very saddened by the delay in sending patients to the hospital.
He added that all hospitals and doctors are paramedics and do not want any patient to die or be sued.
