(Phnom Penh): The Cambodian-Chinese Chamber of Commerce Association estimates that after the closure of online gambling, more than 8,000 people in Sihanoukville lost their jobs. The Cambodian-Chinese Chamber of Commerce Association has convened an emergency meeting of company and enterprise leaders in the Sihanoukville Special Economic Zone to address this challenge.
The meeting was held this week with the participation of more than 40 Chinese factory and company executives. JIANG KEXING, secretary-general of the Cambodian-Chinese Chamber of Commerce in Sihanoukville, said Chinese companies setting up factories and doing business in Cambodia must actively fulfill their social obligations and help local people.
JIANG KEXING hopes that all enterprises should recruit workers who lose their jobs from the casino. He said that helping workers lose their jobs not only meets the needs of the company's own human resources, but also contributes to maintaining social stability and happiness of the people of Sihanoukville and set a good example for Chinese investors. Also.
The Secretary-General of the Association demanded that all Chinese factories fulfill their social responsibilities by re-employing workers who had previously left the factory and accepting new employees who wanted to work in local factories to improve the living standards of the people. Local and ensure social harmony by providing practical employment opportunities.
The owners of the companies and enterprises participating in these meetings accepted the request of the Cambodian-Chinese Chamber of Commerce and welcomed all Cambodian employees who want to work in the factory.
Sihanoukville Special Economic Zone, located 17 kilometers from Sihanoukville, is one of the most important locations in solving the problem of unemployment of staff and workers in Sihanoukville today. To date, Sihanoukville Special Economic Zone has 174 companies from China, Europe, the United States, Southeast Asia and other countries operating factories and employs nearly 30,000 people.
