Minister Hang Chuon Naron announces the appointment of Mr. Ros Sovacha as Secretary General of the Accreditation Committee of Cambodia
(Phnom Penh): Mr. Ros Sovacha, Spokesman of the Ministry of Education, Youth and Sports, has been appointed by the leadership of the Ministry of Education, Youth and Sports as the Secretary General of the Accreditation Committee of Cambodia (ACC). The ceremony was presided over by Dr. Hang Chuon Naron, Minister of Education, Youth and Sports on the morning of January 2, 2020.
Minister Hang Chuon Naron stated that the ACC plays an important role in strengthening the quality of higher education in Cambodia. The Minister of Education also instructed that the establishment of each unit requires the leadership, officials, staff to keep up to date, each time requires management and participation together.
On the occasion of taking this position, Mr. Ros Sovacha was committed to 7 points such as:
First, urge the ACC to strengthen the implementation of the principles of law, justice, transparency and acceptable results.
Fifth: Leading the ACC, respecting and implementing the Notification of the Office of the Council of Ministers No. 1883, dated December 19, 2019.
Sixth: Leading the ACC in accordance with the agreement of the Minister of Education, Youth and Sports on the letter dated November 8, 2019 on the results of the discussion of the private sector education working group on the relevant proposals for higher education.
Seventh, lead the ACC to promote the participation of all Cambodians in strengthening the quality of Cambodia in the sense of responding to the Cambodian economic vision 2030 and 2050 by strengthening the linking of each ACC annual action plan to the education strategic plan and education reform priorities.
