(Phnom Penh): Cambodia's diplomatic policy in 2019 is seen as vibrant and lively in line with the motto of the Royal Government, which states that "internal reform expands external friends in the spirit of independence." Through the vibrancy of diplomacy, Cambodia has had better relations with friendly countries, leading to strengthening cooperation in various fields to bring benefits to the nation and its people.
Through the visits of the Heads of State and Government, these eight friendly countries have contributed to the improvement of relations and cooperation between Cambodia and those friendly countries. The Heads of State and Government who visited Cambodia include:
Vietnamese Head of State Nguyen Phu Trong was Cambodia's first guest in 2019. After assuming the post of Head of State of Vietnam, Mr. Nguyen Phu Trong paid a two-day visit to Cambodia from February 25 to 26, 2019 at the invitation of His Majesty the King of Cambodia. King Norodom Sihamoni.
Nguyen Fu Chung's visit to Cambodia was warmly welcomed. During the visit, the Vietnamese Head of State paid a courtesy call on the King of Cambodia and His Majesty Queen Norodom Monineath Sihanouk, the Queen Mother of Cambodia, at the Royal Palace.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen and Mr. Nguyen Fu Chung met for more than an hour to discuss bilateral, regional and global issues. After the talks, Samdech Techo Hun Sen and Mr. Nguyen Fu Chung presided over the signing ceremony of five important documents, including:
* 1: Protocol Amending the Protocol for the Implementation of the Cambodia-Vietnam Agreement on Land Transport
* 2: Supplement to the amendment of Article 6 and Article 17 of the Agreement between Cambodia and Vietnam on water transport. Both protocols were signed by Mr. Nguyen Van Ther, Minister of Transport of Vietnam and Mr. Toch Chankosal, Acting Minister of Public Works and Transport of Cambodia.
* 3: Memorandum of Understanding on the provision of a grant of US $ 25 million for the implementation of the National Assembly building project. Signed by Mr. Dien Kien Yong, Minister of Finance of Vietnam and Mr. Leng Peng Long, Secretary General of the National Assembly of Cambodia
During the visit, Mr. Moon Jae-in paid a courtesy call on the King of Cambodia and met with Cambodian Prime Minister Samdech Techo Hun Sen.
In this bilateral meeting, Samdech Techo Hun Sen and Mr. Moon Jae-in both expressed their commitment to boost relations and cooperation between the two countries. In particular, promote trade, investment and tourism.
After discussing the work, Samdech Techo Hun Sen and Mr. Moon Jae-in co-chaired the signing ceremony of five important documents, including:
1: Coordinating Framework on Concessional Credit of the Economic Development Cooperation Fund for 2019-2023, signed by Deputy Prime Minister Prak Sokhon, Minister of Foreign Affairs and International Cooperation of Cambodia and Ms. Kang Kyung-wa, Minister of Foreign Affairs of the Republic of Korea.
2: Memorandum of Understanding between the Ministry of Mines and Energy of the Kingdom of Cambodia and the Ministry of Commerce, Industry and Energy of the Republic of Korea on Power Supply Project for Miniature Power Networks and Charging Stations in Cambodia Signed by Minister Suy Sem Ministry of Mines and Energy of Cambodia and Mr. Song Yoon-mo, Minister of Commerce, Industry and Energy of Korea.
3: Concessional Loan Agreement for the University of Health Sciences Hospital Project, signed by Dr. Aun Porn Moniroth, Deputy Prime Minister, Minister of Economy and Finance, and Mr. Eun Song-soo, President of the Export-Import Bank of Korea.
4: Memorandum of Understanding on Bilateral Cooperation between the Korea Trade Investment Promotion Agency and the Council for the Development of Cambodia for Korean Investment Facilitation Cooperation signed by Mr. Sok Chenda Sophea, Deputy Prime Minister and Secretary-General Of the Council for the Development of Cambodia and Mr. Quan Pyeong-o, President and CEO of the Korea Trade and Investment Promotion Agency.
5: Memorandum of Understanding between the Royal Academy of Cambodia and the National Research Council for Economics, Humanities and Sociology of the Republic of Korea, signed by Dr. Sok Touch, President of the Royal Academy of Cambodia and Mr. Song Kyung-ryeong, President of the National Research Council for Humanities and Economics And Korean Social Sciences.
During the visit, Mr. Moon Jae-in also met with Korean investors and people in the Korean community in Cambodia. During his first visit to Cambodia, Moon Jae-in and his wife fell in love with a temple in Siem Reap and visited the temple, a great Khmer treasure.
Moon Jae-in wrote a post on social media expressing his admiration for Cambodia's temples. During his visit, Moon Jae-in was seen as contributing to the development of relations and cooperation between Cambodia and South Korea to a better level.
Aung San Suu Kyi is the third guest to pay a three-day visit to Cambodia from April 29 to May 1, 2019 at the invitation of Cambodian Prime Minister Samdech Techo Hun Sen. The first visit to Cambodia by a strong woman in Southeast Asia and the winner of the Nobel Peace Prize has attracted a lot of attention from the Cambodian people. Her visit was also warmly welcomed.
During her visit, Ms. Aung San Suu Kyi paid a courtesy call on His Majesty the King of Cambodia, His Majesty King Norodom Sihamoni, and Her Majesty Queen Norodom Monineath Sihanouk, Queen Mother of Cambodia. She also paid a courtesy call on Samdech Vibol Sena Pheakdey Say Chhum, President of the Senate, and Samdech Ponhea Chakrei Heng Samrin, President of the National Assembly.
The presence of Aung San Suu Kyi was warmly welcomed by Samdech Techo Hun Sen. During the bilateral meeting, Samdech Techo Hun Sen and Aung San Suu Kyi agreed to further strengthen and expand bilateral relations and cooperation between the two countries. Ms. Suu Kyi mentioned cooperation in the fields of culture, religion, education and the economy.
At the same time, Samdech Techo Hun Sen also said that the year 2020 is the 65th anniversary of the relationship between our two countries, so we should jointly organize a solemn ceremony and promote tourism between the two countries. Especially in Siem Reap and Bakan, which are full of heritage temples. Samdech Techo thanked the Union of Myanmar for allowing Cambodia to build a temple in Myanmar and train Cambodian monks.
Samdech Techo called for review of overlapping taxes and other areas where the two countries have the potential to push for greater growth. In particular, increase the trade volume from $ 10 million to even bigger than before. She and Samdech Techo agreed to promote these important areas and also gave confidence to the Ministers of the two countries to continue to work.
After paying a courtesy call and discussing work with the Cambodian leadership, Aung San Suu Kyi also visited the Angkor and Bayon temples in Angkor, Siem Reap province. While visiting the Khmer temples in Angkor, Aung San Suu Kyi became very interested in an inscription with Burmese inscriptions attached to it.
Aung San Suu Kyi's official visit to Cambodia is a visit to further strengthen and expand bilateral ties and cooperation in all fields, as well as within the ASEAN and multilateral frameworks.
During the visit, Mr. Sama Oli also paid a courtesy call and discussed with Samdech Vibol Sena Pheakdey Say Chhum, President of the Senate, Samdech Ponhea Chakrei Heng Samrin, President of the National Assembly and Samdech Techo Hun Sen.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen warmly welcomed and welcomed Sama Oli's presence at the Peace Palace. During the meeting, Samdech Techo and Mr. Sama Oli discussed in-depth discussions on promoting bilateral cooperation in trade, investment, tourism, culture and education. Samdech Techo and Mr. Sama Oli also exchanged views on regional and international issues of mutual interest.
He told the Prime Minister of Nepal that without political stability and peace, not to mention investment and development. Samdech Techo Hun Sen congratulated Nepal on ending the flames of war and bringing political stability.
Before concluding his visit, Sama Oli also visited the Win-Win Political Monument, a symbol of ending the war in Cambodia.
5: Sri Lankan President Maithripala Srisena
Sri Lankan President Maithripala Srisena is the fifth leader of a friendly country to visit Cambodia. Mr. Maitripala Srisena, President of Sri Lanka, and his wife, Ms. Jayanthi Sirisena, paid a visit to Cambodia from August 7 to 10, 2019 at the invitation of the King of Cambodia, His Majesty King Norodom Sihamoni. .
During his visit, Mr. Maitripala Srisena paid a courtesy call on the King of Cambodia and met with Cambodian Prime Minister Samdech Techo Hun Sen.
2: Memorandum of Understanding between the Cambodian Chamber of Commerce and the Colombo Chamber of Commerce. Signed by Duke Kith Meng, President of the Cambodian Chamber of Commerce and President of the Sri Lankan Chamber of Commerce.
During this visit, to promote business between Cambodia and Sri Lanka, Samdech Techo Hun Sen and Mr. Maitripala Srisena also opened the Cambodia-Sri Lanka Business Forum.
Mr. Maitripala Srisena and his wife visited Angkor Wat and during this visit, Mr. Maitry Palasri Sena went to Wat Lanka to present the Bodhisattva tree from Anuradhapura, Sri Lanka to Samdech Preah Moha Arey Vong Saturday Chanthol. Preah Chao Athikar Wat Langka. The President also planted a tree representing Sri Lanka at the Phnom Udong Vipassana Center.
The visit of the oldest Prime Minister in the world was warmly welcomed and welcomed by Samdech Techo Hun Sen. During the visit, the Prime Minister of Malaysia paid a courtesy call on Samdech Vibol Sena Pheakdey Say Chhum, President of the Senate and Samdech Techo Hun Sen.
In a working meeting with Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Mr. Mahathea expressed his satisfaction with the closer friendship and cooperation between Cambodia and Malaysia in all fields, including trade and investment, halal industry development, defense and tourism security. Agriculture and education.
In this meeting, Samdech Techo and Mr. Mahathea stressed the importance of continuing to strengthen and expand cooperation and cooperation within the bilateral, regional and multilateral frameworks to serve the interests of the people of both countries and to contribute to Maintain peace, stability and prosperity in the whole region.
In addition to the issue of bilateral relations, Samdech Techo and Mr. Mahathea also exchanged views on regional and global issues. Samdech Techo Hun Sen and Mr. Mahathea presided over the signing ceremony of two documents, including:
1: Agreement on the Elimination of Overlapping Taxes, Exemption from Income Taxes and the Prevention of Tax Evasion and Tax Evasion, signed by Mr. Aun Porn Moniroth, Deputy Prime Minister, Minister of Economy and Finance, and Mr. Saifoudin Abdullah, Minister of Foreign Affairs Malaysia.
2: Memorandum of Understanding on Tourism Cooperation signed by Mr. Thong Khon, Minister of Tourism of Cambodia and Mr. Saifudin Abdullah, Minister of Foreign Affairs of Malaysia.
During the visit, Mr. Mahathea gave a lecture to about 700 Cambodian students at the Royal University of Phnom Penh (RUPP) on "Balancing Relations with Great Powers in the ASEAN Context".
In that speech, the Prime Minister of Malaysia praised the rapid development of Cambodia, including the construction of high-rise buildings throughout Phnom Penh. He claimed that when the plane landed at Phnom Penh International Airport, he noticed that Phnom Penh seemed to change rapidly, unlike when he first arrived, now that Phnom Penh has many high-rise buildings.
Mahathir Mohamad told Cambodian professors and students not to eat too much, which leads to premature aging and deterioration of the body. Mahathea is a doctor who graduated from the Faculty of Health and was also a health worker before entering politics.
7: Lao Prime Minister Thongloun Sisoulith
The Prime Minister of Laos, Thongloun Sisoulith, is the leader of the seventh friendly country to visit Cambodia in 2019. The Prime Minister of Laos paid a visit to Cambodia on September 12-13, 2019 at the invitation of Samdech Techo Hun Sen.
Thongloun Sisoulit's visit to Cambodia follows a series of misunderstandings between Cambodian and Lao troops in the border area of Preah Vihear province's Choam Ksan district. During the visit, Mr. Thongloun Sisoulit paid a courtesy call and discussed with Samdech Vibol Sena Pheakdey Say Chhum, President of the Senate, Samdech Ponhea Chakrei Heng Samrin, President of the National Assembly and Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia.
Through this visit, Cambodia and Laos have agreed to assign the Joint Boundary Commission of the two countries to jointly draft the Treaty on the Demarcation of the Border between the Kingdom of Cambodia and the Lao People's Democratic Republic. The border between the two countries has already demarcated 86% of the border line between the two countries.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen and Mr. Thongloun Sisoulit reaffirmed the importance of enhancing bilateral economic ties through joint efforts to increase trade and investment between the two countries, especially to increase bilateral trade. Electric power sector.
During the visit, Cambodia and Laos signed five important documents, including:
1: Memorandum of Understanding on Labor Cooperation between the Royal Government of Cambodia and the Government of the Lao People's Democratic Republic (Signed by Mr. Ith Sam Heng, Minister of Labor and Vocational Training and Mr. Kham Pheng Say Sampheng, Minister of Labor and Social Welfare) ).
2: Agreement on Energy Cooperation between the Royal Government of the Kingdom of Cambodia and the Government of the Lao People's Democratic Republic (Signed by Mr. Suy Sem, Minister of Mines and Energy and Mr. Kham Many Inthirath, Minister of Energy and Mines).
3: Electricity purchase agreement between Electricite du Cambodge and Electricite du Laos for the import of 500 MW of electricity from Attapeu Hydropower Plant, Laos (Cambodian side signed by Mr. Keo Rattanak, Deputy Prime Minister and Deputy Director General of Electricity of Cambodia) Remember the composition from the Lao side).
Janos Ader, President of the Republic of Hungary, is the eighth and last leader of a friendly country to visit Cambodia in 2019. Mr. Yanos Ador and his wife visited Cambodia from October 27 to 30, 2019 at the invitation of His Majesty the King of Cambodia, His Majesty King Norodom Sihamoni.
During the visit, Mr. Yanos Ader and his wife met with His Majesty King Norodom Sihamoni, King of Cambodia and His Majesty King Monineath Sihanouk at the Royal Palace.
Mr. Yanos Ader also met with Samdech Vibol Sena Pheakdey Say Chhum, President of the Senate, Samdech Ponhea Chakrei Heng Samrin, President of the National Assembly and Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia.
In a working meeting with Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Mr. Yanos Ader and Samdech Techo discussed focusing on bilateral cooperation in many fields, including regional and international issues.
During the visit, Mr. Yanos Ader and his wife also visited the temple, a great treasure of Cambodia in Siem Reap.
