(Kampong Chhnang): A suspect and an illegal fishing gear, a motor boat, were cracked down by the police while he was fishing in the Boeung Pra area, which is a watershed conservation area 7B.
The above cooperation in cracking down on the above fishing crimes took place at 1:10 pm on January 1, 2020, with the combined forces including: Sangkat Fisheries, Police Force, Community Administration Post, and People's Defenders. At Boeung Pra point, Kbal Kar Lang village, Pea Chkork commune, Chulkiri district, Kampong Chhnang province, after the force received clear information about the subjects reported by the fishing community.
According to the police, the suspect was 36-year-old Him Hoy, alias Hoy, and his wife, Preung Ratana, living in Daun Viet village, Kampong Hao commune, Kampong Leng district, Kampong Chhnang province.
Authorities said the suspect was also the subject of a crime that authorities have been pursuing for a long time. He often commits illegal fishing activities in the Prachulkiri Lake Conservation Area 7B and in other areas that are prohibited by the authorities, and the activities of the above suspects are often carried out in the quiet of the night.
During the crackdown, the police confiscated a ballast, an 18-horsepower gasoline engine, a pair of people and some fish. The suspects and exhibits were sent to Kampong Chhnang Fisheries Administration District for questioning and to build documents to be forwarded to Kampong Chhnang Provincial Court for processing.
Mr. Ly La, Director of Kampong Chhnang Fisheries Administration District, told Fresh News by telephone on the afternoon of January 2, 2020 that the suspect was led by a joint force led by Kampong Chhnang Fisheries Sangkat Chief in cooperation with the Joint Police Administration Police Force and the fishing community. And the people protect as well.
