(Phnom Penh): The Ministry of Interior has decided to select four capitals-provinces: Phnom Penh, Kandal, Kampong Cham and Siem Reap to study the procedures for re-providing land services at the sub-national level at the OWSOs. One by ensuring the provision of services to the people more easily, especially to increase revenue into the national budget.
He stated that the decision to study the land service procedures in the sub-national administration is to reform the provision of services to make it easier and better quality for the people, while the current procedures for providing land services at the OWSO. But there are complex difficulties, which is why the service is not very good.
During the meeting, Mr. Khuong Sreng supported the reform of the provision of territorial, urban and construction services at the capital-provincial level, saying that this would help solve many difficulties between service officials and service recipients more easily. First, that is, fast and quality.
He claimed that in the past, people have strongly supported the service in Phnom Penh, but also faced some challenges in providing services in a timely manner because the people who applied did not apply. Attached with enough documents, withdrawing documents back and selling them to others, many stages of documents, there are lawsuits, lack of fingerprints, people who are bound.
