Baghdad: Protesters angry over US airstrikes on an Iranian-backed Iraqi militia base attacked the US embassy compound in Baghdad on Tuesday. US President Donald Trump has directly accused Tehran of orchestrating the attack. This was released by the BBC on Tuesday, December 31, 2019.
In response to the attack, the U.S. military decided to use tear gas to disperse the protesters, who set fire to stones and stones on the fence and into the embassy. No arrests or injuries have been reported so far. But immediately after receiving the news, Donald Trump accused Iran of masterminding the attack and warned that Tehran would be held fully responsible for such actions.
