Chinese President Xi Jinping Wishes Happy New Year 2020
Overcoming the three major obstacles has been key to progress. Beijing, Tianjin and Hebei provinces have undergone joint development, the development of the Yangtze River Economic Belt and the construction of the Greater Guangdong, Hong Kong and Macao, and the integration of the Yongse Delta with rapid development of ecological conservation. And the high quality development of the fast river area has become a national strategy.
The "Year of Relief for Local Cadres" activities enables local cadres to perform their work more smoothly. Look all over China, everywhere there are new variations and new faces.
During the past year, I have been inspecting work in many areas. The new Xiongan County has begun to establish a vibrant Tianjing Port, Beijing's satellite center has emerged, Mongolia grasslands in a beautiful western corridor, the fast river has passed through thousands of years, still new, fast river, flexible, large Spacious on both sides of the Yangtze River, there are abundant resources, people have a prosperous life.
In 2019, China continued to be open to the world. We have organized the 2nd "Belt and Road" International Cooperation Forum, the Beijing Horticultural Expo, the 2nd Asia Civilization Dialogue and the 2nd China International Import and Export Fair, showing the world one China. Open, civilized and environmentally friendly.
I have met with many heads of state and government, sharing China's initiatives, strengthening and expanding ties, deepening consensus. A number of other countries have established diplomatic relations with China, bringing the total number of countries with China to 180. Our friends are all over the world!
A few days ago, I participated in activities to celebrate the 20th anniversary of Macau's return to China. I am proud and pleased with the prosperity and stability of Macau. The successful implementation in Macau has shown that the "one country, two systems" policy is feasible, achievable and popular.
In recent months, the situation in Hong Kong has received a lot of attention. Without a harmonious and stable environment, how can there be a peaceful home! We sincerely expect Hong Kong to be better, Hong Kong people to be better too.
A prosperous and stable Hong Kong area is the aspiration of Hong Kong people and also the expectation of all Chinese people. The river of history flows incessantly, sometimes calmly, sometimes with strong waves. We are not afraid of storms, nor are we afraid of obstacles.
China will firmly follow the path of peaceful development, safeguard world peace and resolutely promote common development. We are happy to work with the people of the countries of the world to actively build the "belt and the road", to build the common destiny of mankind, and to work tirelessly to create a better future for mankind.
At the moment, many are working in their roles, many are working for peace, many are working hard. You are all tired! Let us work hard now so that there will be no regrets in the future, let us together welcome the arrival of 2020.
The following is a series of news items that were published in detail on Fresh News Media regarding the 12 missions and visits of Cambodia's outstanding leader Samdech Techo Hun Sen abroad:
1: Samdech Techo Hun Sen visits China for 4 days in January 2019
The Prime Minister of Cambodia Samdech Techo Hun Sen led a high-level delegation to the Second "Belt and Road" Forum and other important meetings in Beijing, China for five days from May 25 to 25. April 29, 2019 At the invitation of Chinese President Xi Jinping.
During Samdech Techo Hun Sen's meeting with Chinese President Xi Jinping, Xi announced about 600 million yuan (about 90 million US dollars) in aid to improve Cambodia's defense sector. Samdech Techo Hun Sen Asks Chinese President to Continue Supporting About 700 Chinese Factories Doing Business in Cambodia to Continue Doing Business in Cambodia and To Encourage More New Chinese Investors to Do Business in Cambodia .
During the mission in China, Cambodia and China signed six major agreements, including:
Cambodia's Prime Minister Samdech Techo Hun Sen attends the 75th Annual Meeting of the United Nations Economic and Social Commission for Asia and the Pacific (UN-ESCAP) in Bangkok, Thailand on May 27. 2019.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen's four-day visit to Japan is not only to attend the 25th International Conference on "The Future of Asia", but also to meet with Japan's top leaders, Japanese investors and other international organizations. Provide important messages for Cambodian political and economic relations. Samdech Techo Hun Sen and a high-level Cambodian delegation arrive in Tokyo, Japan on the evening of May 28, 2019 for a four-day mission.
During the visit, Cambodia and Japan signed an exchange of letters on two grants from the Government of Japan, namely the implementation of the Economic and Social Development Program for the construction of 200 million yen (200 million yen) container terminal. Million US dollars. Cambodia's human resource development scholarship project worth 339 million yen, equivalent to more than 3 million US dollars.
The Prime Minister of Cambodia Samdech Techo Hun Sen led a high-level delegation to Hungary on the afternoon of June 13, 2019 for a two-day official visit. Fifth Asian Confidence-Building Measures (CICA) in Dushanbe, Tajikistan
On the occasion of meeting with Samdech Techo Hun Sen, the Prime Minister of Hungary announced his support for Cambodia in advocating for the protection of the preferential treatment under the All-Purpose Arms (EBA) program in the EU market.
The Prime Minister of Cambodia Samdech Techo Hun Sen attends the 34th ASEAN Summit in Bangkok, Thailand on June 22-23, 2019 under the theme "Promoting Partnership for Sustainability". . The meeting focused on enhancing cooperation and strengthening consensus among ASEAN members to address new global challenges.
The Prime Minister of Cambodia Samdech Techo Hun Sen led a high-level delegation to leave Cambodia at 8:10 am on July 2, 2019 to attend the "Global Review of Trade Aid for the Year" meeting. 2019 "at the World Trade Organization (WTO) in Geneva, Switzerland from 3 to 5 July 2019. The invitation comes at the invitation of WTO Director-General Roberto Azevedo.
During the visit, the two governments agreed to sign nine important documents, agreements and memoranda of understanding with the aim of strengthening relations and cooperation between the two countries.
First, an agreement on the provision of assistance between the Socialist Republic of Vietnam and the Kingdom of Cambodia in the amount of 3 million US dollars to implement the project to build some components of the National Center for Voluntary and Community-Based Treatment Services for Drug Addicts. Addiction in Sihanoukville from 2019 to 2020.
Second: Agreement to provide assistance on the construction of a new administrative building for the National Assembly of Cambodia.
Third, a Memorandum of Understanding between the Ministry of Economy and Finance of Cambodia and the Ministry of Finance of Vietnam on cooperation and mutual assistance in customs work was signed by representatives of the two countries' Ministries of Economy and Finance.
Fourth, the Memorandum of Understanding on the Development and Connection of Trade Infrastructure in the Border Area between the Socialist Republic of Vietnam and the Kingdom of Cambodia.
Fifth, the Memorandum of Understanding on the progress of construction and the handover plan of the Cambodian border model market in Tbong Khmum province between the Ministry of Industry and Trade of Vietnam and the Ministry of Commerce of Cambodia.
Sixth: Memorandum of Understanding on Trade Promotion Cooperation between the Ministry of Commerce of Cambodia and the Ministry of Industry and Trade of Vietnam.
Seventh: Memorandum of Understanding between the Ministry of Mines and Energy of Cambodia and the Ministry of Industry and Trade of Vietnam on Cooperation in the Power Sector.
In addition, the two Prime Ministers signed two other documents recognizing the two countries' border posts, which achieved 84%, including (1): the Supplementary Treaty on the 1985 State Boundary Treaty and the Supplementary Treaty. 2005 between the Kingdom of Cambodia and the Socialist Republic of Vietnam;
Details of Samdech Techo Hun Sen's official visit to Hanoi, Vietnam for 2 days (Video inside) 10: Official visit to the Czech Republic, Hungary and Bulgaria in mid-October 2019
The Prime Minister of Cambodia Samdech Techo Hun Sen led a high-level delegation to leave Cambodia on the morning of October 13, 2019 to visit and attend meetings in three European countries: Czech Republic, Hungary and Bulgaria. . Samdech's presence in Europe lasted for almost a week, from October 13 to 17, 2019.
The Prime Minister of Cambodia Samdech Techo Hun Sen and a high-level delegation of the Royal Government of Cambodia arrive in Jakarta, Republic of Indonesia, to attend the swearing-in ceremony of the President and Vice President of the Republic of Indonesia on the afternoon of October 20. 2019.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen, along with all ASEAN leaders, attends the 35th ASEAN Summit and related summits, which officially opened on the morning of November 3, 2019 at the Impact Exhibition and Convention Center on the outskirts of Bangkok. Nonthaburi Province, Thailand. (Click to read)
