Kien Svay District Authority and Investors in Koki Market Survey Concrete Road Project and Several Drainage System in Market
(Kandal): Mr. Por Seng, Investor of Koki Market and Kien Svay District Authority, led by Mr. Pov Kimly, Deputy Governor of Kien Svay District, inspected the concrete road project and drainage system in Koki Market, Kien Svay District on the afternoon of the 30th. December 2019.
The survey of the concrete road project and drainage system in Koki market was done at the request of the people and the spirit of the meeting on December 20, 2019.
Mr. Por Seng, Advisor Mr. Sim Ka, First Vice President of the Senate and President of Koki Market Investment Company, Kien Svay District, said that at the request of the people, the company plans to build two concrete roads along the entrance to the market with a total length of 255 4 meters wide and 255 meters long drainage system.
The company also plans to build a 2-meter-wide concrete road with a total length of 452 meters and a drainage system with a length of 255 meters. In addition to the concrete road and drainage system, the company plans to build a roof over the concrete road, which is made of galvanized iron so that people can not go to the market to buy shelter from the rain and water.
During the survey, a small number of vendors selling goods on the streets in the market also protested, and most of the vendors asked the authorities and the market commission to strictly enforce the law to make the project a success.
Seeing that the survey of the concrete road project and drainage system in Koki market has been protested by some vendors who sell goods on the road in this market, Mr. Pov Kimly, Deputy Governor of Kien Svay district, on behalf of the district authorities called on traders Please join us to improve the order and beauty of our market for 2020.
Mr. Pov Kimly continued that the construction of this concrete road was done to open the road to make it easier for people to enter the market.
In particular, the project to open a 4-meter-wide concrete road on both sides of the market is for trucks to transport garbage and for fire trucks to enter to put out the fire, because now the entrance to the market is narrow, which can not be trucks and garbage trucks. Transit traffic.
Mr. Pov Kimly confirmed that all these projects are budget projects of the Market Commission with the approval of the Department of Economy and Finance of Kandal Province.
