Cambodian and Chinese companies invest more than $ 10 million in 26-storey condominium project in Sen Sok
(Phnom Penh): A Cambodian and Chinese company have jointly invested in a condominium project called AKJ Bright Pearl, a 26-storey condominium with an investment of more than 10 million US dollars.
The AK-Bright building was completed this morning, December 31, 2019, located in Sangkat Phnom Penh Thmey, Khan Sen Sok, Phnom Penh, behind the National Bank.
Oknha Kouch Pheng, CEO of AKJ Thean Lu Property Development Co., Ltd., said that the condominium was built on an area of 1,200 square meters and an investment of more than 10 million US dollars. Related to this project, there are 286 condominium units and it is divided into 6 types of houses, which are scheduled to be completed in 2021.
Oknha Kouch Pheng said that the reason for investing in this location because in Sen Sok, especially behind the National Bank is a location that in the future will be strongly developed, it is believed that the development in this area will change significantly. In the future, there will be other projects in the surrounding area, which will transform the new Phnom Penh into a city and a modern, civilized town.
Oknha Kouch Pheng added that the AK Bright Bridge was built by a Chinese construction company. The Chinese company is one of the 500 largest companies in the world and is the builder of the Samdech Techo National Stadium in the area of Tycoon Ly Yong Phat and also the builder of the new building of Lok Sang Hospital.
According to Duke Kouch Pheng, "Our decision to invest in this condo is based on many factors, among which we see the potential of our Cambodian economy growing, and most importantly, political stability and development." The growth of our Cambodian economy gives us hope, confidence that sales are not a problem. We focus on customers, both local and foreign, because the style of our architecture is modern. ”
