The Czech Republic will no longer provide scholarships to students from developing countries from next year
Czech media reported on Monday that the Czech Ministry of Education, Youth and Sports will no longer provide scholarships to students from developing countries starting 2020. This was quoted from the Xinhua news agency on Tuesday afternoon, December 31, 2019.
From 2013 to 2019, through the Overseas Development Assistance Program, the Ministry of Education of the Czech Republic assists 130 foreign students studying at Czech universities each year. Scholarships provided by the Czech government cover both living expenses and a salary of more than $ 600 per month.
