(Phnom Penh): Cambodia has hosted the first Cambodian Coastal World Cycling Event from January 4 to 6, 2020, with races across four provinces: Koh Kong, Sihanoukville, Kampot and Kep. We are also working hard to organize this world event.
To organize this event smoothly, Mr. Thong Khon, Minister of Tourism and President of the National Olympic Committee of Cambodia, held a meeting with the last working group at the Ministry of Tourism on December 30, 2019.
On that occasion, the Minister said that the first World Cycling Event in the coastal area of Cambodia will promote the tourism potential of Cambodia's coastal areas and contribute to the production of human resources for the 2023 SEA Games in Cambodia.
The Ministry of Tourism, in collaboration with the Cycling Federation of Cambodia, is organizing a training course for Cambodian technical officers to obtain a UCI-accredited degree, which will cover both theory and practice, and practice will take time for the event.
Minister Thong Khon stressed that in addition to promoting the tourism potential of Cambodia's coastal areas, in addition to promoting Cambodian cycling, it also helped to increase the capacity of national athletes, human resources in the field of human resources in the field of hospitality and organization. A world-class event that will benefit from the organization of this first world-class cycling event.
The Minister called on all relevant provincial, district and municipal administrations to cooperate, promote and organize this work well in order to show tourists, national and international players about the hospitality to them and also to promote the image of the country. .
Ny Phally, Undersecretary of State at the Ministry of Tourism, said that so far about 20 teams have registered to participate, including three Cambodian teams and foreign teams from 16 countries.
It should be noted that the first Cambodian coastal cycling event, which was held in early 2020, will be divided into 3 stages: 1st race: Day 4 from Darasakor to Koh Kong town, 2nd: Day race 5th: From Say Phu Thong roundabout to Bokor mountain, passing through Prey Nob district, and 3rd: Race on the 6th from the foot of Bokok mountain to Kep province.
