(Phnom Penh): With only one day left, 2019 will be over and replaced by 2020. Throughout 2019, Cambodia and China achieved a lot of work based on the close relationship and cooperation between the two countries.
The Chinese Embassy in Cambodia has selected 10 events and activities as the main activities of 2019 due to the good relations and cooperation between the two countries. Top 10 events and activities that the Chinese Embassy considers important include:
1: Samdech Techo Hun Sen pays official visit to China
At the invitation of Chinese Premier Li Keqiang, Samdech Techo Hun Sen paid an official visit to China from January 20 to 23. This is Samdech Techo's first visit to China after the 2018 National Assembly election.
During the visit, Chinese President Xi Jinping announced about 4 billion yuan (nearly 600 million US dollars) in development assistance to Cambodia from 2019 to 2021. The President announced to continue to import 400,000 tons of Cambodian rice to China to help improve the lives of Cambodian farmers.
2019 is the year of cultural tourism between China and Cambodia. On January 30, the opening ceremony of the China-Cambodia Cultural Tourism Year was held at the Chaktomuk Theater in Phnom Penh.
The event is expected to contribute to enhancing relations and boosting tourism between the two countries. In 2018, Cambodia received more than 2 million Chinese tourists, ranking first. In the first 10 months of 2019, Cambodia received more than 2 million Chinese tourists, an increase of 24.4% compared to 2018.
From March 13 to 25, the "Golden Dragon Exercise between China and Cambodia 2019" was successfully organized by the Chinese and Cambodian troops in Kampot province. The theme of this exercise is joint counter-terrorism and humanitarian aid exercises, which include technical skills training, combat techniques training, sand table judging and military practicality, as well as shooting exercises. Really original.
More than 600 military officials from both countries took part in the exercise and used the first Z-9 military helicopters and other sophisticated weapons in the exercise. This is one of the largest military exercises in history. 4: 2019 is the year of law enforcement cooperation between China and Cambodia.
2019 is the year of law enforcement cooperation between China and Cambodia. On March 29, the launching ceremony of the Law Enforcement Cooperation Year was held in Beijing, China.
Zhao Kezhi, Member of the State Council, Minister of Public Security of the People's Republic of China, and Samdech Krala Hom Sar Kheng, Deputy Prime Minister and Minister of the Ministry of Interior, also addressed the ceremony, and the two sides signed the work plan for the year. Law enforcement cooperation between China and Cambodia, as well as the implementation of the law enforcement cooperation action plan.
On September 27, the China-Cambodia Law Enforcement Cooperation Coordination Office was finalized. It is the first police cooperation center in the two countries established by the Chinese police.
On April 28, 2013, Chinese Premier Li Keqiang and Cambodian Prime Minister Samdech Techo Hun Sen witnessed the signing ceremony of a joint Chinese-Cambodian community-building action plan between China and Cambodia.
On May 9, the first Cambodian banana export ceremony to China was held in Phnom Penh. The first 100 tonnes of Cambodian bananas exported to China started from Sihanoukville to Shanghai, China, and fresh Cambodian fruits have successfully entered the Chinese market.
This is an important event of agricultural cooperation between the two countries, it is a valuable experience for other agricultural products of Cambodia to export to China in the future. Participates in the Asian Civilization Dialogue Forum in China
At the invitation of Chinese President Xi Jinping, on May 13-16, His Majesty King Norodom Sihamoni, King of the Kingdom of Cambodia, welcomed the King to attend the Asian Civilization Dialogue. In Beijing, China.
His Majesty King Bhumibol Adulyadej addressed the forum and praised the Asian Civilization Dialogue, which provided significant benefits for the mutual study of the cultural relations of the two countries. The Cambodian people will stand firm with the Chinese people in all situations that arise.
On May 14, on the occasion of His Majesty the King's birthday, Chinese President Xi Jinping and the leaders of the participating countries held a special ceremony to celebrate his birthday. Also .8: The Royal Government of Cambodia announces the cessation of all online betting.
The ban on "online e-gambling business" has improved the investment environment in Cambodia, which could help regulate the activities of Chinese who have invested in Cambodia to create favorable conditions. More practical cooperation between the two countries in the future. 9: The book "Compass for Chinese people to Cambodia" has been published
On August 28, the Chinese Embassy in Cambodia hosted a statement on the day of the Consular Affairs Service and the "Compass for Chinese Citizens to Cambodia" at Phnom Penh International Airport.
Chinese Ambassador to Cambodia Wang Wentian and officials in charge of the Ministry of Tourism, the General Commission of the National Police, the General Department of Immigration and other relevant institutions also attended the ceremony.
On September 25, the Chinese Embassy hosted a reception to celebrate the 70th anniversary of the founding of the People's Republic of China in the City Hall of Diamond Island.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen and six Deputy Prime Ministers, as well as leaders of other political and military parties, attended the ceremony.
The Prime Minister and the Chinese Ambassador delivered a speech and wished the People's Republic of China prosperity and prosperity and wished China and Cambodia lasting friendship. This is a reception organized by the Embassy in the presence of Samdech Techo for the first time.
During the ceremony, Samdech Techo Hun Sen reaffirmed his one-China policy. The event also highlighted the close ties between the two countries and the special friendship between China and Cambodia.
