The inauguration ceremony for Ke Leng was presided over by Samdech Pich Sena Tea Banh, Deputy Prime Minister and Minister of National Defense of Cambodia and Chairman of the National Organizing Committee of the 23rd SEA Games on December 30, 2019. Presiding over the results of the Royal Cambodian Armed Forces (RCAF) sports work in 2019 and the direction of implementation at the Peace Palace.
Ke Leng has won four consecutive world championships: the gold medal at the 2013 World Championships in France, then in Thailand in 2015, in China in 2017 and finally in 2019, hosted by Cambodia. . France Signs Over $ 120 Million Concessional Loan Agreement to Cambodia for Water Treatment Plant and Skills Development Project
1. Concessional loan of 100 million euros (approximately US $ 101.4 million) for the construction of the Bakheng water treatment plant. Phase 2: Through this agreement, the French Agency for Development (AFD) will provide additional concessional loans. 100 million euros for the implementation of this project, following the first phase of the project.
This project aims to: 1. Construction of a pumping station with a production capacity of 195,000 m3 / day, 2. Install water mains, distribution pipes and pipe fittings; and 3. Supervise the construction work and support the capacity building of Phnom Penh Water Supply Authority on procurement and installation of water distribution network.
This project aims to: 1. Improve and improve the quality of technical and vocational education and training after secondary school, 2. Promote study and work in various industries and 3. Strengthen the financial management mechanism of technical and vocational education and training institutions (TVET) with innovation.
