The emphasis of Ms. Velisida De Susa Guterres was made in the presence of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, as she said goodbye to Samdech Techo this morning, December 30, 2019 at the Peace Palace.
According to Mr. Eang Sophalleth, Samdech Techo Hun Sen's personal assistant, during the meeting, the outgoing Ambassador emphasized that during her four years of work in Cambodia, her heart was with Cambodia. . She also expressed her admiration and admiration for Cambodia's economic growth during the four years of her work in Cambodia.
She emphasized that in the past four years, she has seen peace, stability, peace and stability, which has accelerated Cambodia's development.
The Ambassador also praised the Cambodian people. She said that the Cambodian people are happy and fresh, and the freshness of the people with peace and security is the most attractive factor for tourists to visit and invest in Cambodia.
In front of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, she also expressed her pleasure at becoming Timor-Leste's first diplomat to Cambodia. She also expressed her deep gratitude to the Royal Government of Cambodia for providing scholarships to East Timorese students to study in Cambodia, and those students are continuing their studies in Cambodia.
He said that Cambodia and East Timor are developing countries and therefore need to share experiences with each other. Samdech Techo stated that Cambodia has experience to distribute to East Timor and East Timor also has experience to distribute to Cambodia.
"The important thing is that we exchange experiences, learn from each other and use what we have to promote cooperation between the two countries for mutual benefit." These are the words of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, quoted by the press by Mr. Eang Sophalleth.
During the meeting, Samdech Techo also said that he was very happy that East Timorese students came to study in Cambodia. Samdech Techo said that Cambodia wants more foreign students to study in Cambodia to share knowledge between students and to be a student exchange program between Cambodia and other countries.
After the meeting, this morning, Samdech Techo Hun Sen also decorated her with a medal, a gift from the King of Cambodia, His Majesty King Norodom Sihamoni.
Samdech Techo Prime Minister expressed his congratulations to her for receiving this award.
