(Phnom Penh): A Chinese writer has brought paintings and calligraphy to a one-day exhibition in Cambodia with the aim of promoting Chinese literature and calligraphy and exchanging Chinese and Cambodian culture.
The exhibition of Chinese paintings and calligraphy was held on December 27, 2019 at the Phnom Penh Hotel.
Mr. Ly Yong, Master of Calligraphy, said at the opening ceremony that the exhibition was organized to promote Chinese literature and calligraphy, which has a rich history of thousands of years, especially to exchange Chinese and Cambodian culture.
Li said the Chinese nation has 5,000 years of heritage and culture. Chinese literature is made in depth and reflects the wisdom and reasoning collected from the Chinese people for thousands of years.
Chinese civilization has continued to be the spiritual bloodline of our nation and nation. From one generation to the next, all of us have passed through traditional Chinese culture, calligraphy is the foundation of Chinese culture and art.
Calligraphy has nothing to do with paper culture. The words used by the ink brush are true. As a scholar of Chinese literature, I am very proud to bring calligraphy to Cambodia.
Li Yong said that Chinese civilization and Cambodian culture are members of an ancient oriented cultural system. Cambodia and China have a long cultural history of one thousand eight hundred years.
He also stated that 2019 is the year of tourism and culture between China and Cambodia, he wants to make the cultural and civilized exchange between the two countries more beautiful by increasing mutual communication. Today marks the 21st anniversary of the end of the war in Cambodia! 11 Elements of Win-Win Politics Towards the End of the War
