In this morning's ceremony, after offering food and offerings to the Buddha image, the Rattanatrai Samathan Sila, then Dr. And invited members of the Constitutional Council to donate water.
After Samdech Preah Moha Areyvong, Dr. Preah Chao Athikar Charmon and offered water to Brahma, Mr. Kitti Nitikosal, Dr. President of the Constitutional Council and members offered incense and offered offerings to Brahma.
Mr. Kitti Nitikosal, Dr. President of the Constitutional Council and members donated 9 monks to the end of the program.
Please be informed that this Brahma Koh Ker style statue has been approved by the Constitutional Council as a symbol of the Constitutional Council since 1998, and until 2019, the Honorary Legal Doctor, the President of the Constitutional Council, has initiated the idea to build "White" Building, Office of the Constitutional Council of Chamkarmon State Palace.
The construction of this Brahma is a contribution to the promotion of the national cultural heritage and to preserve it as a legacy for future generations, because this Brahma-style image of Koh Ker is a unique sculptural art among the Khmer sculpture.
It should also be noted that in 2018, the Honorary Legal Doctor, President of the Constitutional Council, sent a delegation of the Constitutional Council to copy the scale of the Brahma Koh Ker style from the original statue kept at the Guimet Museum in France.
