Minister of Agriculture inspects cassava flour factory worth more than 30 million USD in Oyadao district, Ratanakkiri province, with a production capacity of 300 tons per day
(Rattanakiri): On the afternoon of December 27, 2019, Mr. Veng Sakhon, Minister of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries, inspected Chea Touch Company 'cassava flour factory located in Som Koul village, Som Thom commune, Oyadao district, Rattanakiri province.
According to the general manager of the factory, the company has invested more than 30 million US dollars to build the factory on an area of more than 40 hectares and was inaugurated on May 7, 2018. The factory has the capacity to produce 300 tons of noodles per day and needs about 1,200 tons of fresh potatoes. At present, 60 people have been employed at this base.
The same manager confirmed that all fresh potatoes were collected from farmers, mostly indigenous people, grown directly in this area at a price of 350 riel / kg, which requires a capital of 1,200 tons multiplied by 350 Riel / kg equals 420 million Riel / day. Currently, the main markets for noodles are India $ 480 / ton and China $ 400 / ton.
After inspecting the production line in the factory, the Minister praised and appreciated her efforts to establish this large cassava processing plant, which is beneficial to absorb local raw materials for processing, adding value. Help find cassava market and create jobs for local people.
