Samdech Techo Hun Sen praises the working style of the members of the Supreme Advisory Council, which is better than the previous opposition party (Video inside) (Phnom Penh): Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Head of the Royal Government of Cambodia on December 27, 2019 He praised the way the working group of the Supreme Advisory Council members worked better than the opposition MPs in the previous term.
At the closing ceremony of the meeting to review the work of the old year and the work direction of the new year of the Supreme Advisory Council, Samdech Techo Hun Sen emphasized that although there is no multi-party in the National Assembly, but the composition of the Supreme Advisory Council So much for social service.
The Prime Minister continued, "So these points, even though the multi-party situation does not exist in the National Assembly, but this multi-party situation is close to the engine of the executive branch." "This has become a culture of cooperation between political parties, which is not necessary until the swear word is called the opposition."
At the same time, Samdech Techo Hun Sen claimed that doing politics to serve society does not need to be biased by a small political party or a large political party, that is, it depends only on the will.
It should be informed that in the past 16 months, the members of the Supreme Advisory Council have visited more than 400 missions across 25 capitals and provinces and made a report accompanied by evidence on the issues they collected and submitted to Samdech Techo Hun Sen. Nearly 200 cases. In nearly 200 reports, the Supreme Advisory Council received 32 responses from Samdech Techo.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen: Samdech Sok Chet Receives Opinions from Political Parties with Different Opinions Better Than Foreign Orders (Video inside) (Phnom Penh): Addressed in front of members of the Supreme Advisory Council The Prime Minister of Cambodia, Sen Sok, stated that Samdech Sok Chet received opinions from political parties with different opinions rather than foreign orders.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen made this remark while presiding over the closing ceremony of the meeting to review the work of the old year and the work direction of the new year of the Supreme Advisory Council held at Sokha Hotel, Phnom Penh. In the afternoon of December 27, 2019.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that in the past 16 months, the Supreme Advisory Council has been active and provided many inputs through practical reports to improve inactivity, which is better than receiving orders from Foreign.
Of course, there are some points that we have mentioned in the meeting, some places are related to the role of the court, some places are related to the role of this class or that class, which requires more time, but some timely reaction raised by the class The leaders of all parties also pointed out the points that we need to address urgently. This is the confirmation of Samdech Techo Hun Sen.
The Head of the Royal Government of Cambodia further stated that the participation of the political parties of the Supreme Advisory Council is a demonstration of the full participation in the implementation of liberal, multi-party democracy for the coexistence and development of the society. .
Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that respect for the principles of the Constitution does not come from the drawing of foreigners, but from the will of the Cambodian people, the implementation of democratic politics in Cambodia must be based on the principles of peace Stable. Maintaining peace requires the participation of all political parties based on the principles of independence, democracy and the Constitution.
The assertion of Samdech Techo Hun Sen was made on December 27, 2019 at the closing ceremony of the meeting to review the work of the old year and raise the new work direction of the Supreme Advisory Council at the Sokha Hotel in Phnom Penh.
During the ceremony, Samdech Techo Hun Sen reminded about the advantages of the Supreme Advisory Council, which collected a lot of input, urging the Royal Government to solve those problems immediately.
Speaking at this point, Samdech also reminded about the case of pouring soil into the sea made by a two-star military officer in Koh Kong province in the past. "The reaction from the Cambodian Youth Party regarding the clearing of the sea, we have now ordered and given firmness, if you do not come out, will be disqualified," he said.
