(Ratanakkiri): The Chinese government has just allowed four more yellow banana growers in Cambodia to export fresh bananas to the Chinese market, after allowing five companies in the past. Nine companies have the right to export bananas to China.
This confirmation was made on the occasion that Mr. Veng Sakhon, Minister of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries, presided over the inauguration ceremony of the fresh banana packaging and export factory of Hang Anh Andong Meas, Hang Anh Lumphat, Daun Penh Agrico and Binh Phuoc Kratie. Robbie 2 Company to the Chinese market on December 28, 2019.
Mr. Nguyen Quan An, General Director and Representative of the four companies that have the right to export fresh bananas to China, highlighted the important achievements that each company has achieved since the beginning of investing in economic land concessions up to now, especially in relation to Progress of multi-crop production and the process of exporting fresh yellow bananas to the Chinese market.
He expressed optimism that by 2020, the company will increase the production of fresh bananas to 500,000 tons / year, in addition to mangoes, grapefruits, dragon fruit and Khmer need more than 15,000 local labor. He added that in addition to business work, which is the main object of investment, the company also pays attention to social work, health, education, housing for workers.
After inspecting the company's production and harvesting chain, Minister Veng Sakhon congratulated and praised the efforts to overcome and overcome all challenges to achieve success in the export of bananas. .
He also thanked the Chinese government through the General Department of Customs for evaluating the quality of Cambodian bananas and allowing the four companies to export more fresh bananas to the Chinese market. Importantly, the Chinese Customs Department also evaluated the company's banana packaging as the best quality and safety standard in ASEAN.
To achieve this goal, the Minister requested to continue to maintain cohesive cooperation with all stakeholders, especially provincial authorities in a spirit of high responsibility in accordance with the "public-private-development partners and communities" approach. However, support and promote the volume of Cambodian agricultural exports to international markets in the future.
Congratulating and supporting the inauguration of the four companies' fresh banana packaging and exporting factories to the Chinese market, the Minister called on the private sector to be able to consider and consider investing in agriculture, especially on Further processing of agricultural packaging to jointly reduce the export of raw materials, which is an important factor in adding value, creating jobs and improving livelihoods.
