APSARA Authority denies allegations that its officials took money in exchange for building permits in Angkor
(Siem Reap): The APSARA Authority confirmed to the public that according to a post on the social networking site Facebook on December 27, 2019, the APSARA Authority asked its officials to take money from 2 houses. $ 000 in exchange for wanting to apply for a house permit? When the law runs out, they have to pay another $ 1,000.
The above Facebook source also confirmed that many families in Veal village, Kork Chak commune were attacked by two people: one named Voeung Kreung and the other named Chea Hak Srun claimed to be an official of APSARA Authority and if anyone wanted to repair their house Or to build a house, you have to go through two of them first and then give them the money to ask the upper class to have the right to build the house.
In fact, a family has been persuaded by these two individuals to take more than $ 2,000 since August 2019, promising that in just one week, they will get a letter to build or repair their house.
Regarding the above mentioned, APSARA Authority denied and clarified as follows: According to the detailed examination, these two people are not officials of APSARA Authority.
In addition, all legal permits related to repair or construction are not required to be paid.
In this regard, the APSARA Authority encourages people living in the Angkor resort to follow the law in force to request repairs or construction to avoid plagiarism and believe in the propaganda of unidentified people.
