Oddar Meanchey Province Celebrates 13th National Day Against Human Trafficking 12 December 2019
(Oddar Meanchey): On the morning of December 27, 2019, Oddar Meanchey Provincial Administration celebrated the 13th National Day against Trafficking in Persons on December 12, 2019 under the theme "Working together to prevent, suppress, save and protect for Cambodia without human trafficking. "
The ceremony was held in the presence of Mr. Pen Kosal, Governor of Oddar Meanchey Province and Chairman of the Provincial Committee for Combating Human Trafficking and Mr. Siprasit, Chairman of the Provincial Council, as well as the leaders of the three Armed Forces, teachers, students and youth. Many other Cambodian Red Cross youth scouts.
This campaign will continue to spread the word in the provinces and in the media to spread awareness to people all over the country, especially in Oddar Meanchey.
The provincial governor said that human trafficking and sexual exploitation are a global context that continues to occur depending on three main factors: social education, law enforcement and seizing opportunities from perpetrators. The image of human trafficking is not only the trafficking or exploitation of labor and sex, but also a number of other phenomena that tend to lead to organ trafficking and cross-border smuggling of so-called surrogate mothers. .
This is a new concern that the Provincial Committee for Combating Human Trafficking has been taking measures to investigate, investigate and crack down in a timely manner and study the context of the relevant laws and regulations to avoid the spread of crimes that lead to more dangers. Many to society and people of all ages.
At the same time, the provincial governor also called on all relevant departments, municipalities and districts to pay more attention to the tricks of human trafficking perpetrators who have been trying to attract and push all kinds of citizens of all genders. Age to suffer to prevent and suppress in time.
