Key remarks by Samdech Techo Hun Sen on the occasion of closing the meeting of the Supreme Advisory Council
(Phnom Penh): Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, presided over the closing ceremony of the meeting to review the work of the old year and the new year on December 27, 2019. Set the direction for the new year work of the Supreme Advisory Council held at Sokha Hotel, Phnom Penh.
The following are the main remarks of Samdech Techo Hun Sen:
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen expressed his pride in the political situation in Cambodia through democratic mechanisms until the establishment of the Supreme Advisory Council.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that after 2023, he may request the party locomotive of the members of the Supreme Advisory Council to continue the validity of this institution.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen praised the way members of the Supreme Advisory Council work better than the opposition MPs in the previous mandate.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that although there is no multi-party system in the National Assembly, the composition of the Supreme Advisory Council has made a significant contribution to society.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that respect for the principles of the Constitution does not come from the drawing of foreigners, but from the will of the Cambodian people.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that the implementation of democratic politics in Cambodia must be based on the fundamental principles of maintaining peace and stability.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that maintaining peace requires the participation of all political parties based on the principles of independence, democracy and the Constitution.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that in the past 16 months, the Supreme Advisory Council has been active and provided many inputs through practical reports to improve inactivity rather than receiving orders. Foreign goods.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that Samdech Sok Chet received opinions from political parties with different opinions better than foreign orders.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen reminded that the land clearing activities in Koh Kong province received a report from Mr. Pich Sros's Cambodian Youth Party. Samdech Techo added the pouring of soil to clear the sea, if not, the removal of the person who poured this land.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that in 2022 and 2023, there is no need for all political parties to form an alliance with the CPP.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that for the commune and parliamentary elections, all political parties can act independently and in accordance with the law.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that the mechanism of the Supreme Advisory Council is not to diminish the power of the CPP.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that he was very satisfied with the suggestions of the members of the Supreme Advisory Council.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that without the Supreme Advisory Council, some reports would not have reached Samdech.
* Samdech Techo stated that the participation of various political parties of the Supreme Advisory Council is a demonstration of the full participation in the implementation of liberal, multi-party democracy for the coexistence and development of society.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen praised and highly appreciated the activities of the Supreme Advisory Council.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that under the roof of peace is an ideal for national development.
* Samdech Techo is optimistic and believes that the Supreme Advisory Council will continue to carry out beneficial activities for social reform.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that in the closing ceremony of this conference, Samdech did not make recommendations like other ministries and institutions.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that sometimes the policies put forward by the Royal Government are not all right.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that Samdech has no need to submit recommendations to the Supreme Advisory Council, leaving the possibility for all members to find out the mechanism and submit their work on their own.
