On December 27, 2019, Deputy Prime Minister Yim Chai Li, Chairman of the Council for Agricultural and Rural Development, inaugurated the Cambodia Business Center (Kunming) in Kunming, Yunnan Province, China. Chinese people.
In his speech at the time, Deputy Prime Minister Yim Chhay Ly informed the ceremony that the Cambodian Business Center was a place to promote and attract foreign investment and business to Cambodia through the display of Cambodian potential products and related documents. Cambodia's trade, investment, culture and tourism sector to Chinese investors, business people and people to explore business opportunities, invest and visit Cambodia.
The opening of Cambodian business centers in major cities in China is a strategy to promote trade, investment, tourism and culture, with centers being the focal point of information that Chinese investors, business people and the general public can access directly and at hand to explore. In-depth understanding of export products, business and investment potential, as well as the culture and tourism destinations of Cambodia in order to attract both traders, investors and tourists to Cambodia.
Deputy Prime Minister Yim Chhay Ly hopes that the Cambodian Business Center in Kunming, as well as other Cambodian business centers, will help promote comprehensive cooperation between Cambodia and China, as well as boost bilateral trade.
On that occasion, Deputy Prime Minister Yim Chhay Ly thanked the Chinese government and people for their continuous support and development in all areas of Cambodia, including the economy, society, security and people, and expressed confidence that the two countries would continue to work together. More good cooperation in the future.
Welcoming the presence of Deputy Prime Minister Yim Chhay Ly at the same time, Minister of Commerce Pan Sosak also informed that the Cambodian Business Center in Kunming, the sixth Cambodian business center, has opened five such centers. Already in Guangzhou, Heining, Xi'an, Hong Kong and Yantai.
With the five trade centers, as well as the agreements that Cambodia already has with China, Cambodia and China will also examine the possibility of reaching a bilateral free trade agreement in 2020, all of which will strengthen cooperation. Strengthen trade operations as well as create mutual benefits for the people of the two countries. Iraqi plane carrying 200 passengers forced to land in Russia after technical problems!
