The Cambodian Red Cross wishes Samdech Techo Hun Sen on the occasion of the New Year, Global Year 2020
(Phnom Penh): On the occasion of the New Year 2020, Samdech Chao Feang Kong Sam Ol, Permanent Vice President of the Cambodian Red Cross, sent a message of congratulations to Samdech Akka Moha Sena Padei Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of the Kingdom of Cambodia.
The following is the full text of Samdech Chao Feang's message to Samdech Akka Moha Sena Padei Techo Hun Sen: Samdech Krala Hom Sar Kheng outlines some priorities and necessities that the Royal Government is paying attention to in terms of administrative reform
(Phnom Penh): Samdech Krala Hom Sar Kheng, Deputy Prime Minister, Minister of Interior and Chairman of the National Committee for Sub-National Democratic Development, outlined some priority and necessary tasks that the Royal Government is focusing on. Administrative reform.
On the occasion of closing the General Assembly of the National League of Associations of Municipal, District, Khan, Commune and Sangkat Councils called the National League of Local Councils on the morning of December 27, 2019, Samdech Krala Hom Sar Kheng presented five priority tasks, including:
* First: Increasing the development resources of the commune administration:
Recently, the Royal Government issued Sub-Decree No. 121 dated 21 August 2019 on the transfer of additional resources from the state budget to the Commune / Sangkat Administration for local development expenditures from 2020 onwards, in which each Commune / Sangkat Administration Each will receive an average total budget of approximately $ 122,000.
* Second: the integration of the unit office and the transfer of staff into the new structure of the municipal, district and khan administration:
* Third: Ensuring the sustainability of the administration and the provision of services to the people in the process of restructuring the administration of municipalities, districts and Khans:
* Fourth: About the transfer of financial resources, assets:
Due to the transfer of financial resources associated with the functions transferred to the Capital, Province, Municipality, District and Khan Administration, therefore, the procedural financial management systems at those administrative levels need to be properly reviewed and adjusted to respond. To the new management structure of those administrations as well.
Regarding the transfer of assets as real estate, which can not be arranged in time, ministries and institutions must allow sub-national administrations to continue to use those assets and must continue to prepare the transfer form before the end of the first half of 2020. This face.
In order to ensure that the municipal, district and khan administration can operate under the new management structure and be able to effectively manage and implement the transferred functions, it is necessary to provide more capacity development to the sub-national administrative staff.
In the near future, the subjects to be trained should give priority to the main tasks related to the new functions and structures of the municipal, district, Khan administration, staff management procedures and procedures and the revised financial management system. To ensure the commencement of work under the new management system and structure of the municipal, district and khan administration.
In this regard, the National School of Local Administration is cooperating with the relevant ministries and institutions in preparing these training documents and must strive to complete training courses for all municipal, district and khan administrations by the first quarter of 2020. After that, continue to study and organize other necessary skills training courses from time to time.
In addition to the training organized by ministries and institutions at the national level, I request that the Association of Sub-National Administrative Councils continue to pay more attention to the development of the capacity of the Council of Sub-National Administration to lead, manage and monitor. Examine the effective implementation of transferred functions and resources, transparency, accountability and participation.
