(Phnom Penh): Seeing the importance of community building and agricultural contracting while producing and facing the lack of markets and falling vegetable prices, Veng Sakhon, Minister of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries Still urge farmers, especially vegetable growers, to organize as a community to easily find markets through contract farming with buyers to prevent falling prices.
The request of the Minister of Agriculture comes after a few days of complaints from some farmers in Battambang and other provinces who grow vegetables and lack a market and prices have fallen by the mouth of traders.
There are many important factors that lead to the mobilization of farmers as a community because:
First, when people are organized into farming communities properly, it will be easier to manage the planting in the cultivation and supply a stable product according to market demand through the cultivation of a variety and variety of crops.
Second, the establishment of community clusters makes it easier to negotiate and contract contracts with collectors because farmers ensure the amount of vegetables in accordance with their desired needs, which makes farmers more stable and affordable. Get a decent income.
Thirdly, the group of farmers' communities can easily obtain technology from the Ministry / Department of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries through modernization of agriculture, training in cultivation techniques, use of fertilizers, pesticides, etc. in accordance with market needs and may have Seed sponsorship and so on.
4: Together to form an agricultural community, easy access to credit to use as capital for business, which is also important for farmers.
Minister Veng Sakhon said, "The Ministry of Agriculture has been working hard to strengthen the capacity of agricultural communities. So far, 1,190 communities have been established to facilitate the Ministry of agricultural innovation and modernization." "Competitive environment and sustainability for the people to prosper and well-being."
However, the Minister stressed that the consequences of receiving limited financial assistance, which led to the assistance of farmers from the Ministry of Agriculture is not yet complete.
"Today, for the support of development partners and national resources provided by the Ministry of Agriculture, it is still limited to only a quarter of the more than 4 million farmers, we help only 1 million farmers," he said. "There are still more than 3 million farmers who have not been helped by the ministry due to the lack of financial support, including technical strength, so they do not want to have this problem, especially farmers outside the community."
Supreme Advisory Council plans to request the remaining annual budget to purchase mission vehicles
(Phnom Penh): The Supreme Advisory Council plans to request the Prime Minister of Cambodia Samdech Techo Hun Sen to use the remaining 2019 budget to buy a car for the mission on the ground. This is according to Mr. Chhim Phal Varun, Director of the Secretariat of the Supreme Advisory Council.
Speaking on the occasion of the meeting to review the work of the first 16 months and the work direction for 2020 of the Supreme Advisory Council, on the morning of December 27, 2019, Mr. Chhim Phal Varun said that all the work of the Supreme Advisory Council and Advise on the 2019 budget with a total amount of 1,318,925 US dollars.
He continued, "For the remaining budget, the Supreme Advisory Council intends to request in principle respect for Samdech Techo Prime Minister to give permission to use this budget to buy a car for the local mission, because in the past, both missions and delegations "Both the party and the secretariat use private cars because the Supreme Advisory Council does not have a car."
Mr. Chhim Phalvarun added that the request does not affect the 2020 budget and that the vehicles must be listed as state property.
