(Pursat): In response to the request of the village chief and commune chief as well as the people, Mr. Mao Thunin, Governor of Pursat Province, on December 26, 2019, led the specialized department to inspect the water supply situation. Dry rice cultivation in some irrigation systems at the ninth gate in Romlech commune to Boeung Kanseng in Otapong commune, Bakan district, Pursat province.
He also reminded that for the following years, farmers should listen to the announcement of the Ministry of Water Resources first to avoid dry rice because of the lack of water. He also instructed farmers to discuss with rice mills or agricultural agents who regularly visit to select rice varieties that are market demand and guarantee 100% export price.
At the same time, he also mentioned the purpose of meeting and relaxing with farmers all night at Boeung Kanseng in Otapong commune to know their well-being.
The farmers expressed their gratitude to Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, for bringing peace and development in all fields, especially for providing the irrigation system to the people of Bakan district. At the same time, the farmers also expressed their happiness and gratitude for the presence of Mr. Mao Thunin, Governor of Pursat Province, who came down directly to help solve and coordinate effectively.
At the same time, the development of irrigation system in Pursat province has also taken place under the strong efforts of the working group of the Ministry of Water Resources and Meteorology under the direct command of Minister Lim Kean Hor, who built the canal system. Maze in the provinces, not only in Pursat, to bring water to irrigate tens of thousands of hectares of farmers to get good yields during the harvest season.
The following is An Kun Kola's interpretation: The Confucius Institute at the University of Battambang is officially inaugurated!
(Battambang): The University of Battambang officially celebrated the inauguration of the Confucius Institute on the morning of Thursday, December 26, 2019. The institute is located on the campus of the University of Battambang.
The inauguration ceremony was presided over by Mr. Sar Sokha, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Education, Youth and Sports, Representative of Dr. Hang Chuon Naron, Minister of Education, Youth and Sports.
The opening of the Confucius Institute at the University of Battambang has four main objectives: first, to teach Chinese to the general public in northwestern Cambodia; second, to train Chinese teachers, organize Chinese language exams, and provide language teachers certification. China, third, information, social media, economics, culture, education, and fourth, joint doctoral research, doctoral scholarship programs in China, and young leadership scholarships.
Mr. Sar Sokha mentioned the diplomatic ties between Cambodia and China, which began on July 19, 1958, with King Norodom Sihanouk as its founder with the Chinese leadership. This road of communication continues to connect and expand under the wise leadership of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, and has become a strategic and comprehensive relationship, becoming a good friend, good neighbor, good brother and good partner.
Mr. Sar Sokha also mentioned the reform of the Ministry of Education, Youth and Sports on physical education and sports to prepare for the SEA Games in 2023, which Cambodia will host. It is noteworthy that the Cambodian sports sector has grown steadily, for example, our athletes have won a series of medals in the recent SEA Games.
Please be reminded that the Confucius Institute of the University of Battambang is the second institute in the Kingdom of Cambodia, where the headquarters of the Confucius Institute was approved to operate in late 2018 after the Confucius Institute of the Royal Academy of Cambodia in Phnom Penh in 2009.
Confucius Institute at the University of Battambang will open to all university students in Battambang to be officially enrolled from 2020 in subjects such as: Chinese along with IT, e-commerce, e-commerce, tourism, law. Engineering and Agriculture.
(Oddar Meanchey): Mr. Pen Kosal, Governor of Oddar Meanchey Province, told the people that under the leadership of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, the Prime Minister of Cambodia, Cambodia has maintained peace, freedom and progress in all areas.
On the morning of December 26, 2019, Mr. Pen Kosal said that the field of Buddhism has played an important role in serving the public. It is an effective center for the elderly, orphans and a repository of ideas, education, social morality for all levels of the masses, especially the youth.
The provincial governor still has a warm belief that Buddhism, our revered deity, will continue to play an important role in continuing to build, protect, maintain peace, and strengthen social stability for the nation and humanity through the Dharma, which is the advice of God. Samma Samput, the teacher who saved the nation from various disasters such as war, violence, drug trafficking, human trafficking, AIDS and other atrocities.
Mr. Pen Kosal continued that the Buddhist sector is connected with the empire and for Cambodia, the Buddhist sector has played a huge role in building and defending the nation, in which the Constitution states that "Buddhism is the religion of the state" and plays a role. Important in national development and strengthening national defense.
Mr. Pen Kosal also reminded local authorities and people to be careful of fire because this season is the dry season, there must be measures to store water for future use, because according to the forecast of the coming dry season in some areas There will be a shortage of drinking water.
The provincial governor urged all people, both Buddhist and imperial, to work together to build a nation for continuous progress under the leadership of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia.
