(Phnom Penh): With the attention of the leadership of the General Department and the Head of the Camcontrol Dry Port Branch in Phnom Penh, who always consider the health of the people in their daily diet, only on December 26, 2019, CamControl officials The Phnom Penh Dry Port has cooperated with the Toul Tompong Market and Boeung Tompun Market Commission to investigate and research to prevent defective goods, especially some fruits that affect the health of consumers.
Mr. Kong Vuthy, Deputy Director of Camcontrol Branch at the end of Phnom Penh Dry Port, who led the inspection, said that during the operation, the professional officers inspected the food on hygiene, the sale and introduced to educate the traders on food safety and fruit sampling. Fifty samples of the high-risk specimens, especially cherries, were sent to mobile laboratory vehicles for detection of banned chemicals, resulting in no banned chemicals.
He said that CamControl officials have advised and advised all traders not to secretly add other chemicals that affect the health of consumers, not only those who commit the highest risk because he is close. And is a direct contact with this substance.
Mr. Vice President stated that in order to be more convenient and have high confidence in the food from the people now in some markets, there are CamControl officers on duty if any people have any doubts that vegetables, fruits, food and groceries. Any chemical can be brought to CamControl officers for inspection and if there is any abnormality will be removed immediately.
In order to avoid any confusion, the Joint Committee on Border Affairs clarified to the national and international public as follows:
* Official border post 78 is a type of twin post, including post 78 (1) on the west bank of the Cham River on Cambodian territory in Choam Kravien commune, Memot district, Tbong Khmum province, and post 78 (2) on the east bank. Cham River on Vietnamese territory in Lok Ninh district, Binh Phuoc province. The border line in this area follows the middle of the Cham River. The official border post 78 is drawn on an official map approved by both countries.
* The creation of the fake border point 78 on the Google Map internet site came after a number of anti-government groups attacked the Royal Government for cutting off land for Vietnam after Cambodia-Vietnam signed a border document. Two of them were signed on October 5, 2019, including the 2019 Supplementary Treaty and the Khan Seima Protocol and the demarcation of the land border between the Kingdom of Cambodia and the Socialist Republic of Vietnam.
The Joint Committee on Border Affairs also called on our compatriots, both inside and outside the country, not to believe in the fraudulent posts of some unscrupulous people who often create false information with malicious intent to attack the Royal Government's border affairs.
The Joint Committee on Border Affairs reaffirmed to the national and international public that in the demarcation and demarcation of the border between the Kingdom of Cambodia and the Socialist Republic of Vietnam under the leadership of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia. To date, 84% of the common border line has been achieved and is continuing to be 100% completed to ensure territorial integrity and national sovereignty.
