Koh Kong Provincial Prosecutor Reminds Judicial Police Officers to Perform Ethically and Professionally
(Koh Kong): Mr. Ros Saram, Prosecutor of Koh Kong Provincial Court, reminded all judicial police officers and specialized departments to conduct their work in a professional manner to avoid the exploitation of state public property as property and use. Corruption.
Mr. Ros Saram's remarks were made on the afternoon of December 26, 2019 in a meeting between the units in the field of criminal justice to the Judicial Police Unit and specialized departments in the presence of Mr. Min Makara and lower officials. Advice and participation in all departments and institutions and held at the Koh Kong Provincial Court.
Mr. Ros Saram stated that in accordance with the instructions of the Ministry of Justice and the Prosecutor General of the Court of Appeal, the Court of First Instance and the Prosecutor General of the Court of First Instance must hold at least three meetings of the Judicial Police in each court jurisdiction. Per year.
In this meeting, he asked the participants to raise as much as possible the problems encountered during the implementation to unite to solve together to find solutions in accordance with legal procedures.
He stated that the opening of today's meeting for three main purposes, including:
* 1: To regularly follow the instructions of the Ministry of Justice and the Attorney General of the Court of Appeal to help resolve the challenges between the Judicial Police Unit and the relevant units, including the judiciary.
* Second, to strengthen the working relationship of solidarity to create efficiency, productivity and efficiency of the performance of roles and responsibilities between the judicial police unit and the judiciary.
* Third: To find out the main criminal principles in the implementation of the Dharma Police function under Cambodian law, such as: the action of criminal complaints, the search for evidence and the minutes of the Judicial Police, which will be discussed in detail in the meeting. This.
Veteran was rejected by his girlfriend after stepping on a landmine in Kampong Thom province, now receiving a house from Samdech Techo Hun Sen
Lt. Gen. Som Sun confirmed that Lt. Col. Om Hak had joined the battalion in 1984 in the former 36th Battalion and was crippled by a landmine in the battle of Ny Pech village, Ny Pech commune, Kampong Svay district, Kampong Thom province in early 1993. . Lt. Col. Om Hak is a single man without a wife, currently living with his sister and nephews (before he was disabled, he had a girlfriend ready to be his fiancé, but after he became disabled, his girlfriend refused to marry him).
Lt. Gen. Som Sun also confirmed that the back of the 139th house was built of wood high above the ground, a staircase, a wall and a 4-by-6-meter corrugated iron roof, built by the Sandan District Veterans Association Committee. Kampong Thom Veterans Association Committee, by order of Senior Minister Kun Kim, Secretary General of the Cambodian Veterans Association.
During the handover ceremony, the working group of the Cambodian Veterans Association of Kampong Thom Province brought a gift from Lt. Gen. Dr. Hun Manet to support him with 100 kg of rice, 2 boxes of noodles, 2 bags of fish sauce and soy sauce. 420,000 Riels.
The families of veterans, the people and the local authorities would like to express our deepest gratitude to Samdech Techo Hun Sen, who always pays all kinds of attention to the lives of our veterans.
