Today is the last day for the recruitment exam, the results will be announced on January 29, 2020
(Phnom Penh): For December 26, 2019, this is the last day of the cadet recruitment exam, with 8,063 female candidates applying for the exam nationwide, and the exam results will be announced on January 29, 2020 is coming. This was confirmed by Major General Su Sokha, Deputy Director of the Royal Cambodian Armed Forces Sports Center and Deputy Director of the Phnom Penh Municipal Examination Center.
The lieutenant general said that for the recruitment exam, the officers will be divided into two stages: on December 22, all candidates will take the general knowledge exam, and on December 24 to 26, the physical exam Fitness at the old stadium.
According to Major General Su Sokha, on December 23, for the active officer exam, on the 24th, the Army officer, on the 25th, and on the 26th This December, which is the last day, is the military technical officer exam.
The lieutenant general added that there are more female candidates who have tried their best to win the exam, and this year there are more female candidates who have applied for the exam than in previous years in the field of sports in which they are candidates. All contestants are capable as well.
Candidates' examinations take place in the districts where they applied for the exam, including: Phnom Penh at Bak Touk High School, at Military Zone 1 at Hun Sen Stung Treng High School, Military Zone 2 at Kampong Cham Regional Teacher Training Center, Military Zone Third at Chea Sim High School, Takeo, at the 4th Military Zone at Angkor High School, Siem Reap Province and at the 5th Military Zone at Preah Monivong High School, Battambang Province.
Wesleyan International Day Celebrates ASEAN Tourism Destinations
(Phnom Penh): The International Wesleyan Day 2019 was held under the theme of tourism destinations in ASEAN, including Malaysia, Indonesia, Singapore, Thailand, the Philippines, Vietnam, Brunei, Laos, Myanmar and Cambodia.
ASEAN Tourism Destinations took place on December 25 at Wesleyan School, Santhor Mouk Branch, with five main objectives, including:
1: Provide in-depth analysis and understanding of the factors that contribute to the success of tourism in these countries 2: Understand the diversity of the cultural, political, social, educational and economic environment of those countries 3: Promote and strengthen solidarity Among the 4 students, teachers and staff: Implement the 7 habits and TLIM concepts, especially the leadership role of each student in The Leader in Me 5: Improving 21st Century Skills.
Mr. O Saroeun, Director General of Westline School, Santhor Mouk Branch, said that so far the school has done it five times. He said that the first time, the topic of ASEAN countries, the second time, the topic of Khmer from the time of birth to the present, the third time, the topic of countries in East Asia, the fourth time the topic of superpowers. Top 10 economies in Asia, and the fifth theme on the high tourism potential of ASEAN.
Mr. O Saroeun said that students who can participate in research in this program is called until they know English, whether children, adults, primary and secondary, and they are distributed to research. This research is guided by teachers.
He added that the goals of the ASEAN Tourism Day are threefold: first, students want to know the success of each tourism sector in ASEAN, second, students know all about their civilization and culture, including economy, politics, clothing, status. All the tourist areas have food, what is there ?, and thirdly, want the students and teachers to cooperate and the staff to participate together.
Ly Hiek, a student at Wesleyan School, expressed her interest in the program, saying that through this program, she gained knowledge as well as good experiences for future use. Those knowledge and experience include education, economy, culture from other countries in ASEAN.
"In the past, I remember being told about the Khmer era, which instilled in students a love for our homeland," he said. As we all know, the next generation of Cambodians is strongly influenced by foreign cultures, and when we program to explain each era, we can know how to manage different cultures, beliefs, as well as the economy of that era. ”
Lee Hiek added that the program also gives students a sense of leadership, which is an important goal the school wants to provide. The young woman recalled that while participating in this program, they collaborated and shared their research work, with some researching economics, culture, customs and food.
"We can also compare our country to where our country lacks, and draw on good experiences from other countries to fill those gaps," he said.
"This is also a concern because it is a problem in the relations between regions, regions, countries, but the palm oil war between Indonesia, Malaysia and Europe will continue until there are measures," he said. "Response from Indonesia to Europe."
Indonesia is the number one country, while Malaysia is the second largest exporter of palm oil to the world market. Both countries are under threat from the European Union. In the past, the European Commission has ruled that the use of palm oil is a catalyst for deforestation and should be eliminated.
In early December, Indonesia filed a complaint with the World Trade Organization (WTO) against the European Union over plans to reduce biofuels from palm oil for automobiles. The lawsuit could escalate trade disputes between Indonesia and the European Union, which plans to end its use of biofuels by 2030.
Indonesia has threatened retaliation and imposed a ban on EU alcohol imports to its country.
(Phnom Penh): A karaoke business location owned by Nguon Srey, located in Chong Khsach Village, Sangkat Toul Sangke I, Khan Russey Keo, which stubbornly disobeyed instructions and continued to play noise without a license, was closed on December 25, 2019. It was finalized after Mr. Chea Pisey, the district governor and a member of the secretariat of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, the Prime Minister of Cambodia, received complaints from the people through the social network Facebook.
Several instructions were received after receiving complaints until the final closure of the karaoke business venue owned by Nguon Srey, which caused a disturbance to the above residents, led by Mrs. Sous Solida, Deputy District Governor and Village-Sangkat Authority. And some other relevant officials.
Mr. Chea Pisey said that before reaching the decision to close the karaoke business, the village-sangkat authorities had instructed the business owners to reduce the volume and stop playing music until nightfall. On the other hand, the owners of this place are still stubborn and continue to make noise again and again, affecting the lives of the people, in addition to finding the business unlicensed and located in an unregulated area on the railroad tracks.
The district governor warned that after the closure of the karaoke business, which disturbs the lives of the people, and if the owner does not follow the instructions, that is, the district administration will continue to open. Take action to confiscate materials and store them without being responsible for any damage or loss. Thirty-three men and women were arrested by police during an operation to crack down on online pawn shops and games in Takhmao City, Kandal Province.
(Kandal): Kandal Provincial Police under the direct command of Major General Eav Chamroeun, Provincial Police Commissioner, launched an operation to crack down on pawn shops and open two online games in Takhmao City, arresting 33 men and women. This transaction was made on December 25, 2019.
According to the report of Kandal Provincial Police, obtained by Fresh News on the afternoon of December 26, 2019, the first location is in Takhmao Thmey Village, Sangkat Takhmao, Takhmao City, Kandal Province, where the owner is Seng Piseth. Male Address: # 207, Street 114, Prek Samrong Village, Sangkat Takhmao, Kandal Province. Among them, 16 people were arrested, including 2 women.
According to the report, the second location is on Street 109, Takhmao Thmey 2 Village, Sangkat Takhmao, Takhmao City, Kandal Province. Arrested 18 suspects (2 females) and tested the urine of 17 drug addicts, 1 female. Exhibits seized 2 motorcycles and 4 mobile phones.
The results showed that the above location has online gambling business without a license, with young people visiting both day and night, a place where drugs are used, traded and distributed. Currently, this case is being handled by the provincial authorities and the Takhmao City Inspectorate.
(Kampong Chhnang): Most of the people in Prek Reang village, Teuk Hot commune, Rolea Bier district, Kampong Chhnang province are engaged in weaving red mats for sale, which can weave 80 to 100 mats in 3 to 4 months in one season. Income from 3 million to 4 million riels per family.
Under another aunt's house, two teenage girls, 10 and 12 years old, were weaving mats. Mats to help mothers earn money to support the family, which in one day they can weave small mats to help earn some money for the family.
Prek Reang villagers, who weave red mats, also appealed to Cambodians to support the purchase of red mats by Prek Reang villagers in order to preserve their work and heritage left by their ancestors, and also to help improve people's lives. People in rural areas to have jobs and live a comfortable life.
