JAKARTA: December 26, 2019 marks the 15th anniversary of the worst tsunami disaster that has killed more than 230,000 people in four countries. The eastern Indian Ocean, such as Indonesia, Sri Lanka, India and Thailand, has suffered the most.
Today, 15 years ago, more than 200,000 people were killed in Aceh province on the Indonesian island of Sumatra as a result of a massive earthquake caused by a submarine earthquake near Sumatra. Vibration up to 9.1 magnitude.
That natural disaster was named one of the worst natural disasters in human history on earth. Apart from Indonesia's Aceh province, it has also severely affected the living and economic conditions of countries along the coast of the Indian Ocean, including Sri Lanka, India and Thailand.
To this day, Indonesians will never forget the great tragedy, especially for those who survived the tsunami but lost their loved ones. Every year, the Aceh provincial administration holds a program to commemorate the 2004 earthquake and tsunami tragedy.
