In addition, Samdech Techo Prime Minister also said to maintain the stone bridge in front of Battambang Provincial Hall, which is more than 100 years old. Samdech also advised to find ways to build more bridges there.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated: "In the past, we were surprised that we were trying to hit the bridge in Battambang, the bridge of the French era. Please note that what is left over 50 years is Khitam Reaksa. Ah, it has become an achievement, and that is more than 100 years, what should I do? Try to keep it repaired, how to prevent it from breaking.
"Battambang provincial authorities just want to avoid the danger of the people how to prevent people from passing through it. "But instead we have to find a way to build more bridges there, not to demolish them." Samdech emphasizes further.
Please note that after the disagreement from the Ministry of Culture and Fine Arts, including the public about the project to demolish the old stone bridge left over from the French colonial era in front of Battambang Provincial Hall, on the night of December 19, 2019, the Battambang Provincial Administration Come out and declare your position that this ancient stone bridge will be preserved without being demolished.
In her letter, Ms. Phoeung Sakona stated that the old stone bridge left by the French colony in front of Battambang Provincial Hall in Kamakor Village, Sangkat Svay Por, Battambang City-Province should not be demolished because it is more than 100 years old. On the other hand, this bridge is the only remaining urban heritage building in Battambang province and the only remaining in Cambodia with historical, architectural, urban and environmental value.
The minister added that the bridge, considered a rare heritage, should be preserved and repaired and used as a pedestrian bridge. The proposal to preserve this stone bridge has led to a lot of support from the Cambodian people, both in Battambang as well as in other provinces, where they want to preserve this historic building.
