(Siem Reap): Eight ancient ponds in Daun Keo commune, Puok district, Siem Reap province, located in the Angkor resort area, have been allowed to be restored for the benefit of the villagers for storing water for use in the dry season as well as for the benefit of the community. Round.
The above 8 ponds include: Kak pond, Lpeuk pond, Veng pond, Ta Sneh pond, Kok pond, Treas pond, Tras pond, Pranet pond and Chhok Snay pond.
These eight ancient ponds have already been evaluated by the specialized department and should be allowed, but this restoration should be avoided to be used for business or profit.
In principle, the APSARA Authority always cooperates with local authorities who want to restore ancient ponds in order to keep the ponds intact, avoiding the use of other sites or pouring soil when it is shallower.
In addition, it is also the work of maintaining and conserving the remaining ancient ponds to prevent fraudsters from stealing private property when these ancient ponds are out of water. EDC suspends electricity supply in some areas at different times and places. From today to December 29 to carry out repair work, installation of equipment and dismantling of network lines to create conditions for road widening
