(Phnom Penh): The Ministry of Economy and Finance presented the results of the third meeting of the National Council for Social Protection under the presence of Dr. Aun Porn Moniroth, Deputy Prime Minister, Minister of Economy and Finance and Chairman of the National Council for Social Protection. This is according to the press release of the Ministry of Economy and Finance, which was received by Fresh News on December 25, 2019.
The third meeting of the National Council for Social Protection was held this morning, December 25, with the participation of Mr. and Mrs. Chea, Vice Chairman and members of the National Council and leaders, as well as professional officials from relevant ministries and institutions. To review and discuss the following important agenda:
1: Progress of cash support program for pregnant women and children under 2 years old:
In the future, the Ministry of Health will promote the dissemination of additional training to health officials in the implementation of this program in accordance with the authority, as well as cooperation to prepare to hand over this task to the Ministry of Social Affairs, Veterans and Youth Rehabilitation to lead the implementation on a regular basis.
2: Mechanisms and legal standards for the transfer of cash support programs for pregnant women and children under 2 years of age to the Ministry of Social Affairs, Veterans and Youth Rehabilitation:
In the past, the Ministry of Social Affairs, Veterans and Youth Rehabilitation, which is in charge of this work, has continued to work closely with relevant ministries and institutions and a number of development partners to develop work mechanisms, including the preparation of manuals, the provision of tablets to officials. Responsible for commune work, and training commune officials throughout the country.
3: Progress of the implementation of the social security system:
In order to ensure the security of the income of public officials and to contribute to reducing the gap between old and new retirees, in 2019, the Royal Government fully covered the cost of pension subsidies, with the Royal Government allocated 926,671 million Riels. .
The meeting also reviewed and approved the draft sub-decree on the establishment of the Social Assistance Subcommittee of the National Social Protection Council and the priority action plan for the development of the social protection system for 2020.
Prey Veng MPs Inspect Water Pumping to Help Irrigate Rice in Svay Antor District
(Prey Veng): Mr. Sok Pheng, Member of Prey Veng Constituency, accompanied by the Provincial Department of Water Resources and relevant authorities, inspected the pumping condition on December 25, 2019 to help irrigate dry rice in Svay Antor district. Water for farming to increase this yield.
Regarding the pumping of water to save the dry rice of the people in Svay Antor district, Mr. Sok Pheng said that the Provincial Department of Water Resources and Meteorology has released two medium-sized machines with 65 horsepower to pump water to save. Dry rice of the people in two communes: Angkor Tret and Damrei Puon communes, Svay Antor district, Prey Veng province, which is equivalent to 14 villages that can irrigate more than 600 hectares of rice on more than 600 hectares.
Mr. Sok Pheng also said that the Department of Water Resources and Meteorology of Prey Veng Province has released 14 medium-sized water pumps and 2 floating pumps with 65 horsepower to pump water to save rice. Available in Pearang, Sithor Kandal, Svay Antor, Ba Phnom and Peam Chor districts.
Mr. Sok Pheng also donated 1 million Riels for the construction of a canal in Damrei Puon commune, which cuts through two villages. Chamkakuy and O'Kandol village and also supported the people who own 444 liters of water pump from the canal to the rice field.
