(Phnom Penh): On December 26, 2019, Mr. Sak Setha, Permanent Secretary of the Ministry of Interior, opened the 3rd General Assembly of the National League of Associations of Associations of Municipal, District, Khan, Commune and Sangkat Councils (National League of Local Councils) organized For the purpose of reviewing, revising and approving the statute for the election of the Chairman, Vice-Chairman of the National Executive Committee and the National Council for the third mandate.
The General Assembly was attended by 470 people, including 320 delegates from Municipal, District, Khan, Commune and Sangkat Councils, with the presence of the Chairman of the Council and the Board of Governors of the Capital and Provinces, as well as Senators, National Assembly members, representatives of relevant ministries and institutions of the Royal Government. Government.
The National League of Local Councils was established with the aim of enhancing the capacity development capacity of municipal, district, Khan, commune and sangkat councils, protecting the legitimate interests and interests of its members.
The General Commission of the National Police Continues to Hold the 25th Private Security Agency Skills Training to Improve and Strengthen Capacity
(Phnom Penh): The General Commission of the National Police through the Department of Private Security Management this morning, December 26, 2019, continued to hold the 25th Private Security Agency Training Course to ensure that private security agencies have the full capacity to participate in the work. Protect security, order and safety according to the goals as well as the society as a whole.
Speaking on the occasion, Lt. Gen. Lim Sokharasmey, Director of the Department of Private Security Management, said that at present, the private security sector has grown significantly in line with the country's development in all areas, and this sector has contributed to maintaining security, order and social security. Absolutely.
Lt. Gen. Lim Sokharasmey emphasized that the private security sector must have high quality and benefits for the protection of security, safety and public order, so all private security agencies must be competent, understanding and professional.
Seeing all these values, the General Commission of Police, which is headed by the Department of Private Security Management, organized this refresher course with the main purpose of understanding the duties and responsibilities of the private security sector on maintaining order and capacity building. Improving private security agencies means making them more effective in protecting social security.
He sincerely hopes that all participants will make an effort to listen to Veal Khmin explain and apply this knowledge to fulfill their role in a positive way with high efficiency to protect the private interest, public and society as a whole. .
Remarks by Samdech Techo Hun Sen Presenting Diplomas to Nearly 3,000 RULE Students at National Institute of Education
(Phnom Penh): Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, on December 26, 2019, presided over the graduation ceremony of approximately 2790 graduates from the Royal University of Law and Economics (RULE). 1,380 women. The graduation ceremony took place at the National Institute of Education.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that he was very pleased to present the diplomas to the students of the Royal University of Law and Economics before the end of the year.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that from 1982 to the present, the Royal University of Law and Economics has provided education to a total of more than 50,000 students.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen calls for a search for images that he taught at the Royal University of Law and Economics during the Cambodian state.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that he was very proud of the progress of the Royal University of Law and Economics.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that through the school school policy, the school has made this school develop.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen calls for the preservation and display of images of Phnom Penh's past after its liberation from the genocidal regime.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that rebuilding the country is much more difficult than building a new city.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen said that today's youth are very lucky compared to the youth of the past. The youth of the past lost the opportunity to study because of the war between 1970 and 1975 and from 1975 to 1979.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that between 1979 and 1998, young people had many opportunities to study, but there were also those who lost opportunities because Cambodia has not yet completely ended the flames of war.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that other structures that are 50 years old or older must be maintained. At this point, Samdech confirmed that the French-era bridge in Battambang province was not demolished.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that after higher education, the number of female students began to decline. Samdech Techo advised to jointly encourage more women to study after higher education.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that Cambodia is influenced by many European cultures, including dress. Samdech Techo Hun Sen asked for the face of the creator and arranged to wear a tie. Samdech Techo considered wearing a tie a mess.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen praised Muslims for maintaining their traditional dress without being influenced by the West.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that the Royal University of Law and Economics is a university that receives interest and study from foreign students.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen wants the Ministry of Agriculture to divide the area for cultivation. That is, what areas should be cultivated and what areas should be cultivated, especially areas that lack water.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen saw that some land in Prey Veng province was cultivated by sugarcane people with good results, which he wanted to consider when considering which areas have potential for crops to divert the people's cultivation.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that some people hated the communist regime, but instead urged the Royal Government to establish a communist market regime by having Samdech set the price of rice.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that rice pricing is a planned market, a practice of the socialist country.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that for the Royal Government of Cambodia, it was only an appeal, but could not set a price.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen continues to call on landlords not to increase house and room rates beyond what workers receive.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen called on the authorities to work with landlords to prevent problems with rents and rooms to ensure that workers benefit from wage increases.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that the collection of revenue from customs and tax institutions exceeded the plan up to 1,400 million US dollars. Samdech Techo considers this a success on public budget reform.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that this year Cambodia may have up to 9 million tons of rice left. Samdech Techo proposes to consider and promote rice exports.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that the policy on the agricultural sector is to boost rice production and export 1 million tons of rice per year. But this policy is not the only one, it is a policy to promote rice production, but rice exports do not meet the target.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that Cambodia is currently trying to attract investors to process rice into rice for export, because processing rice into rice is more profitable than exporting rice to neighboring countries.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that relying on the garment industry can not make the national economy grow well, it is necessary to expand modern industry, especially on technology.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen wants to see the production industry of toys and toys, which is currently in high demand in Cambodia as well.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that South Korean television is controlling almost the entire world market.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen is waiting to see North Korean gifts for the Christmas of the West.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that whether the North Korean gift, the missile launch or the political message that will reach any agreement between the United States and North Korea.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that if China, Japan and South Korea agree, it will also facilitate ASEAN.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen calls for a meeting between China, Japan and South Korea to have a positive impact on the economy in Asia.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen said that a trade agreement between the United States and China, as announced by President Donald Trump, is good for the world economy.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that Indonesia and Malaysia's palm oil trade war with the European Union is a concern and will not end easily.
