This Thursday's eclipse is an annual eclipse that will spread from Saudi Arabia to India and South Asia. According to the map presented by the experts, the countries that will be able to see 100% full solar eclipse are Saudi Arabia, Oman, southern India, Sri Lanka, Indonesia's two largest islands, Sumatra and Kalimantan, Kuala Lumpur-Malaysia. Brunei, Singapore and the southern Philippines.
