This Morning, Samdech Techo Hun Sen Presents Diplomas to Nearly 3,000 RULE Students at National Institute of Education
(Phnom Penh): Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, on the morning of Thursday, December 26, 2019, presided over the graduation ceremony of graduates from Royal University of Law and Economics (RULE) about 2,790, including 1,380 women. The graduation ceremony took place at the National Institute of Education.
According to Ministry of Education, Youth and Sports spokesman Ros Sovacha, today's graduates have bachelor's and master's degrees.
The Royal University of Law and Economics is a state-run higher education institution that has played a key role in training human resources in law, economics, and other areas to serve Cambodia's economic and social development.
According to the university report, from 1982 to the present, there are a total of 54,889 students and 20,409 female graduates from this university. There are 158 foreign students, 53 females. Currently, the graduates are working in government, private sector, national and international NGOs and starting their own businesses.
At present, the university has a board of directors, management, staff, faculty and lecturers of 585 national and international contracts, 146 females and 16,296 students, 8,059 females.
According to the university report, 93.69% of the graduates are employed, of which 93.16% are undergraduates and 98.27% are undergraduates. .
Minister Thong Khon and Governor of Kampong Thom Distribute Land Certificates to More Than 100 Families in Taing Kork District
(Kampong Thom): Mr. Thong Khon, Minister of Tourism and Chairman of Kampong Thom Provincial National Working Group and Mr. Sok Lou, Governor of Kampong Thom Province, on December 25, 2019, distributed leaflets on 124 people. People (representing 124 families) living in Kork Trabek village, Sra Lao commune, Tang Kork district, each family received 5 hectares of land.
The village of Kork Trabek above is an important remote area where Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia and Samdech Kittipritthbandit Bun Rany Hun Sen have always taken care of and built many achievements of the Empire and Buddhism, including temples, schools, and infrastructure. .
Minister Thong Khon instructed the above-mentioned people to use this land to their full potential and to preserve it for future generations, never to sell it again. On the other hand, the land title deed cannot be used for resale of their land.
At the same time, the Minister called on the people in Kork Trabek village to be ready to save enough water for use in the dry season this year. For dry farming, please do it once, but when the harvest is over, people can also grow other crops, especially watermelon, cucumber, soybeans, vegetables and so on.
He also reminded the people in that area to remember the gratitude of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Samdech Kitt Prith Bun Rany Hun Sen and the Royal Government of Cambodia, which always pays attention to the people in Kork Trabek village as well as the people in Nationwide. He said that although the leaders are far away, the worries, anxieties, memories and thoughts of the people in the area along the Tonle Sap Lake are never far away.
