(Phnom Penh): Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, will preside over the graduation ceremony of graduates on Thursday, December 26, 2019. About 2,790 from the Royal University of Law and Economics (RULE), including 1,380 women. The graduation ceremony will take place at the National Institute of Education.
According to Ros Sovacha, a spokesman for the Ministry of Education, Youth and Sports, the graduating students will have bachelor's and master's degrees tomorrow.
The Royal University of Law and Economics is a state-run higher education institution that has played a key role in training human resources in law, economics and other areas to serve the economic and social development of Cambodia.
According to the university report, from 1982 to the present, there are a total of 54,889 students and 20,409 female graduates from this university. There are 158 foreign students, 53 females. Currently, the graduates are working in government institutions, the private sector, national and international NGOs and starting their own businesses.
