In 2019, CMAC found and destroyed more than 360,000 landmines, clearing an area of nearly 67 million square meters
(Phnom Penh): Mr. Heng Ratana, the Royal Government Delegate in charge of the Director General of the Cambodian Mine Action Center (CMAC), confirmed that in the first 12 months of 2019, CMAC found and destroyed a total of landmines and unexploded ordnance. More than 36,165 munitions, including 5,415 anti-personnel mines, 75 anti-tank mines, 15 improvised explosive devices and 30,660 unexploded ordnance.
Mr. Heng Ratana summarized the work results of CMAC 2019 as follows:
1: Mine Awareness and Explosive Ordnance Disposal Education: For the first 12 months of 2019, CMAC has been educating the group about the dangers of landmines and explosive remnants of war to the group. The target was 11,235 times and 533,242 people participated.
Work to rescue people with disabilities from landmines has also achieved good results in both mobilization and support for victims. This activity has received active participation from local authorities and stakeholders, such as facilitating the digging of ponds, canal systems, roads and education, creating new jobs.
In addition, for the first 12 months of 2019, CMAC provided demining training to mine action officers from Iraq / Kurdish, Colombia and Laos. These trainings were supported by JICA and JICS with a total of 115 participants.
