Ministry of Agriculture announces the official launch of the Strategic Plan for Agricultural Development 2019-2023
(Phnom Penh): The Ministry of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries in the morning of Wednesday, December 14, 2019, held a ceremony to announce and officially launch the strategic plan for sector development. Agriculture (PYOK) 2019-2023 under the chairmanship of Mr. Veng Sakhon, Minister of Agriculture.
The event was also attended by the leaders of the Ministry of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries, the leadership of the Department under the auspices of private sector development partners, NGOs, agricultural communities, the Department of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries and about 460 members.
Minister Veng Sakhon praised the efforts of the technical working group to prepare this strategic plan, especially the relevant ministries, institutions, development partners, national and international organizations that have cooperated well to achieve important policy documents. This.
Taking this opportunity to achieve the development goals of the agricultural sector and especially for the successful implementation of the EIA 2019-2023 as expected, the Minister provided guidance and set out some key measures. For the foundation to be implemented more effectively and efficiently, those recommendations are related to:
* In-depth reform of the sub-sector to be more comprehensive.
* The specialized unit under the supervision must prepare a comprehensive strategic development plan, review all projects or programs in progress.
* All specialized units, departments, development partners and the private sector must cooperate to implement intelligent technology, use inputs effectively to make agricultural products competitive, reduce costs, ensure quality and safety in accordance with market standards and promote good agricultural practices.
* Participate more actively in adaptation measures or resilience to climate change and mitigate the effects of climate change.
