APSARA Authority urges people to use baray water with high savings
(Siem Reap): This dry season, APSARA Authority calls on farmers who are using water in the western baray to save money in the future to avoid water shortages in the future as water management is an important task after conservation. Of APSARA Authority.
The Water Management Department of the APSARA Authority has advised farmers who are using the western baray water to save money when this year's dry season can be prolonged. Currently, some farmers in Siem Reap and Puok districts are pumping water from the western baray to irrigate about 7,500 hectares of dryland rice.
In addition to supplying dry rice to farmers, part of the western baray water is distributed to the Siem Reap Water Supply Authority about 10,000 cubic meters per day to supply the people's consumption, while the other part is stored in the baray for water supply. Underground.
