Samdech Techo Hun Sen wants the Cambodian Border Model Market (Dar Market) to be clean and tidy and to be inspected regularly, but not to disturb the people who sell. Samdech said that if there is a disturbance, people will create their own corridors, and that is uncontrollable. If not controlled, criminals engage in drug trafficking and other crimes. Samdech asked to do this work carefully.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen continued that the Royal Government has already delegated power, so the management of this market must be done by the provincial authorities without going to the Ministry of Commerce.
"Cambodia Border Model Market (Phsar Dar)" is located in Thary Tbong Khmum Special Economic Zone, Dar Kandol Village, Dar Commune, Memot District, Tbong Khmum Province, on an area of nearly 2 hectares, approximately 300 meters from the Cambodian-Vietnamese border. The location of this model market is the territory of the former battlefield where Samdech Techo Hun Sen fought 20 times during 1971.
The "Cambodian Border Model Market" was opened in 2018 at a cost of nearly $ 2 million, funded by the Vietnamese government. The market has 68 booths divided into 6 categories. The Cambodian border model market is only allowed to sell Cambodian and Vietnamese products, not to other countries.
