Vital Drinking Water and Noodles Co., Ltd. Holds "Warm Gift" Charity Program for More Than 200 Elderly People
(Phnom Penh): Vital Drinking Water Company, a manufacturer of high quality drinking water and noodles, a local instant noodle product, has co-organized a charity event "Gift of Warmth" to distribute food, coats, blankets and medicine to the elderly. And about 200 poor and homeless people in Phnom Penh.
The charity event was held on the morning of December 24, 2019 at Wat Botum Park in the presence of Ms. Chheng Sokuntheavy, General Director of Vital Drinking Water and Noodle Products Company, with the participation of local authorities, company management. Citizens, youth, volunteers and many working groups.
Ms. Chheng Sokuntheavy, General Director of the company, said, "The onset of the monsoon season has made it difficult for the elderly and the poor. Some of them do not have proper shelter, some do not have enough equipment and some do not have access to food and medicine for daily use. "We are really saddened and saddened to see these pictures."
"Therefore, through this program, we hope to be able to share some of the hardships and give warmth to them who are having difficulties this winter," she said.
It should be noted that in this program, about 200 elderly and homeless people came to receive donations from both companies, which include rice, sweaters, blankets, scarves, medicine, drinking water, vital noodles and some money. Most of the elderly and people are migrants from other provinces to Phnom Penh to earn a living.
Some are street broom sellers, some are knife sharpeners, some are weighing scales in markets and towns, and some are cyclo drivers. These regimes earn so little that they can not afford to rent a house other than to sleep on the street, on the porch of another house, in a pagoda, or on a cyclo.
