The Prime Minister emphasized that after the end of the war, the Royal Government of Cambodia and the Vietnamese side had made efforts to restore what had been destroyed along the border and left behind many landmines. Do your best to destroy all these bullets to ensure the safety of the people on both sides.
According to Samdech Techo Hun Sen, until now, trade between Cambodia and neighboring countries, especially bordering countries, has increased, in fact, the official trade volume between Cambodia and Vietnam is more than 4,600 million dollars. But the informal trade volume could reach $ 5 billion.
Vietnam's imports to Cambodia include steel, gasoline, textiles and clothing, and agricultural products such as fish, meat and vegetables, fruits, as well as consumer goods, while Cambodia's exports to Vietnam include cashew nuts, rubber, wood and handicrafts. Wood, vegetables, fruits and many other products.
In the field of investment, according to the records of the Council for the Development of Cambodia, from 1994 to August 2019, Cambodia has approved 84 investment projects of Vietnamese companies with a total investment of about 2.5 billion US dollars. Agriculture accounts for about two-thirds of all investment projects.
