Last Friday, US President Donald Trump signed a defense law that created a new military force, the Space Force. Trump decided to set up the force because of concerns that China and Russia were growing in power in space, which poses a major threat to the United States. The Space Force will be the sixth force after the Army, Air Force, Navy, Marine Corps and Coast Guard.
The US space force will have duties such as protecting US interests in space, preventing threats in space or from space, and conducting space operations.
