In addition, Mr. Oknha Leang Khun also thanked Minister Khieu Kanharith and all journalists who were honored to participate in this press conference. Doctors recommend a new drug that can control hypoglycemia for diabetics
"Insulin basal is the best and easiest option for diabetics to start insulin therapy," said Dr. Lim Huy, head of medical and regulatory affairs at Allianz Pharmaceuticals. "Because Toujeo is an insulin basal that is active for more than 24 hours, it can meet the needs of patients who can lower blood sugar throughout the day."
Hypoglycemia is a major concern among insulin users, he said. But Toujeo has been shown to be effective in lowering blood sugar and reducing the risk of hypoglycemia both day and night. Thus, the doctor can confidently prescribe this new generation of insulin to his patients for first-hand experience.
"Diabetes is a chronic disease that affects about 246,200 Cambodians in 2017 and the number continues to increase every year," said Prof. Dr. Koy Vanny, President of the Cambodian Diabetes and Endocrinologists Association. "
"This disease greatly affects the daily life of an individual, so the ease of treatment is very important and should not be overlooked because it can help the patient to manage his condition well," he said. "Diabetes pills are still important and the first choice for people with type 2 diabetes."
However, at some point, many diabetics will face the problem that these supplements are not enough to control blood sugar, he added. And he will need to take extra insulin to control his diabetes. A Chinese man was killed by his landlord while another was seriously injured in a burglary in Sihanoukville.
(Sihanoukville): Two Chinese men broke into a house and were shot by the owner, killing one and seriously injuring another.
The two Chinese nationals broke into a house in Village 03, Sangkat 04, Sihanoukville, Preah Sihanouk Province at dawn on December 23, 2019.
According to local authorities, two Chinese nationals broke into a safe deposit box to collect money while the suspect was acting as the owner of the house, a water border police officer.
The suspects then used two razors to hit the victim, but the owner of the house, a water border police officer with a weapon in his hand, fired several shots at the suspects under the pretext of self-defense. One suspect died at the scene and another was seriously injured and is currently being treated at the Provincial Referral Hospital (Chamkar Chek Hospital).
Authorities confirmed that the owner of the house was Ly Ty, a 35-year-old male, who was a naval border police officer. At present, the authorities do not know the background of the two Chinese people and are still researching the procedure. In response to the support and needs of customers, Daikin opened a branch in Cambodia.
(Phnom Penh): Daikin has further expanded its services following strong customer support, especially to meet the growing market demand. In addition, the branch will organize trainings and workshops to share knowledge and design of Daikin VRV to provide an understanding of the latest air conditioning technology to Cambodia.
For Daikin's global expansion, Indochina markets such as Cambodia, Laos and Myanmar are the company's next focus. Given Cambodia's economic stability and GDP growth of 7% over the past 10 years, Daikin has identified Cambodia as a growth potential in active markets, especially in the tourism and real estate industries.
Through the establishment of a branch office in Cambodia, Daikin is able to provide ongoing high quality service support such as project support, technical support, training and after-sales service support to all stakeholders such as installers, vendors and contractors, project consultants. Project designers and building owners.
In addition, Daikin aims to train talented local human resources through workshops that provide knowledge of products, techniques and uses, as well as quality service standards. With this, Daikin was able to build a professional image and at the same time expand its awareness of Daikin quality to the market. Eventually, customers will have high expectations for the efficiency and quality of air conditioners, improving the entire market.
With control solutions, many controllers can be used automatically to avoid unnecessary wastage of air conditioners from user behavior such as setting the temperature too low or forgetting to turn off the air conditioner. With all these efficient products and smart management, Daikin is confident in reducing energy costs in the market.
