A man was crushed to death by a car in HYUNDAI Machinery Company in Po Sen Chey District
(Phnom Penh): A man died suddenly while he was repairing a Ben Yidup car that crashed into a cage, due to the negligence of the manager and the company manager, suddenly the cage collapsed.
The incident happened on the evening of December 22, 2019 in the HYUNDAI machinery company located along National Road 4 in front of Sangkat Choam Chao III, Prey Pring North Village, Sangkat Choam Chao III, Khan Por Sen Chey. The victim, Khan Narin, male, 60 years old, was born in Udong district, Kampong Speu province and lived in the company.
Prior to the incident, the victim was used by the boss and the manager of the company to repair a Ben Yidup car with the cage up and he went up to sit on the car under the cage. While repairing, the pump suddenly fell on the cage, causing the victim to die immediately at the scene.
After the incident, the police went to the forensic examination, and this case was caused by the manager and the manager of the company were negligent and did not have the correct technique while working to cause such deaths.
This morning, Samdech Techo Hun Sen inaugurated the Cambodia-Vietnam Commodity Exchange, the first market on the Cambodia-Vietnam border.
"Cambodia Border Model Market (Phsar Dar)" is located in Thary Tbong Khmum Special Economic Zone, Dar Kandol Village, Dar Commune, Memot District, Tbong Khmum Province, on an area of nearly 2 hectares, approximately 300 meters from the Cambodian-Vietnamese border. The location of this model market is the territory of the former battlefield where Samdech Techo Hun Sen fought 20 times during 1971.
The "Cambodian Border Model Market" was opened in 2018 at a cost of nearly $ 2 million, funded by the Vietnamese government. The market has 68 booths divided into 6 categories. The Cambodian border model market is only allowed to sell Cambodian and Vietnamese products, not to other countries.
Minister of Commerce Pan Sosak said that the Cambodian border model market has great potential to create jobs, increase income for people along the border and boost bilateral trade between the two countries to 5 billion US dollars. The plan that both countries have planned.
The Minister emphasized that the market will help strengthen good relations in all fields between the people of the two countries and promote good cooperation between the Royal Government of Cambodia and the Government of Vietnam.
The presence of the Cambodian border model market is another new historical achievement in the territory of the border area between Cambodia and Vietnam in response to the policy of Samdech Techo Hun Sen. On December 2, 1998, Samdech Techo Hun Sen launched a purely policy triangle, with one corner of the strategy focusing on building the border, which was once a battlefield into an area of peace, friendship, development and trade.
The Prime Minister saw that only by bringing a peaceful border and development can the lives of the people in the border areas be developed and prosperous.
Letter to readers: What do Cambodians really want?
(Phnom Penh): Some time ago, in Cambodia, I noticed some political and social problems that made me not understand the character of the Cambodian people. The first issue is the preferential tariff system (EBA), the second issue is the Cambodia-Vietnam border, the third issue is the Khmer heritage and the fourth is the presence of Chinese people in Cambodia. The reaction of the Cambodian people to the lack of basis makes me wonder what the Cambodian people really want.
In fact, Cambodia has been the victim of the Cold War, civil war, and the most heinous genocide in human history. Under the Pol Pot regime, the Black Shirts killed millions of people, starved them to work, but Cambodia was able to recover and prosper as it is today. Would Cambodia die without the EBA?
It is shameful that the EU wants to withdraw the EBA from Cambodia, accusing Cambodia of violating human rights. But there are many countries that have received EBA favors from Europe, which have a record of respect for human rights worse than Cambodia. Some countries in the ASEAN region have a lower level of respect for human rights than Cambodia.
Some Cambodians say the loss of the EBA is a punishment for the Cambodian people, especially the poor workers, the vulnerable women who are working in the garment sector. In this regard, the Royal Government is working hard to maintain the EBA. Opposition groups, on the other hand, seemed pleased to hear that the EU was withdrawing the EBA from Cambodia to put pressure on the Royal Government of Cambodia. What do Cambodians want for sure?
Unscrupulous groups have rallied for the promulgation of the Law on the Approval of the Supplementary Treaty between Cambodia and Vietnam, in order to nurture border disputes for use as a political excuse to incite hatred and erode confidence in the Royal Government of Cambodia.
The leaders of the Royal Government of Cambodia are working hard to preserve the territory that Cambodia has today so that it will not be lost like in the past through the implementation of the Cambodia-Vietnam Supplementary Treaty on the State Boundary Treaty. Lack of understanding, some accuse Cambodians of cutting off land for Vietnam. What do Cambodians want for sure?
When Khmer culture was included in the World Heritage List, they never applauded the Royal Government's efforts, but when their neighbors did, they accused the Royal Government of being careless. What do Cambodians want for sure?
Finally, let the Cambodian people learn to understand in depth what they really want. The current Royal Government is working hard to find peace, security, stability and development for the Kingdom of Cambodia. Finding peace is difficult, but maintaining peace is more difficult than achieving peace.
This is a noble contribution of Cambodia to the cause of world peace on behalf of a country that has suffered from war. Cambodia's economy has grown at more than 7% in more than two decades, making it the sixth fastest growing economy in the world.
The poverty rate has been reduced to less than 10%, compared to more than 50% in 1993. Our primary school enrollment rate has reached 98%. Our average life expectancy has increased from 54 years in 1993 to 69 years in 2016. Cambodia is on the right track towards becoming a low-middle-income country by 2030 and a high-income country. By 2050, if political stability is maintained and bureaucratic reforms are lasting.
Therefore, let the Khmer people put the national interest first. We must remember that "no one loves Khmer more than Khmer." All Cambodians, especially young people, must reduce criticism, be open-minded, listen to others, and strive to develop their capacity to respond to the rapidly evolving and dangerous regional and global situation.
Khmer people, especially young people, must strive to acquire knowledge and strengthen ethics for the nation, family and themselves. Leaving ignorance with a dignified demeanor frees us from suffering and avoids anti-racist incitement, fanaticism, and the ideology of national destruction of Cambodia.
