Posting systematic plots of land in Leuk Dek district, authorities ask people to come and check for problems
(Kandal): The Department of Land Management, Urban Planning, Construction and Cadastral Affairs of Kandal Province has called on the people who own the plots in Peam Reang Leu village, Peam Ram commune, Leuk Dek district to come and check and verify the plots data within 15 days from December 23, 2019 to January 6, 2020.
Mr. Prum Chat, Deputy Director of Land Management, Urban Planning, Construction and Cadastral Affairs of Kandal Province, made this appeal during the public posting of systematic land judgment documents in Peam Reang Leu village, Peam Ram commune, Leuk Dek district, Kandal province on the morning of the 23rd. December 2019.
"After posting for 15 days, we will receive accurate data for the issuance of real estate ownership certificates (hard titles) to the people, which also contributes to reducing land disputes, reducing people's poverty." Mr. Prom Chat emphasized.
Mr. Som Phalla, Deputy Governor of Leuk Dek District, stated that the posting of the judgment now reflects the high attention of the Royal Government under the wise leadership of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia. Improve living standards, welfare and reduce poverty, as well as contribute to the strengthening of justice and social stability.
He said that in implementing the systematic land registration procedures, we used advanced techniques, including aerial photographs, automatic machine measurements, as well as data storage and computerized cadastral mapping.
Please note that throughout Peam Reang Leu village, there are 1631 plots of land that have been posted to the public.
