This statement was made on the occasion that he was invited to attend the groundbreaking ceremony for the construction of Bavet City Rainwater Drainage on the morning of December 23, 2019, with a length of more than 6 km, which took 12 months to build and cost about 7 Million dollars is a construction project of the Asian Development Bank (ADB) through three villages: Bavet Leu, Bavet Kandal and Chrak Lao.
"These cities are located along the southern economic corridors. "Ten infrastructure sub-projects have been studied and put into practice in these four cities." Bavet Mayor emphasizes.
He said that on behalf of Bavet City Authority, it will cooperate with the Ministry of Public Works and Transport, the Ministry of Economy and Finance and the Asian Development Bank to implement future projects, which will include wastewater treatment projects and landfills that are being studied and Must be implemented in the near future.
