(Kratie): Mr. Nut Puth Dara, former Governor of Dangkor District, was officially appointed as the Deputy Governor of Kratie Province this morning, December 23, 2019.
The ceremony was held in the presence of Mr. Ngy Chanphal, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Interior, Representative of Samdech Krala Hom Sar Kheng, Deputy Prime Minister, Minister of Interior, as well as the participation of the Kratie Provincial Board of Governors, the Armed Forces and many government officials. .
Mr. Nut Puth Dara, Deputy Governor of Kratie Province, who will be taking office, is committed to serving the nation and the people, such as:
Mr. Ngy Chanphal spoke about the work experience and achievements of Mr. Nuth Puth Dara, who was: * Deputy Director General of Administration, Ministry of Land Management, Urban Planning and Construction * Deputy Governor of Khan Russey Keo, Phnom Penh * Governor of Dangkor, Phnom Penh * and now Governor Deputy Governor of Kratie Province and also an assistant to Samdech Techo Prime Minister.
On that occasion, the Secretary of State of the Ministry of Interior instructed the new Deputy Governor to work hard to perform their duties effectively with the provincial leadership and relevant departments of the province to serve the people at the local level even better.
