Minister Tram Iv Tek Visits Cambodia Post Exhibition Hall at Kampot Sea Festival
(Kampot): Mr. Tram Iv Tek, Minister of Posts and Telecommunications and accompanying delegates, as well as other institutional leaders were honored to visit the Cambodia Post Exhibition booth at the Sea Festival in Kampot. Completed on December 23, 2019.
The second round of the 8th Sea Festival 2019 in Kampot City, Kampot Province ended this morning. A senior official of the Ministry of Posts confirmed that for the past three days of the Sea Festival, Cambodia Post has introduced its services with the highest confidence to customers.
At the same time, Cambodia Post would like to thank Minister Tram Iv Tek and the accompanying delegation, as well as the leaders of other institutions, for the honor of visiting the Cambodia Post Exhibition. Local aquaculture farmers in Teuk Phos are receiving support from customers who can earn more than $ 300 per month
(Kampong Chhnang): A family living in Sre Ta Chey village, Aphivath commune, Teuk Phos district, Kampong Chhnang province, who has been growing vegetables on the water for more than 7 years, has received satisfactory results and is receiving a lot of support from customers. Domestic and foreign, never left as long as there is.
By selling his vegetables grown on water without chemicals, he earns more than $ 300 a month thanks to the hard work of his family.
Yang Sarim, 55, an education officer in Teuk Phos district who has been growing vegetables on the water, said he had been learning the techniques of growing vegetables on the water for more than seven years. Now his vegetable growing is successful, with local and foreign customers, especially traders in the market, coming to order his chemical-free vegetables, never left only his vegetables. He is old enough to eat.
In particular, at the market in Phnom Penh, he also used to order his vegetables, but he did not receive the supply because he did not have the budget to expand the vegetable garden to supply customers in Phnom Penh, because the expansion of the vegetable garden serves More customers, unless you spend a lot of capital up to tens of thousands of dollars.
The farmer, who is a civil servant, stated that for more than 7 years, he has also trained 6 students who came to learn how to grow vegetables, some from the province. Others are just as successful as he is. So, if any farmer likes and wants to try to grow vegetables on water like him, he can come and learn from him and train for free.
