The post of Cuban prime minister was dissolved in 1976, but was only restored this year after Cuba amended its constitution through a referendum in February. The last incumbent was Fidel Castro, who ran from 1959 to December 1976, when the name was changed to chair the cabinet.
However, from now on, Cuba has the same presidency and prime minister as it did decades ago. The current president of Cuba is Miguel Diaz-Canel. The prime minister is in charge of the Cuban government, but under the control of the president.
Cambodian philanthropist in the United States donates 200 bicycles and school supplies to poor students at Samdech Hun Sen Angstok High School
(Kampot): Cambodian philanthropists living in Texas, USA raised money to buy 200 bicycles and other school supplies for needy students at Samdech Hun Sen Angstok High School in Samlanh Commune, Angkor Chey District, Kampot Province. While some students come to school late because there is no way to travel.
The handover ceremony was held on the morning of December 22, 2019 under the chairmanship of Mr. So Visothy, Undersecretary of State, Ministry of Tourism and Chairman of the Youth Working Group for the South Central Region of the United States, on behalf of Mr. Moeng Ponlok, Working Group Chairman. Organize a CPP youth organization in the United States.
Speaking at the handover ceremony, Mr. Chan Eng Long, Chairman of the Texas Branch Committee of the United States of America, said that this humanitarian aid came from the help of Cambodian philanthropists living in Texas, USA, and this aid is two bicycles. Hundreds of study materials such as books, pens and pencils.
Mr. Chan Eng Long continued that Cambodians living in Texas have joined the Royal Government of Cambodia in helping people in need, especially students, and this assistance is not limited to Ang Chey. Helped in communities in other provinces as well.
At the same time, Mr. Sovisuthy said that the Cambodian philanthropists living in Texas, USA, who have helped the students now is an expression of their generosity in joining the Royal Government in reducing poverty and Promote the human resources sector in Cambodia to be even stronger while the country is enjoying peace and continuous development.
However, Mr. Sovisothy called on all students to continue their efforts to study more after receiving these bicycles and study materials from our Cambodian charity overseas.
He told the students that learning to know will help themselves and their families to prosper if the family grows, society and the nation grow as well.
According to the principal of the high school, some students are in dire straits as they travel on foot and sometimes they do not come to school on time due to the distance from home. After receiving the bikes, the principal expects that the students will not be too late to study, and he expects that they will work harder without the help of philanthropists. No hope.
