(Kampot): Garbage is a small problem, but if people do not take care of it properly, it will become a big problem, said Mr. Hout Rithy, Director of the Department of Clean City Support and promote Race of the Ministry of Tourism as he leads a group of young people to collect garbage in public places in Kampot on the occasion of the Sea Festival.
This garbage collection activity is part of the "Clean Cambodia, Clean Kampot Clean" campaign organized by the Department of Clean City Support Services and promoting the competition of the Ministry of Tourism in collaboration with the Kampot Administration, Kampot Municipality and thousands of young people, including Noble Youth for Society and Environment Ga Eia Garbage Collection Company, Union of Youth Federations of Cambodia, Kampot Province, Cambodian Red Cross, Peace Lovers, Scouts, etc.
Mr. Hout Rithy stated the purpose of this campaign: "We do not want to have litter in the open field after the Sea Festival, which affects the beauty of Kampot and the country as a whole. "We do it every day during this sea festival, not just one day."
He added that the daily activities also include the distribution of "Clean Cambodia, Kampot Clean" stickers to inspire participants, people, tourists, law enforcement forces, doctors to join them to promote the campaign "Clean Cambodia Kampot Clean. »This to be more revived.
Mr. Leang Roeun Sothy, Governor of Kampot City, said, "Participating in the Clean Cambodia Kampot Clean Campaign is not as quiet as it is criticized for just taking a selfie in front of the camera. "But this activity has helped a lot to clean up the sanitary environment in the city, contribute to the country is clean and beautiful."
The Governor of Kampot City said that people, youth and tourists who visit the Sea Festival also get to know about this campaign, which is to promote the spirit of love for the environment even more.
Trying to stop from Phnom Penh, Pov Seaklin, a member of the group of about 100 young people who joined the group of friends, expressed the impression that although the hands are a little dirty, but they are very happy to Participate in garbage collection activities in the Sea Festival in Kampot Province because it helps to clean up the environment and helps spread the word to others even more.
Mr. Hout Rithy is optimistic that from year to year, young people are more aware and concerned about sanitation, environment and garbage, including the Sea Festival, River Festival, Royal Water Festival and events.
He said that clean and green, as well as attention to the issue of garbage is a promotion of clean Cambodia, Cambodia is desirable to visit to international tourists, which is a factor driving the growth of tourism in Cambodia. Online Businesses Organize Successful Training Rules for About 800 Participants
(Phnom Penh): While everyone understands that the business of selling products online is an easy thing that anyone can do and do not need training from the school, experts and successful in this field. Responded that online business is the most difficult and complex business. The same expert said that because it requires rules to be successful, she decided to open a training course for about 800 participants on December 21, 2019.
(Phnom Penh): Cambodia and China are committed to jointly building a community of common destiny with the goal of cooperation in building a roadmap for development and promoting Cambodia-China relations to a new level in the future.
This was stated by Dr. Sok Touch, President of the Royal Academy of Cambodia, speaking at a scientific forum on the establishment of a joint Cambodian-Chinese community of destiny within the framework of "Lines and Roads" and celebrating the 10th anniversary of the establishment of the Confucius Institute of the Royal Academy. Cambodia organized on December 22, 2019.
Dr. Sok Touch expects that in the future, we believe, based on the reason that under our joint efforts, Cambodia and China will be able to build a community of common destiny with the first strategic meaning as a contribution to community building. A common destiny in Asia.
Mr. Van Persin, Director of the Political Bureau of the Chinese Embassy in Cambodia, on behalf of the Chinese Embassy in Cambodia, said that the friendship between Cambodia and China dates back more than 1,700 years, and the two countries are considered as brothers. The meeting between His Majesty King Sihanouk and Prime Minister Zhou Enlai at the Bandung Conference in 1955 marked a turning point in the history of Cambodia-China relations.
"Since the establishment of diplomatic ties in 1958, the two countries have respected and supported each other, strengthened political, social and economic cooperation and people-to-people exchanges," he said. Origin became a model country for inter-country exchanges. At present, the comprehensive strategic partnership between Cambodia and China has been constantly evolving.
He added that Samdech Techo Hun Sen, the Prime Minister of Cambodia, has made the leadership of the two countries like a family and has drawn up a plan for the development of bilateral relations in the future, as well as a strong driving force in Promote relations between the two countries as well.
According to Ms. Vuth Sopheakna, Director of the Confucius Institute at the Royal Academy of Cambodia, at the Scientific Forum on the Establishment of the Cambodia-China Joint Destiny Community within the framework of "One Belt and One Road", "Belt and Road" is An important Chinese foreign strategy.
Since 2013, initiated by President Xi Jinping, China's influence on the country's politics, economy and culture along the line of initiatives has increasingly shown its different responsibilities as a Chinese superpower and promoting China's image and role in the international arena as well.
Ms. Vuth Sopheakna added that along with the deepening progress of the development of the "Belt and Road", China and Cambodia hope to form a common destiny community with their own unique characteristics but a common future through win-win cooperation.
Ministry of Interior National Police Recruitment Exam for 2019, 4,000 Candidates Apply for the Exam
(Phnom Penh): On December 22, 2019, the Ministry of Interior organized the National Police Officer Examination for 2019 throughout the country to fill in the Capital-Provincial Police Commission, while next week there will be an examination for specialized departments. Of the General Commission of the National Police.
General Pen Vibol, Deputy Commissioner of the National Police and Director of the Personnel Department, told Fresh News that about 4,000 candidates applied for the exam this morning, but the ministry decided to select only one. , 000 people only.
General Pen Vibol said that for the general situation of the exam was completed smoothly, there were no significant incidents, that is, with good cooperation from the relevant authorities who monitor Exam centers in 19 capitals and provinces to ensure that the exam runs fairly.
The Deputy General Commissioner of the National Police and the director of the Personnel Department confirmed that the exam was held only one morning, and for the exam subject, there is a general culture and some questions related to the police.
Please see the pictures of the National Police Officer Selection Examination process below: Vattanac Bank opens its 17th new branch in Boeung Tumpun area, Phnom Penh
Vattanac Bank Boeung Tumpun Branch is built in a modern and luxurious style with comfortable service hall and large parking space.
Mr. Phal Sokchea, Branch Manager, said that he and all the staff of Vattanac Bank, Boeung Tumpun Branch were committed to provide daily banking services to customers as quickly as possible, honestly, responsibly. And high professionalism.
In addition, he and his colleagues are ready to welcome as well as support small and medium enterprises and businesses to help increase capital and promote these enterprises and businesses to double growth.
Regarding the opening of the Boeung Tumpun branch, Lok Chumteav Oknha Chhun Leang, the editor of Vattanac Bank, also said, Vattanac Bank is getting closer to its customers to respond in a timely manner to the growing support.
In addition, Vattanac Bank plans to open 11 new branches in 2020 with specific plans to expand its branches throughout the Kingdom of Cambodia to 25 capitals and provinces by 2022, each branch is Born from the investment by Vattanac Bank itself, both in the purchase of land and the construction of all kinds of buildings.
Vattanac Bank is a financial institution established in 2002 by purely Cambodian investors. The Bank is headquartered on the second floor of Vattanac Capital in Phnom Penh. Currently, Vattanac Bank has 17 branches in Phnom Penh and other provinces including Siem Reap, Battambang, Kampong Speu, Pursat, Takeo and Kampong Cham.
