Some previously published articles related to the remarks made by Samdech Techo Hun Sen and Mr. Var Kimhong on the border issue with Vietnam
(Phnom Penh): The Royal Government of Cambodia and the Government of Vietnam on October 10, 2019 signed the Supplementary Treaty on the demarcation of the two countries in 1985 and the Supplementary Treaty of 2005 in Hanoi, Vietnam.
Based on the maps left over from the French colonial period and the Supplementary Treaty, both Cambodia and Vietnam demarcated and demarcated the land border on the actual land from Ratanakkiri to Kampot from June 2006 to July 2019. The result is 84 percent of the land border, which is about 1,270 kilometers long.
During the signing of the treaty, Cambodian Prime Minister Samdech Techo Hun Sen considered the achievement of demarcation and demarcation of the border with Vietnam, a great achievement that the two countries have achieved by seeking joint solutions. With brotherhood and mutual understanding in friendly brotherhood decades ago.
Samdech Techo emphasized that if the two countries do not make efforts to end this border issue, the two countries will continue to have border disputes for generations to come, easily becoming political rivals, and peace and development in At the border will not be able to happen.
The Prime Minister of Cambodia, Samdech Techo, emphasized that on behalf of the Royal Government of Cambodia, Samdech was very proud that the two countries had overcome the difficulties and almost completely completed the land border between the two countries.
The Law on the Supplementary Treaty of the 1985 State Boundary Treaty and the 2005 Supplementary Treaty between Cambodia and Vietnam was approved and promulgated by the King of Cambodia, His Majesty King Norodom Sihamoni, on 5 December. 2019 ago.
After the two supplementary treaty laws were signed and adopted by the King of Cambodia, illegal groups living abroad and some of their allies in Cambodia launched a series of attacks. Respectfully yours, the King of Cambodia, the highest honor of the Khmer people.
Their actions are severely punished according to the Constitution of the Kingdom of Cambodia, which upholds the King's power so that no one can insult him.
Border issues between Cambodia and neighboring countries, including Vietnam, Thailand and Laos. Once. It should be noted, however, that the group, which claims to be patriotic, has never shown any measures to protect its territorial integrity.
In fact, when Cambodia had a border dispute with Thailand in 2008 and a border dispute with Laos in 2017 and this year, only the Royal Government has made every effort to use all possible armed forces and diplomacy, plus international law. To protect these territories. In particular, the group of people who claim to love the land do not seem to see their shadow.
