Key questions and answers related to Donald Trump's political destiny in 2020
The following are the key questions and answers regarding Tram's political destiny in 2020:
1. When will the US Senate hold a debate?
The date for the debate on the election of Mr. Tram in the Senate has not yet been confirmed, but according to US media, the hearing may take place in the second week of January or may remain. January 20
The hearing will be chaired by the 100 senators, who will quietly monitor the presidential impeachment case, the lawmakers will act as prosecutors, and the Supreme Court President John Roberts will chair the Senate hearing. Donald Trump and his Minister of Justice will act as defendants.
However, the removal of Tram from the current Republican-controlled Senate is widely seen as impossible.
The US Constitution does not prohibit this, that is, nominations are possible. But the appointment of Tram as vice president by Pence requires a majority vote in the House of Representatives and the Senate in a context where Democrats and senators may not vote in favor.
4. If the Senate does not vote to remove Mr. Tram, what will happen?
If the election to oust Donald Trump from the White House fails by the Senate, President Trump will have more power to act in the future, which could have a negative impact on Democrats in the House. 2020 election. That is, if Mr. Tram is not ousted, it may anger some loyal Democrat supporters, or they may lose confidence or not go to the polls.
