The Minister of Tourism is optimistic that the people and tourists will increase their participation in the Sea Festival.
(Kampot): Optimistic about the organization of the Sea Festival, which has been held eight times, Mr. Thong Khon, Minister of Tourism, noted that the organization of the Sea Festival from year to year more and more active participation. From all stakeholders, both public and private, as well as receiving increasing interest from citizens and tourists.
On the occasion of the official opening of the 8th round of the 8th Sea Festival in Kampot Province, which was presided over by Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, Minister Thong Khon said that for 2019, the coastal area will receive About 1.3 million international tourists, an increase of 4.5%, with a market share of about 15% of the total market, and about 3.4 million domestic tourists, an increase of 3%.
By 2020, the coastal region is expected to receive about 1.7 million international tourists and about 3.5 million domestic tourists, and by 2030, the coastal region will receive about 7.5 million international tourists. With an average growth of 10% and about 5.5 million national tourists, an average increase of 5%.
"This shows that the organization of the Sea Festival from year to year has the participation of all stakeholders, both public and private, and has received more and more attention from the people and national tourists," he said. "International."
The Minister emphasized that in order to celebrate this year's Sea Festival, the Inter-Ministerial Commission has organized some important activities as follows:
1: Exhibition of Achievements, Food and Beverage Festival and Coastal Development Project, a total of 461 booths, including: booths for major tourism development projects in the coastal area, tourism products, local products and small and medium enterprises, foreign exhibition booths, and especially the organization of food streets. (Food Street) can be a model for other provinces.
2: Performances of ancient and contemporary mixed art performances with the participation of national artists and friendly countries including: China, Thailand, Indonesia, India and Vietnam.
3: Sports activities, including: running, beach cycling, beach wrestling, international jet skiing, international Khmer boxing, international belt wrestling, bokator, chess and mountain adventure. .
In addition, a number of pre-event activities, such as workshops and giveaways for outstanding tourism businesses, include: accommodation, food, transportation and model beaches in the four coastal provinces; Commemorative tree planting ceremony along with many other celebratory events.
