Speaking on the night of December 21, 2019, on the occasion of presiding over the opening ceremony of the 8th Sea Festival in the second round held in Kampot province, Samdech Techo Hun Sen expressed his deep surprise to those who disagreed. And for those who do not value peace.
The Prime Minister of Cambodia, Samdech Techo, stated: "It is not just the affairs of the people of Kampot, but the common thing of our nation to maintain peace and political stability. "This is very important. First of all, before we talk about democracy, before we talk about human rights, before we talk about development, we have to talk about peace."
"We do not agree with anyone who underestimates the value of peace because our country has gone through countless hardships, tragedies and deaths," he said. We can not accept any insults to us for what we do for our peace, but we must accept insults from some quarters that we do not agree with, because this points to Cambodia from the past war from 1970 to 1975. Continuing the genocidal regime of Pol Pot.
The Father of Peace of Cambodia reminded that if there had been no war in 1970, there would have been no genocidal regimes in 1975 and 1979. After the genocidal regime, the war continued until 1998, when it was over. Samdech Techo stated that the ties that the previous generation tied were solved by the next generation.
"The wars waged by the previous generation are resolved by the younger generation, and it is a tragedy that we experience the need for our country to have a permanent presence of peace in our miserable land." Samdech Techo Hun Sen emphasizes.
