For almost two years, the skirt weaving business has grown proudly, unexpectedly
(Kampong Chhnang): Skirts are almost a product of Khmer children from their ancestors, this product is now being preserved by the next generation of Khmer children.
On the morning of December 21, 2019, Fresh News Agency in Kampong Chhnang Province visited a village called Tbeng Village, located in Teuk Hot Commune, Rolea Bier District, about 20 km from Kampong Chhnang Province. Meet two families who have been weaving skirts for almost two years, with success in this business as well.
Initially, he started with only one weaver, but now has up to five weavers, and is trying to expand when he has enough money. This may be the first family to take up this business in Kampong Chhnang, because in the past, weaving skirts was a Khmer work in this province has never existed.
Chan Narin, a 32-year-old woman who has been paralyzed since the age of three, said she and her four siblings had been learning to weave skirts in Koh Dach commune, Muk Kampoul district, Kandal province, since they were young. After learning how to weave, they were weaving skirts almost there for 6-7 years.
Nowadays, skirts are almost ordered by customers, especially during the Kan Ben festival in the past, in addition to customers who come to buy almost all skirts produced at Koh Dach, Muk Kampoul district, Kandal province, without being sold in the provincial market. This is Kampong Chhnang.
Another woman, Chan Narin's younger sister, who is disabled, said that after they had been weaving for almost two years, she had bought a plot of land and built a decent house. Previously, he took refuge under the roof with his mother. At the same time, they asked the people to support the work of Cambodian children, this is our Cambodian skirt weaving product to encourage them.
It should be noted that on average, a weaver earns $ 300 to $ 400 per month, which may be more than a factory weaver, but this business can still reunite families and take care of children, parents, the elderly. . Samdech Pich Sena Tea Banh Leads a Delegation of the Ministry of National Defense to Attend the 75th Anniversary of the Establishment of the Vietnamese People's Army
