Nowadays, the Department of Commerce pays a lot of attention to it, always taking him and his products to exhibitions in different provinces when there is an exhibition of a village, a product, and so on. In the future, his family will bring this ceramic product to Koh Pich, Phnom Penh again. He has been to the exhibition on Koh Pich a few times.
The owner of the handicraft said that the production of ceramics is very difficult, such as plowing, sifting, pottery to get the desired shape and burning paint. Until he succeeds and is as successful as he is today, it will cost money and time.
