Mr. Khleang Huot: Chroy Changvar is a district with the potential to invest in real estate.
Mr. Khleang Huot said that Chroy Changvar is one of the potential districts of Phnom Penh for investment in real estate among the suburbs and a district with a bright future. He said that in terms of the environment in Chroy Changvar, there is no concern about flooding because there are two rivers, the Mekong River and the Tonle Sap, and this location also provides a good atmosphere and air to live.
The district governor added that in terms of security, Chroy Changvar district is more perfect compared to other districts, which is a factor that makes investors pay attention to investment. He claimed that another factor that favors investment in real estate due to Chroy Changvar is the new geography. The new area has a better layout and infrastructure than other suburban areas due to less congestion.
"This place, from the Sangkum Reastr Niyum era to the era of the Cambodian state, there was no water, no electricity, no road, only National Road No. 6. And the people who make a living in this area are agriculture and fishing ... but this area has turned into an incredible face, an area with real estate and strong development in real estate. "Now there are a lot of big investment projects coming in and this area will be a civilized city in the future." The district governor emphasized.
Finally, he also advised project developers to pay close attention to the quality and standards of construction to give confidence to those who wish to invest in this area, including those who wish to. Looking to buy for living as well.
He added that the rental price of condominiums also increased by 4.3%, the average type of condominium 3% for luxury condominiums, although the number of condominiums increased by 9%. These are the factors that motivate both local and foreign investors to pay more attention to investing in real estate.
