(Kampong Cham): Vattanac Bank inaugurated its 15th branch in Kampong Cham under the strong presidency of Lt. Gen. Hun Manet, Deputy Commander of the Royal Cambodian Armed Forces and Commander of the Army.
The new branch is located in the center of Kampong Cham provincial town, with a 14-storey building and a large courtyard along Monivong Blvd., Kampong Cham city, Kampong Cham province, which was inaugurated on October 19, 2019.
This new branch will provide all kinds of banking services to customers or traders living in Kampong Cham province, especially to provide all kinds of tax payment services more easily and quickly.
Vattanac Bank welcomes and supports small and medium enterprises in Kampong Cham to increase their capital and promote their growth.
In addition, Vattanac Bank Kampong Cham Branch has a comfortable banking service hall and a large parking lot for customers to do banking operations, and also has a special service office "Golden Service" waiting to serve customers of Vattanac Bank.
Ms. Soy Sunnary, Branch Manager, and Ms. Hor Thida, Branch Vice President, are residents of Kampong Cham Province, who are in charge of the branch's daily banking operations.
Vattanac Bank is a local net bank established in 2002. The Bank is headquartered on the 2nd floor of Vattanac Capital in Phnom Penh.
Vattanac Bank offers all kinds of commercial banking services with 9 branches in Phnom Penh and in the provinces of Siem Reap, Battambang, Kampong Speu, Pursat, Takeo and Kampong Cham, the 15th new branch opened today.
Vattanac Bank has gained the trust and confidence of customers with continuous progress and has gained a good reputation for providing excellent customer service and good corporate governance through the recognition of national and international institutions during the period. Its operations for many years.
