(Central): Lt. Gen. Sman Sary, Deputy Director of the Personnel Department, instructed the police officers who are in charge of the examination center to be very careful in checking the candidates and not to let the candidates have mobile phones, iPads and flashcards. Absolutely enter the exam room.
He said so in the meeting to disseminate the mechanism for the examination of candidates for the National Police of Kandal Provincial Police for 2019 this morning, December 21, 2019 at the Commission. Kandal Provincial Police.
Mr. Sman Sary stressed that the rangers did not allow the iPads to enter the examination room to avoid any unintentional mistakes. In addition to all this work, the ranger officer is responsible for supervising and instructing the candidates to fill in their names, table numbers, room numbers and sign correctly.
Kandal Provincial Police Commissioner, Major General Eav Chamroeun, stated that the process of recruiting candidates to join the National Police of Kandal Provincial Police for 2019 only 136 places (136 people) will take place this morning. Sunday, December 22, 2019 at Hun Sen Takhmao High School, with a total of 397 candidates / 105 females.
