(Phnom Penh): Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, will preside over the opening ceremony of the 8th Sea Festival in the evening of Saturday, March 21, 2019. Two held in Kampot province.
The Sea Festival was first held in Sihanoukville in 2011 to celebrate the membership of the most beautiful beach club in the world and to contribute to the promotion of tourism potential of the coastal provinces and to support the policy of Royal Government in the development of sustainable tourism.
Mr. Thong Khon, Minister of Tourism, said that this year's Sea Festival event featured a total of 461 booths for food and beverage festival achievements and coastal development projects, including booths for major coastal tourism development projects, tourism products and local products. And small and medium enterprises, foreign exhibition booths, and especially the preparation of Food Street can be a model for other provinces.
In addition, there will be performances of ancient and contemporary mixed arts with the participation of national and international artists from China, Thailand, Indonesia, India and Vietnam. Sports activities include: sprinting, beach volleyball, beach wrestling, international jet skiing, international Khmer boxing, international belt wrestling, bokator, chess and mountain adventures.
According to the Minister of Tourism, the Sea Festival in Kampot also has a number of pre-event activities, such as workshops and the distribution of prizes to outstanding tourism businesses, including accommodation, food. Transportation and model beaches in the four coastal provinces and a tree planting ceremony along with many other celebratory events.
The Prime Minister expressed his hope that the celebration of the Sea Festival will be a great new opportunity for Cambodia to turn Cambodia's coastal cities and beaches into quality tourism destinations in line with the slogan "Beach". Sea of Cambodia: Star of the Southwest ”as well as increase the spirit of patriotism, solidarity and friendship.
Minister Thong Khon expects that the 8th Sea Festival in the beautiful Kampot province will contribute to the promotion of tourist sites in the province more widely. The minister also expects this year's Sea Festival to have more than half a million participants.
Nutritionists share tips for better health that can be applied daily!
(Phnom Penh): Nestlé Unprecedented Exciting Excursion to Cambodia, Aiming to Promote Healthy Living Habits That Lead to Better Health, Happier Life Arrived at Aeon Mall 1 on December 20, 2019 after traveling to 5 provinces.
The aim is to encourage and motivate Cambodians to become health champions, to be healthier, to live a more active life and to choose the right nutrition to improve their physical and mental health.
Bringing the awareness of nutrition to the people, this tour has already traveled to many provinces, including: Kandal, Kampong Cham, Battambang, Siem Reap and Tbong Khmum, with participants up to To about ten thousand people.
This big event was attended by DJ Nana and nutrition experts who shared many useful tips that can be applied daily to improve health, make life happier and discuss nutrition issues. Impact on the Cambodian people, including the ongoing challenges related to iron deficiency and malnutrition.
Malnutrition among children in Cambodia remains a challenge and the company will continue to address this issue by educating local people through this tourism program and providing high quality micronutrient products for children and Adults through some products such as: Bear Brand raw milk and Milo drinks.
The event will end in Takeo on December 28-29, 2019 and will bring a variety of fun activities along with exercise activities such as: dancing and spinning. There are also a lot of prizes.
Free health check-ups are available throughout the day, along with body mass index (BMI) checks and bone tests, along with a host of key tips based on daily health results and tips.
