Mr. Sok Touch considers the International Conference on Asia-Pacific Cultural Values in the Age of Technology as the Best Forum for Researchers
(Phnom Penh): Dr. Sok Touch, President of the Royal Academy of Cambodia, on December 20, 2019, presided over the closing ceremony of the 15th International Conference on "Asia-Pacific Cultural Values" and "Cultural Challenges in the Technological Age". Participation by researchers from 18 countries in Asia at the Phnom Penh Hotel.
Dr. Sok Touch considers the 15th International Conference on "Asia-Pacific Cultural Values" in the age of technology to be the best forum for researchers to raise a wide range of topics of fundamental value. Researchers from up to 18 countries, including Cambodia, are invaluable in bringing together scholars to uncover the rich cultural values of the people of the world.
