(Kampong Speu): Boeung Ket Mango Confectionery Company, established in 2017, is actively involved in processing mangoes into confectionery for export to China. With the presence of a factory in Phnom Sruoch district, Kampong Speu province, the company has collected mangoes from all over the country to process into sweets for export.
Heng Sreng, the company's representative, said that the company needs between 150 and 180 tons of mangoes per day to make this mango candy. But now only 60 to 100 tons can be collected.
According to Heng Sreng, the company collects about 20 percent of the mangoes from the villagers, 60 percent from the brokers and 20 percent from the community.
According to Heng Sreng, the amount of mangoes he collected was not enough to produce sweets for China, as the market in China was in high demand.
To meet his demand for mango production, Mr. Heng Sreng announced to collect mangoes from people everywhere. The mangoes that the company buys are mangoes, turmeric and some other types of mangoes.
The mangoes that the company buys are not subject to many conditions, that is, not only rotten and borrowed, but his company collects all of them. This is according to Mr. Heng Sreng.
The price of mango and turmeric that the company buys is about 1,450 riel per kilogram.
