Cambodian, Vietnamese Defense Ministers Sign 5-Year Bilateral Cooperation Protocol "2020-2025" and 2020
(VOVworld) - The signing ceremony of the five-year bilateral cooperation message "2020-2025" and the year 2020 between the Ministry of National Defense of Cambodia and the Ministry of Defense of Vietnam was signed at the Ministry of Defense of Vietnam in Hanoi. Of the Socialist Republic of Vietnam on December 20, 2019.
The signing ceremony was held between Samdech Pich Sena Tea Banh, Deputy Prime Minister and Minister of National Defense of Cambodia, and General Ngo Sun Lich, Minister of Defense of the Socialist Republic of Vietnam.
During the bilateral meeting, General Ngo Sun Lich thanked Samdech Pich Sena Tea Banh for accepting the invitation of the Vietnamese Ministry of Defense to attend the 75th anniversary of the establishment of the Vietnamese People's Army and attend the Ministerial Meeting. Defend the three nationalities of Cambodia, Vietnam and Laos.
General Ngo Sun Lich considers the visit of the Cambodian Defense Ministry delegation to Vietnam as important to evaluate the results of the implementation of the cooperation protocol between the two armies from 2015 to 2019 and the direction for the next 5 years. . He hoped that the cooperation between the two armies would be successful in contributing to the strengthening of friendship, solidarity and cooperation in all fields between the two armies, Cambodia and Vietnam.
In response, Samdech Pich Sena Tea Banh conveyed the greetings of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia to the leaders of the Party and State, especially officers, soldiers, deputies and soldiers of the Vietnamese People's Army. Celebrating the 75th anniversary of the founding of the historic Vietnamese People's Army.
On behalf of the Ministry of National Defense of Cambodia, Samdech Pich Sena Tea Banh thanked the Government of the Ministry of Defense of Vietnam for always supporting the Ministry of National Defense of Cambodia to improve the understanding of the Royal Cambodian Armed Forces in all areas.
In fact, on December 18, 2019, the Ministry of National Defense of the two countries recently organized a joint exercise on disaster relief on the Cambodian-Vietnamese land border and humanitarian work in 2019, which is another new achievement among Many achievements have been made under the cooperation between the Ministry of National Defense of Cambodia and the Ministry of National Defense of Vietnam under the initiative of the leaders of the two countries in the past.
Samdech Pich Sena Tea Banh strongly hopes that this exercise will be organized regularly every year by taking turns to promote peace and stability along the border, as well as to strengthen the relationship, contributing to the deepening of mutual trust. Cooperation and understanding between the armies of the two countries.
According to the needs of the Royal Cambodian Armed Forces, which is responsible for contributing to the hosting of the 2023 SEA Games in Cambodia, Samdech Pichey Sena Tea Banh requested the Vietnamese side to examine the possibility of Cambodia in the field of army sports such as training and training. Help repair and maintain the existing infrastructure and support equipment, materials and means for training Cambodian sports.
In response, General Ngo Sunlich expressed his appreciation to the two countries' Defense Ministries for meeting to evaluate the results of the implementation of the protocol on cooperation between the two armies.
