(Preah Vihear): A large number of study materials and clothes donated by philanthropists were handed over by Brigadier General Rith Sona, Police Inspector of Tbeng Meanchey District, Preah Vihear Province, to many needy students living in Po Khoeun Village, Po Srok Commune. Tbeng Meanchey, Preah Vihear province on December 19, 2019.
Lt. Gen. Rith Sona said that under the guidance of Mr. Sou Serey, Deputy Governor of Preah Vihear Province and Chairman of the Tbeng Meanchey District Assistance Team and Mr. Nuth Sophorn, Tbeng Meanchey District Governor, he led the team. Tbeng Meanchey district brought a variety of study materials and clothes to distribute to the students of Stung Touch Primary School.
He added that what made the team sympathetic was that when they met in person, the students were studying under a barn, thatched roofs and wooden walls, which did not look like a school at all. However, the site will turn into a decent school as student growth increases in the coming years.
Mr. Rith Sona said that the gift that was distributed at this time was that each student received a variety of study materials and a set of clothes. He said that these donations came from various philanthropists and leaders through a telegram group called "Tbeng Meanchey District Humanitarian Working Group", which as of today has been distributed to poor students twice.
From now on, Kep has a wastewater treatment plant, Minister Thong Khon urges the provincial administration to implement the first wastewater treatment
(Kep): On December 20, 2019, the Kep Provincial Administration received a wastewater treatment plant and equipment to support the tourism sub-project to improve the environment around Crab Market, as well as Kep province as a whole, which is part of the tourism infrastructure development project. For inclusive growth in the Greater Mekong Subregion under concessional financing from the Asian Development Bank (ADB).
The handover of the wastewater treatment plant and equipment took place at the station (east of Crab Market) under the chairmanship of Mr. Thong Khon, Minister of Tourism and Mr. Ken Satha, Governor of Kep Province, as well as government officials representing ADB. Many citizens and students.
Minister Thong Khon urged the Kep Provincial Administration and relevant departments and units to pay attention to the development of sustainable and clean and green tourism.
The Minister said that in order to develop tourism in Kep province sustainably, the first thing to pay attention to the filtration of wastewater before discharging into the sea absolutely not to flow into the sea. Because it seriously affects the tourism sector, especially the bathing of tourists.
The recommendation of Minister Thong Khon is to urge the Kep Provincial Administration, Department of Tourism and relevant departments in the province to work together to clean up the environment, beaches, seashells, crab markets and other public places in the province to always attract visitors. National-international tourists.
The Minister also called on the people and traders in the Crab Market to cooperate in cleaning the environment, hygiene, safety, improve the quality of hospitality services, especially not to drain sewage, garbage, etc. into the sea. Instead, we must work together to maintain a sustainable tourism environment in our locality to attract more tourists, increase living standards and enhance the prestige of our province.
The Minister of Tourism stressed that the Royal Government identifies and promotes to tourists that "Kep is a high-level tourist destination" where tourists can visit with satisfaction, and in the future, Kep will There is also a proper "tourism development master plan", however, it requires the participation of all citizens and tourists.
At the same time, the Department of Tourism of Kampot Province and the Department of Tourism of Koh Kong also received a sewage truck to work in their respective provinces to improve the cleanliness of public places and tourist resorts.
