Battambang Provincial Gendarmerie Commander and a total of 5 children were disciplined for work irregularities (Video inside) (Battambang): Battambang Provincial Gendarmerie Commander Brigadier General Meas Sovann and his children The Deputy Provincial Command, the District Commander and the Deputy Commander of the District Armed Forces are subject to disciplinary action related to irregularities in the performance of their roles and responsibilities within the unit.
The disciplinary action was taken by General Sao Sokha, Deputy Commander of the Royal Cambodian Armed Forces and Commander of the National Gendarmerie, on December 6, 2019, after an inspection team conducted a search. And find out the facts about the abnormal leadership of these five military officers.
According to a press release issued by the National Gendarmerie on December 20, 2019, the five Gendarmerie officers who received disciplinary action include:
* First: Brigadier General Meas Sovann, Commander of the Battambang Provincial Gendarmerie * Second: Lieutenant Colonel Sam Bunthoeun, Deputy Commander of the Battambang Provincial Gendarmerie * Third: Lieutenant Colonel Chuob Nou, Commander of the District Gendarmerie Samlot * 4th: Lieutenant Chhoeun Sophat, Deputy Commander of Samlot District Gendarmerie Base * Fifth: Chief Chamnang Nop Sam Oeun, Assistant Samlot District Gendarmerie
Brigadier General Eng Hee, spokesman for the National Gendarmerie, also called on the public to use defamatory remarks to incite the internal divisions of the Gendarmerie, but apparently General Sao Sokha insisted. Professional ethics and the rule of law in the performance of their duties and will not be exempt from any military officers who violate the law.
It should be noted that General Meas Sovann was formerly the Commander of the Kandal Provincial Gendarmerie, then was transferred to the Commander of the Kampong Chhnang Provincial Gendarmerie before moving to the Commander of the Gendarmerie in Battambang until now.
(Phnom Penh): At 3 pm on December 20, 2019, the police force of Dangkor District Police Inspectorate sent Mr. Sarun Vithurak, the owner of PTT gas station near Kuosrov roundabout, Dangkor district, to the Phnom Penh Municipal Court after completion. The interrogation at the district inspectorate involved the use of severe violence against a teacher and was widely shared on Facebook.
