Ahead of the UN Climate Change Conference (COP25), which began on December 2, a UK-based website warned of carbon emissions. Encourage the implementation of the Paris Agreement to break through barriers and to avoid dangerous changes.
Many questions have been raised as to whether the action out of this meeting could be effective in curbing global warming and other biodiversity changes that are plaguing the planet. Ours.
The report states that a study of the causes of the melting of the ice sheet was compiled from up to 26 satellites, which monitored the effects of global warming. A suffix also leads to higher sea levels.
According to an analysis of climate change by the researchers, if there is a change in the glaciers of Antarctica and Greenland, it is important and of great concern to society. Humans, meanwhile, have a direct impact on sea level rise, which in turn leads to global climate change.
Analysis by NASA shows that wildfires in NSW emit no less than 195 tons of CO2. The British newspaper quoted experts as saying that the smoke from the wildfires was "extremely polluting" in the aftermath of the epicenter, which was a matter of concern among scientists.
At the UN Climate Conference in Madrid, the five principles that led to this meeting were presented: First, leadership is important because the COP25 meeting in Madrid took place due to the Chilean government's proposal. Come to this city after the social unrest in San Diego.
Second, there is a discrepancy between the discovery of climate change issues in practice because some major countries have not complied with the United Nations' desire to reduce carbon emissions. Not fully engaged to prevent overheating.
Third, the lack of consensus that will exacerbate climate change in 2020, and the next conference may be held in Glasgow, while the European Union expresses hope that by 2030 the EU bloc will set goals. No carbon, determined to reduce by 55%, as in the 1990s.
In 2014, there was an agreement on the environment signed by US President Barack Obama and Chinese President Xi Jinping, but since then there has been little realism.
Fourth, the complexity is like an elephant in a cramped room, impossible, because in 2015 in Paris, many countries submitted their first environmental plan. But for 2020, they appear to be finding it difficult to resolve, as the United States withdraws from the Paris Agreement on Climate Change.
Climate change has been going on since prehistoric times, but by the middle of the 20th century, it seemed to be on the rise. The Intergovernmental Panel on Climate Change (IPCC) has released its fifth assessment report, concluding that it is unfortunate that human influence dominates global climate change.
The report states that in the 21st century, the Earth's surface temperature has risen by 0.3 to 1.7 degrees Celsius. Rising sea levels, fluctuations in local climate, irregular weather events such as heat waves, desertification, sea level rise, acidity in seawater are also components of greenhouse gas emissions.
The scientists explained that it is important for people to work together to respond to global warming by reducing greenhouse gas emissions, adapting to the phenomenon, and for countries to work together to combat global warming. Climate change is under the auspices of the United Nations Framework Convention on Climate Change (UNFCCC).
