* Modern sports or mass sports such as running, recreation, distance 3 km and 5 km, with the preparation of nearly 2,000 participants. Cycling, which prepares nearly 200 students and residents to compete with professional athletes in the Cycling Federation.
* Traditional sports such as on-stage bokator performances for the presidency at the opening ceremony of the Sea Festival as another venue and off-stage performances. Chess, which competes for the first and second place, while a series of qualifiers have already been held in Phnom Penh, with about 10 remaining.
He added that there is also an international jet ski race in Kampong Bay canal, in front of Kampot Provincial Hall, which is a friendly competition with foreign riders from Indonesia, China, Thailand, Arabia and some other countries.
Not only that, there is also an international Khmer boxing competition to win the world title at the semi-professional level, which involves three types of boxers, including: amateur, semi-professional and professional boxer. Join famous players such as Roeung Sophoan and many other foreign players.
Apart from this, there are also traditional martial arts competitions of Indian athletes to make the sports activities in the sea festival in Kampot more diverse, provide fun for tourists and people while security issues. It has also been confirmed.
