On that occasion, Ms. Mean Sam An brought the memories and greetings from Ms. Men Sam An to all of you in the most friendly and warm feelings.
At the same time, she also welcomed and congratulated all the sisters of the Oddar Meanchey Provincial Women's Association Branch Committee who were newly appointed.
Ms. Mean Sam An added that since Cambodian women make up more than 52% of the total population, they have played an important role in the agricultural, industrial, informal and service sectors and have contributed to the national economy.
That is why the Royal Government has clearly defined that women are the backbone of economic and social development. The Royal Government of Cambodia has taken care to promote the value of women, especially in terms of gender composition. In the National Development Plan, the Royal Government is committed to continuing to implement the policy of gender composition through gender mainstreaming in all sectors and development programs. Nigerian drug dealer with 3kg of drugs sent to court
(Phnom Penh): The Phnom Penh Municipal Armed Forces on the morning of December 20, 2019, sent a 50-year-old black Nigerian man named FRANK UBALE and various drugs including pills, white gram, powder A total of 3 kg of white to the Phnom Penh Municipal Court to be handed over to the prosecutor's office to open an investigation and charge according to the law related to the crime of storing several kilograms of illegal drugs.
The suspect named FRANK UBALE was arrested by the Phnom Penh Military Police at 6:50 pm on December 16, 2019 at the point on Concrete Road No. 19 and Room No. 09, 1st Floor, Trapeang Thleung 4 Village, Sangkat Choam Chao 1, Khan Por Senchey, Phnom Penh.
In fact, the mission to crack down on drug trafficking by Nigerians was led by the Armed Forces of Po Sen Chey District, led by Lt. Col. Chim Rithy, in collaboration with the Special Forces of the Phnom Penh Military Police Drug Crimes Investigation Office, led by Lt. Col. Panh. Sopheap worked diligently for more than 3 months until the crackdown was completed.
After being taken to the Phnom Penh Gendarmerie Headquarters, the suspect confessed that all the drugs really belonged to him for trafficking in Phnom Penh, and that he had a Nigerian affiliation. The other two drug dealers who escaped are being investigated by the Phnom Penh Military Police.
Death news! Former University Rector of the University of Health Sciences, Dr. Wu Kimpor, has died.
(Phnom Penh): Prof. Dr. Vu Kimpor, former Rector of the University of Health Sciences and father-in-law, Mr. Vongsey Visoth, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Economy and Finance, passed away this morning, December 20, 2019, at the age of 88. By old age.
At present, the body of Professor Dr. Vu Kim Por is being kept for a traditional Buddhist ceremony at No. 29, Street 1966 in Poung Peat Village, Sangkat Phnom Penh Thmey, Khan Sen Sok, Phnom Penh. The body will be cremated at Wat Samrong Andet on the morning of December 23, 2019 at 9 am.
Prof. Wu Kimpor served as Undersecretary of State at the Ministry of Health and Rector of the University of Health from December 1998 to July 2006.
This news is considered as an invitation to relatives and close friends to attend the funeral of Professor Dr. Vu Kim Por for everyone.
