Please be informed that on December 19, 2019, Ms. Pheung Sakona, Minister of Culture and Fine Arts, did not agree with the intention of the Battambang Provincial Administration to dismantle the stone bridge in front of Battambang Provincial Hall left over from the French colonial period. .
Disagreeing with the intentions of the Battambang Provincial Administration, Ms. Phoeung Sakona wrote a letter to Deputy Prime Minister Chea Sophara, Minister of Land Management, Urban Planning and Construction, asking for intervention to find a solution to save the stone bridge. This one.
In her letter, Ms. Phoeung Sakona stated that the old stone bridge left by the French colony in front of Battambang Provincial Hall in Kamakor Village, Sangkat Svay Por, Battambang City-Province should not be demolished because it is more than 100 years old.
On the other hand, this bridge is the only remaining urban heritage building in Battambang province and the only remaining in Cambodia with historical, architectural, urban and environmental value.
The minister added that the bridge, considered a rare heritage, should be preserved and repaired and used as a pedestrian bridge.
The proposal to save this stone bridge has led to a lot of support from the Cambodian people, both in Battambang as well as in other provinces. They want this historic building to be preserved.
