Khmer Rouge tribunal issues press release on consideration of appeal and closing order in Case 004/02
The Pre-Trial Chamber was unable to obtain at least four affirmative votes for a joint judgment on the merits of the appeal against the Closing Order of the National and International Co-Investigating Judges in the case file. Case 004/02 against the accused O An. According to Rule 77 (13) of the Internal Rules, this judgment closes the way for protests.
In the same judgment, the Pre-Trial Chamber declared that the postponement of the Co-Investigating Judges' closing order after the completion of the investigation on O'An was incorrect and declared that the Co-Investigating Judges were at fault in their assessment. On the value as evidence and the unreliability of the evidence.
At the same time, the Pre-Trial Chamber declared in its unanimous decision that the issuance of two conflicting resolutions by the Co-Investigating Judges was illegal and in violation of the ECCC Legal Framework.
