Disagreeing with the intentions of the Battambang Provincial Administration, Ms. Phoeung Sakona wrote a letter to Deputy Prime Minister Chea Sophara, Minister of Land Management, Urban Planning and Construction, asking for intervention to find a solution to save a stone bridge. This.
On the other hand, this bridge is the only remaining urban heritage building in Battambang province and the only remaining in Cambodia with historical value, architecture, urban planning and environment.
The proposal to save this stone bridge has led to a lot of support from the Cambodian people, both in Battambang as well as in other provinces. They want this historic building to be preserved. Senior Ministry of Health official: Smoking and cigarette smoke are the main causes contributing to the high mortality rate in the world
(Kampong Thom): Smoking not only affects smokers, it also affects those around us, because the effects of cigarette smoke are many toxins that can cause people Can cause various malignant diseases.
Dr. Ung Phirun, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Health, said so on December 19, 2019 during the seminar on leadership in law enforcement and legal documents on tobacco control to lower authorities. National.
According to a senior official at the Ministry of Health, about 4,000 substances have been found in cigarette smoke, some of which are toxic and can cause cancer.
He said that due to addiction, deliciousness and reducing stress, most smokers ignore the effects of secondhand smoke on health. Whether you are a smoker or an indirect smoker, you can be affected to some degree. The health effects increase with the number of cigarettes smoked daily and the total time consumed.
He said that diseases caused by smoking include chronic respiratory diseases, lung cancer, chronic bronchitis and asthma. In addition to the effects on the respiratory system, smoking can also affect the cardiovascular system and can cause other cancers. Therefore, you should quit smoking and stay away from cigarette smoke for your own health and the health of those around you.
In addition, if you are a smoker who has symptoms such as chronic cough, fatigue or anxiety, shortness of breath, please seek medical advice to diagnose and get effective treatment.
Finally, the Secretary of State also advised that "smoking cessation can slow down the progression of bronchitis as well as the decline of the respiratory system." Therefore, all of you, young and old, should exercise diligently and stay away from drugs.
