She added that for today's business, there is nothing for sure, sometimes working as a weeder, sometimes harvesting rice or doing other work with all one's strength.
In particular, winning the grand prize from the carabao energy drink company here is very exciting. She confirmed that last weekend, after returning from harvesting rice for the villagers, she returned home to buy a can of Carabao energy drink from a vendor near her house. 100 million Riel prize on canned earrings.
At first, she did not think that it was a prize of 100 million Riel because she was illiterate, so she took it to someone to help her find out that she really won the prize of 100 million Riel and called to inform the company.
She stated that after receiving the big prize of 100 million riels, she will use some of it to pay off her debts and buy some farmland, and the rest will be used to build a house for a decent stay and set up a business to support the family's livelihood in the future.
Please note: The real prize is only available in cans with Khmer letters as symbols. Cambodia and Indonesia Launch Book and Workshop on "Moving Forward 60 Years of Friendship"
Ms. At Sophea expressed her deep gratitude and appreciation to the Indonesian Embassy in Phnom Penh, especially to Ambassador Sudirman for organizing this memorable event and for her many efforts to publish a special memoir on the historical journey of the people. The two nations have worked together for the last 60 years and shared a common desire for the future.
She said today's event was a summary of activities organized throughout the year to commemorate the establishment of diplomatic ties 60 years ago.
"Cambodia and Indonesia established formal diplomatic relations in 1959, but the communication between our two peoples has existed for centuries," she said. The similarities between Cambodia's first Angkorian temple of Angkor and Indonesia's Borobudur confirm the friendly relations between our two countries in the past.
This has laid a solid foundation for the two nations to maintain friendship and cooperation in both bilateral and multilateral frameworks to this day. Despite changes in the international and national contexts of the two countries over the past 60 years, the people of Cambodia and Indonesia continue to cultivate close friendships and work together to strengthen better ties. Between the two countries.
She added that Indonesia played a key role in hosting the negotiation process leading up to the 1991 Paris Peace Accords and sending nearly 2,000 peacekeepers to Cambodia as part of UNTAC's operations. (UNTAC) in the early 1990s. Therefore, the peace that allows Cambodia to develop as it is today is inseparable from Indonesia's contribution, and that is something we are still grateful for.
She said that commemorating the 60th anniversary of diplomatic relations between Cambodia and Indonesia this year will further strengthen the spirit of solidarity as well as strengthen fruitful cooperation between the two nations. The foundation of the existing interaction between our two peoples is long overdue.
