(Phnom Penh): Government officials in charge of providing loans to rice millers to collect rice to maintain the price of rice of farmers claim that the continuous investment to maintain the price of rice farmers is not a subsidy policy of the Royal Government That is a purely free market mechanism.
He said that the mechanism to maintain the price of rice farmers has been introduced by the Royal Government since 2016 after a small number of farmers dumped rice on the road in Battambang province to protest the decline in rice prices. This dumping of rice has caused a lot of trouble from some crooks.
He added that seeing the consequences in the rice sector related to the drop in prices, the Royal Government has gradually invested to provide credit for rice procurement and development of rice warehouses and rice dryers in some areas such as: Battambang province. , Prey Veng, Kampong Thom and plans to expand to other provinces.
Mr. Song Saran, President of the Rice Federation of Cambodia, mentioned the advantages of implementing the market mechanism for the Royal Government's rice sector, considering that this mechanism is appropriate to the global market situation.
He said that Cambodia's rice contributed only 1.2 percent to the world, so in the context of Cambodia's free market, such a small share can not prevent the decline in rice prices in the world market. No, therefore, if the government uses the subsidy mechanism, it will fail.
Mr. Song Saran also stated that in order to keep the price of farmers from falling, there are some mechanisms, farmers have to grow rice that has market demand, especially fragrant rice, which has the right variety and technique. Farmers must unite as an agricultural community to have access to accurate technical and market information.
As for the current price of rice for farmers, government officials and the private sector claim that it is reasonably priced, which helps farmers to benefit. Central Security Forces of the Ministry of Interior arrested two men on charges of fraud in connection with the purchase of a house in Sen Sok district
