Cambodia Airways is a local Cambodian airline based in Phnom Penh. Established in September 2017, the company officially launched its flight on July 10, 2018, flying from Phnom Penh to Siem Reap. The company currently has Airbus A319 and A320 aircraft serving a variety of domestic and international destinations, including Phnom Penh, Siem Reap, Sihanoukville, Macau, Bangkok, Fuzhou and Wenzhou. Etc.
As the "wing of Cambodia", Cambodia Airways focuses on setting up a network of flights between Phnom Penh, its hub, covering both China and ASEAN, and connecting North East Asia, Europe and the United States. North. Promote cultural exchange between Cambodians and people from other countries and build bridges between Cambodia and the world.
