(Tbong Khmum): Professor Thea Kruy, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Health and Chairman of the Medical Council of Cambodia, on December 18, 2019, stated that all doctors who have not yet registered with the Medical Council are strictly prohibited from examination. And cure disease.
This statement was made on the occasion of Prof. Thea Kruy presiding over the 6th Medical Professional Development Day in Tbong Khmum Province at the Provincial Health Department this morning, December 18, 2019.
Also present were Dr. Keo Vannak, Director of Tbong Khmum Provincial Health Department, Dr. Chhorn Mony, Deputy Director of the Department and Chairman of the Provincial Medical Council, as well as the presence of representatives of the Medical Council in the surrounding provinces, including: Kampong Cham, Kampong Thom, Kratie, Prey Veng, Svay Rieng and the presence of doctors, doctors from public and private institutions throughout the province.
Professor Thea Kruy stated, "All doctors who have not yet registered with the Medical Council are strictly prohibited from examining and treating patients, and doctors must come to register with the Medical Council and renew their development licenses." "The medical profession of the medical team can only be guaranteed to be a full and competent doctor."
Prof. Thea Kruy stated that a full-fledged doctor means a professional, strong, dignified, up-to-date, advanced, honest, highly ethical, do not do anything that should not be done, do not do, do work carefully, be careful and do not neglect. Absolutely with a high sense of responsibility.
