WASHINGTON (Reuters) - The US House of Representatives on Wednesday (Washington time) will vote on two articles drafted by the Justice Committee on formal prosecution or the removal of President Donald Trump. The abuse of power will hamper congressional investigations, and this election will be the third in US history.
US lawmakers will begin meeting to debate the article on the presidential removal procedure at 9 a.m. But the debate is not expected to have immediate results. All lawmakers will have six hours to debate, and the final vote will take place between 6:30 and 7:30 p.m. (Washington time).
Will Trump become the third US president to be formally charged?
When will the Senate election take place?
But that is unlikely to happen because the US Senate is currently under the control of Donald Trump's Republican Party. On the other hand, this party usually never voted against each other for fear of damaging the image and honor of the party as a whole, especially the supporters.
According to Article 2 of Article 4 of the US Constitution, federal officials, including the president, vice president and federal judges, will be removed through a dismissal procedure in the event of a formal indictment. For committing crimes such as treason, corruption and other serious crimes.
