(Battambang): In the case of the murder of a teacher in Boeung Run village, Samlot commune, Samlot district, Battambang province, the police searched and arrested the perpetrator, the victim's husband and a drug user.
Battambang Provincial Police Commissioner Major General Ouch Sokhon told Fresh News on the afternoon of December 18, 2019 that immediately after the incident and a thorough search, his professional forces finally identified the target and The perpetrator was arrested on the night of December 16, 2019, the victim's husband.
The commissioner added that the assailant was 31-year-old Prum Sous Samnang. In particular, the cause of the murder was because the assailant was jealous of the victim with his ex-girlfriend and the assailant was also a drug addict. After questioning, the task force prepared a case to be sent to court this afternoon for legal action.
(Kampong Cham): Dr. Ma Chhoeun, Member of Parliament for Kampong Cham Constituency and Chairman of the Central Working Group for Cheung Prey District, handed over six large-scale pump wells to people living in three communes, including: Sotip commune and two wells. Prey Char 2 Andong, Sramor 2 Andong Commune, Cheung Prey District, Kampong Cham Province.
In addition, Kampong Cham MPs also built a 500-meter-long red paved road for people in Sotip commune and provided 20 trucks of land around the school.
Dr. Ma Chhoeun always understands the well-being of all people without leaving anyone behind, especially to solve all the difficulties and shortages immediately to help improve the lives of the people to be better.
On the occasion of handing over 6 pump wells to the above people, the people were happy to have enough water sources without having to spend money to buy water for daily use. In addition, help improve the health of people through this well and stop using water from canals, which can cause problems for the health of residents.
On that occasion, the people who benefited from the use of the six wells were very happy and said, "Now our family has enough water to use near the house. Spend money to buy water like every other day. I am very thankful to our MP because he always came to visit to find out the difficulties, shortcomings and challenges, including natural disasters.
MP Ma Chhoeun has addressed all our specific requests, such as water wells, roads, pagodas, food and some materials that are necessary to provide peace in the lives of the villagers.
At the same time, Dr. Ma Chhoeun said that from the beginning of 2019 to December 14, 2019, he handed over 16 large-scale pump wells and out of 20 wells to people in each commune. There are two pump wells in each commune.
On the occasion of handing over the six wells, MP Ma Chhoeun also provided some funds to the people.
MP Ma Chhoeun said, "We will continue to visit and find out and solve all the problems or concerns of our people more to develop villages, communes and the country better, especially to improve the lives of our people." .
Please be informed that a pump well costs $ 2,000, which is the direct budget of MP Ma Chhoeun, and next week, Dr. will continue to use some more pump wells in each commune in Cheung Prey district.
Minister Say Sam Al: Due to the factors of complete peace and political stability, Cambodia has the opportunity to protect the environment, biodiversity conservation and sustainable development
(Phnom Penh): Mr. Say Sam Al, Minister of Environment, stated that due to the factors of complete peace and political stability, development has allowed Cambodia to have ample opportunity to consider environmental protection, biodiversity conservation and sustainable development to build society. Cambodia has a good, clean and comfortable environment for the people to live, and environmental quality and environmental sustainability are guaranteed.
The young minister said this in front of the students of the Active Military Academy (Tmat Tang) on the occasion of his lecture to more than 500 active military students on December 18, 2019.
Mr. Say Sam Al said: "We can do nothing if there is no peace and the Royal Cambodian Armed Forces has played an important role in maintaining peace, protecting the life of the nation, the life of the people who need to be strong. "Always."
The Minister emphasized that the success of the Ministry in the reform due to the factors of peace and development and the efforts to sacrifice the physical, mental and intellectual strength of the leadership of civil servants of the Ministry of Environment and under the support and guidance of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister.
Minister Say Sam Al said that until now, the Royal Government has increased the area of protected areas under the jurisdiction of the Ministry of Environment to about 41% of the country, equivalent to about 7.2 million hectares, which makes Cambodia stand. Second in Asia after Bhutan. As of 2019, there are about 168 communities in the protected areas of the Ministry of Environment.
It should be noted that the Active Officers' School is one of the many training centers of the Royal Cambodian Armed Forces. The school has a mission to train young officers, who in the future they will become battalion commanders or infantry platoon commanders in the future Royal Cambodian Armed Forces.
According to Lt. Gen. But Sopheap, Director of the Active Officers 'School, from 1995 to 2019, the Active Officers' Training School conducted 19 training courses for active duty officers, with a total of 1,574 students (102 females) who left. Served in various units throughout the Royal Cambodian Armed Forces.
The Minister of Environment encouraged and encouraged active military students to study hard to improve their service to the nation and for their future.
