During the graduation ceremony for Western University students on December 18, 2019, Samdech Techo Hun Sen highlighted the ability of the current sub-national officials, most of whom are at least graduates. Also higher education. Samdech Techo emphasized that at present, almost all provincial officials have completed higher education, while almost 100 percent of district officials have also completed higher education.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen also revealed that in the future, not only provincial and district officials will graduate from higher education. Even commune chiefs and commune chiefs may have higher education graduates running for mayor and commune chiefs.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen said that currently the national budget for development in communes is larger, so there is a need for highly capable officials to manage. According to Samdech Techo, placing commune chiefs and commune chiefs to complete higher education will improve the situation of governing the country.
Cambodian officials indicate that there are a total of 1,646 commune chiefs and commune chiefs across the country. Most commune chiefs and commune chiefs are elderly and have been educated in the old society.
It has been studied that management and development at the commune level is still limited due to the limited capacity of officials as well as the budget allocated to the commune level.
In 2020, the Royal Government will increase the budget for commune development to more than 120,000 US dollars. This reduction in funding to the commune level is seen as helping to improve the commune's current development. At the same time, the placement of younger and higher-level officials will also contribute to better development in communes.
Minister of Tourism and Governor of Kampot Province chaired a meeting of the Inter-Ministerial Commission to prepare for the Sea Festival in the coming days
(Kampot): Mr. Thong Khon, Minister of Tourism and Mr. Chiao Tai, Governor of Kampot Province, on December 18, 2019, chaired a meeting to review the final decision on the preparation of the Sea Festival, which the provincial administration and inter-ministerial Collaborate several months ago.
The Governor of Kampot Province said that the Kampot Provincial Administration has been working hard to implement the work of each sub-committee and cooperate with the relevant ministries for several months now. As a result, the work of implementing the plan to prepare for the organization of the 8th Sea Festival Round 2 in 2019 in Kampot province has achieved good results and can hope to run smoothly.
In fact, the achievements of the six sub-committees include:
* 1: Art exhibitions and other sports activities * 2: Food, beverage and environmental sanitation work * 3: Celebration and infrastructure * 4: Security, safety, public order and emergency * 5: Work Content of related protocols and meetings * 6: Supply work.
At the meeting, Minister Thong Khon encouraged the commission to bring in local agricultural products and food that show the identity of the province to be displayed and sold to as many people and tourists as possible. Can be done in the Sea Festival in Kampot.
The Minister of Tourism added that the promotion of video exhibitions on tourism products such as tourism communities, resorts, etc. is to show the people, tourists and promote more widely. And also to maintain security, safety and order for the delegates who come to the Sea Festival to facilitate the travel of artists, athletes, both national and international.
The minister also urged the subcommittee to visit restaurants, cafeterias, guesthouses, hotels, boutiques, bungalows, to ask them to present a list of food and services and to set prices correctly. The Minister expressed his hope that on the occasion of the 8th round of the 8th Sea Festival in Kampot Province in 2019 will receive no less than 500,000 tourists and people.
