Samdech said: "The second type of people are the people who solve the problem there, to share the well with the people to solve the problem. Intervention from above is one thing, but solving the problem at that place only shows the real ability, and if the officer does not solve it, just think about the report, the officer will continue to be taken to the so-called warehouse. "I can not continue to hold the job."
In this regard, Samdech Techo Hun Sen reminded of the case of the collapse of a nine-story building in Sihanoukville in June 2019. At that time, Samdech praised the relevant local authorities for joining forces to solve the problem on the spot, even though there was no intervention from the upper level.
Samdech said: "I can honestly say that I was sorry at that time, it was a time when the building collapsed for about two hours, I had to leave for Bangkok, I went down personally, but because I could not miss the meeting there. "That ASEAN meeting and related meetings, but I also ordered from Bangkok."
Samdech Techo continued: "What I regret is that the national officials lost their intervention. I commend the local officials who came together to gather forces to solve the problem there." "These points show the ability without waiting for the national level to go down."
