New flights from Phnom Penh to Yangon, Myanmar and Guiyang, China will launch on December 29!
(Phnom Penh): JC Airlines will officially launch flights from Phnom Penh to Yangon, Myanmar and Guiyang, China on December 29, 2019. This is a flight that flies through three countries: Cambodia, Myanmar and China, with direct flights from Phnom Penh to Guoyang.
JC Airlines continues to support a new policy called "One Road, One Belt" by working to develop and expand new airline networks, as well as to develop an "open sky policy" from Cambodia. For flights to destinations around the world.
JC Airlines' new routes aim to strengthen tourism integration and make it easier for customers to travel to all three cities. JC Airlines, based in Cambodia, will continue to maintain the position of "serving customers with love from the heart" as a top priority.
(Svay Rieng): Senior Minister Kun Kim, Secretary General of the Cambodian Veterans Association, on the afternoon of December 18, 2019, led a working group to visit the families of veterans and inspect the construction of houses donated by Samdech Techo Hun Sen. And Samdech Kittipritthbandit to give 200 houses to veterans in Chik Dey village, Andong Trabek commune, Romeas Hek district, Svay Rieng province.
