Samdech Krala Hom Sar Kheng changes Poipet border police chief, Brigadier General E Chamroeun to replace Colonel Khem Chetra
(Phnom Penh): Samdech Krala Hom Sar Kheng, Deputy Prime Minister and Minister of Interior, has announced the replacement of Poipet International Border Police Chief by Brigadier General E Chamroeun, replacing Colonel Khem Chetra. This is according to the announcement received by Fresh News on the afternoon of December 18, 2019.
According to Samdech Krala Hom Sar Kheng's announcement, Brigadier General E Chamroeun changed from the O'Yadao International Border Police Chief of the Second Gate Department to the Poipet International Border Police Chief of the First Gate Department. Separately, Colonel Khem Chetra from Poipet International Border Crossing Police Chief to O'Yadao International Border Crossing Police Chief.
Deputy Prime Minister Aun Porn Moniroth: Cambodia has great potential to seize the opportunities of the Fourth Industrial Revolution and the digital economy
(Phnom Penh): Dr. Aun Porn Moniroth, Deputy Prime Minister and Minister of Economy and Finance, on December 18, 2019, stated that Cambodia is a country with high potential for living in seizing opportunities from the revolution. The fourth industry and the digital economy.
This statement was made on the occasion that Dr. Aun Porn Moniroth presided over the opening of the first National Conference on Accounting under the theme "Role of Accounting Sector in the Digital Economy" held at Sokha Hotel, Phnom Penh this morning. December 18, 2019.
Deputy Prime Minister Aun Porn Moniroth stated that Cambodia is a country with high potential and livelihood to seize the opportunities from the Fourth Industrial Revolution and the digital economy based on four factors:
First, the demographic potential due to the presence of a large number of young people who are highly educated and quickly adapt to digital technology. Second, the rapid growth of the use of mobile phones and smart devices (Smart devices). Third, the rapid growth of technology through the flow of foreign direct investment. Fourth, the rapid impact of digitalization is happening in all major sectors of the national economy.
Dr. Aun Porn Moniroth added that in Cambodia, the digital economy is gradually emerging as new business activities emerge, such as the use of digital payments, the rise of online entertainment, e-commerce activities. Etc.
In addition, Deputy Prime Minister Aun Porn Moniroth stated that the Royal Government of Cambodia, the sixth legislature of the National Assembly, has considered the development of the digital economy as one of the most important priority areas for the country's development, as defined in the Rectangular Strategy - Phase 4.
In the first National Conference on Accounting under the theme "The Role of Accounting Sector in the Digital Economy", Deputy Prime Minister Aun Porn Moniroth also asked stakeholders to pay more attention to the following points:
1. The National Council for Accounting and the Institute of Professional Accountants and Auditors of Cambodia, together with other stakeholders, shall prepare, improve and harmonize the legal framework for the comprehensive management of the accounting sector that can meet the needs of the digital economy.
2: All professional accountants and auditors must adhere to professional ethics and technical standards, as well as develop professional capacity on a regular basis to strengthen the quality of audit and to improve the profession even better.
3. The National Accounting Council must prepare a clear and specific plan to modernize the technology system to manage the accounting and auditing profession more effectively.
4. The National Council of Accountants and the Institute of Professional Accountants and Auditors of Cambodia shall establish a legal framework to increase the number of accounting and auditing professionals at a rapid pace and to develop and implement capacity development plans for accountants and auditors in response to the impact. Of technological advancement in the context of the digital economy.
Please be informed that the first National Conference on Accounting under the theme "Role of Accounting Sector in the Digital Economy" was organized by the National Accounting Council, the Institute of Professional Accountants and Auditors of Cambodia and the ACCA Association of Professional Accountants and with the participation of national institutions, More than 600 private companies, accounting professionals and nonprofits.
The main purpose of the one-day National Conference is to provide participants with information on the latest developments in the accounting sector in Cambodia, and the role of professional accountants in the technological age in the digital economy.
In addition, to gather input from all participants as an additional basis for the preparation and improvement of policy and regulatory frameworks related to the accounting sector, especially to strengthen the role of regulators and professional accountants in the digital economy era. Mr. Ith Sam Heng wants to turn the National Technical Training Institute into a new technology research and innovation center
(Phnom Penh): In a meeting with civil servants, professors and academic staff and to celebrate the 20th anniversary of the National Technical Training Institute (NTTI), Mr. Ith Sam Heng, Minister of Labor and Vocational Training expressed his willingness to turn this institute into a research center And innovation in technology to provide students with the opportunity to explore innovations and research in the fields of civil engineering, civil engineering, electrical and information technology.
At the same time, this center is also a place to exchange ideas and share experiences with the private sector and institutions.
The Ministry of Labor has started to implement the modernization strategy of the Vocational Technical Education and Training System (TVET) and has issued recommendations urging all educational institutions under its supervision to pay attention to the effective implementation of this strategy to the trainees in response to Advancement of modern technology or so-called industrial revolution 4.0.
In order to promote the implementation of the above strategy, Mr. Ith Sam Heng determined to visit directly in all educational institutions under the Ministry of Labor one by one, for example, on December 18, 2019, Minister Ith Sam Heng Accompanied by Mr. Pich Sophoan, Permanent Secretary of the Ministry of Labor, as well as some leaders, visited the National Technical Training Institute (NTTI).
The above direct inspection activities were conducted to encourage the implementation of technical and vocational training policies and to implement the second priority set out in the strategic plan for employment development and technical training and Vocational 2019-2023, which further strengthens the modernization of the Vocational Technical Education and Training (TVET) system.
Mr. Ith Sam Heng encouraged the professors in the National Technical Training Institute to continue their education and training and encouraged the students to study hard in their skills to make this National Institute a leading institution in training. Technical and professional of the Ministry of Labor, including the management system of the capacity of trainers and the quality of students and trainees.
On that occasion, the Minister also drew the attention of young Cambodians should turn to the study of technical and vocational skills that are necessary and in great demand in the current and future labor market.
This statement was made by Samdech Pichey Sena Tea Banh this morning, December 18, 2019, on the occasion of Samdech together with General Ngo Sun Lich, Minister of Defense of the Socialist Republic of Vietnam, during the closing ceremony of the training exercise. Together on disaster relief on the Cambodia-Vietnam land border and humanitarian work in 2020 in Daun Tay village, Tuol Sdey commune, Chantrea district, Svay Rieng province.
