Mr. Chea Kimseng said that when he led the team to inspect the primary school, he saw that one of the school buildings that students are studying today is a kind of auditorium with two rooms made of corrugated iron sheets and a corrugated iron roof. There are leaks, the walls are old and some places are broken.
At the same time, the governor of Choam Ksan district advised the school leaders and the community, who are the guardians of the students, to renovate the old auditorium building to make it easier for students to study.
