The Association of Southeast Asian Nations (ASEAN) is a regional organization comprising the ten member countries of Southeast Asia, including Thailand, Malaysia, Singapore, the Philippines, Indonesia, Brunei, Vietnam, Myanmar, Laos and Cambodia. April 1999, during a meeting in Vietnam.
ASEAN is a regional organization that has been promoting intergovernmental cooperation and facilitating integration among all members since its inception on 8 August 1967. The main purpose of this organization is to promote economic growth, social progress. And social development for all members, as well as the protection of regional stability and the provision of a mechanism for member states to resolve conflicts peacefully.
ASEAN covers an area of 4.4 million square kilometers, equivalent to 3% of the total land area. All member countries have a total population of over 600 million, or 8% of the world's population. ASEAN has been compared to the world's fifth largest economy after the United States, China, Japan, Germany and the United Kingdom. Camel Cement receives high support from customers for both quality and good service of construction material distribution depot owners.
