(Svay Rieng): On the morning of December 18, 2019, the Royal Cambodian Armed Forces and the Vietnamese People's Army held a ceremony to open and close the disaster relief exercise in the border area together and humanitarian work in 2020 in Dauntei village, Tuol Sdey commune, Chantrea district, province. Svay Rieng.
The ceremony was held in the presence of Samdech Pich Sena Tea Banh, Deputy Prime Minister and Minister of National Defense, and General Ngo Sun Lich, Minister of Defense of Vietnam, and inaugurated the Cambodia-Vietnam Friendship Health Center.
The military exercises are aimed at sharing experiences and benefiting the people of the two countries when disasters such as natural disasters such as floods, wildfires or other natural disasters occur. Eventually, along with contributing to the promotion of cooperation and development in the border areas for growth.
The duration of the training exercise is 9 days from 10 to 18 December 2019. 265 participants from the Vietnamese side, 471 from the Cambodian side and 1,143 participants.
The general said that the disaster relief exercise with the Vietnamese side is to prepare joint forces to help people along the border of the two countries as they face natural disasters or disasters. One happens that.
"In accordance with the instructions of the Royal Government, the Ministry of National Defense will continue to do this exercise with neighboring countries, not only with Vietnam, but also with Thailand and Laos," he said. The exact time has not yet been set.
General Moeng Samphan confirmed that the disaster relief exercises jointly conducted between the armies of the two countries, Cambodia and Vietnam, now have four exercises, including:
Exercise 1: Rescue people during floods, with two helicopters to fly to check the flooded area and transport people to safety.
Exercise 3: The activities of the 911th Parachute Special Forces, the 70th Brigade and the Navy, which searched and transported people to safety with the construction of shelters. Disaster and short-term livelihood security.
Exercise 4: is to transport people to the health center when people have various diseases in a timely manner.
It should be informed that this is the first disaster relief exercise that Cambodia and Vietnam have done together and the Ministry of National Defense will continue to do this exercise with neighboring countries, not only with Vietnam. Will have to do with Thailand and Laos as well, but at this time has not been set a specific time.
The organization of the exercise between the Cambodian army and the Vietnamese army is an initiative of Samdech Techo Hun Sen himself, which aims to cooperate to help people along the border in case of disasters.
