Minister Tram Iv Tek: Although there is no digital government policy yet, some government ministries and institutions are using electronic systems to manage their work digitally.
(Phnom Penh): Mr. Tram Iv Tek, Minister of Posts and Telecommunications, on December 17, 2019, chaired an inter-ministerial meeting on the drafting of a digital government policy framework with the participation of leaders. Inter-ministerial-related institutions as well.
He added that although the Royal Government does not yet have a digital government policy to guide the implementation, but now in some ministries, state institutions and public entities have been using electronic systems to manage digital work and provide. Its administrative services remotely reach the people and are convenient.
The Minister emphasized that building a digital government is a big task that requires the participation of senior leaders of the Royal Government at all levels through the formulation of strategic policies, the development of laws, regulations, institutional management, strategic planning. Finance, phase planning, implementation of computer systems and the provision of public services to the people.
The Minister gave a presentation to the meeting to better understand the work arrangements related to the formation of digital government and the experience that some of the leading countries in this field such as the Republic of Korea, Singapore and Estonia have done in The development of digital government as well.
