10 Cambodian universities join BNEUF World Digital Library
The BNEUF Digital Library provides easy access to up to 10 million datasheets, resources, pedagogical methods, science and culture in French and many other languages.
These resources come from 990 institutions that are members of the French Higher Education Agency (AUF), which is present in 118 countries, including Cambodia. Ten AUF member universities in Cambodia will contribute to the development of this library.
Mr. Oum Romney, Director General of the Institute of Technology of Cambodia (Techno) said that BNEUF allows us to raise the value of expertise at the international level, and also allows unlimited access to documents such as knowledge and skills. He said the library, which has already been built and distributed, can find about 18,000 professionals from all disciplines.
"Opening the door to the international community is at the heart of our institution's strategy," he said. "BNEUF will enable us to expand our network of global education partners and exchange experts to improve the quality of training and research."
BNEUF is within the framework of the four programs of IDNEUF activities that the AUF has launched in accordance with the mandate decided by the French-speaking Minister of Higher Education. It is an initiative that emerges from the decision of the first meeting of the French Minister of Higher Education in 2005 in Paris to meet the challenges of universities, especially universities. Developing countries.
In this context, digital tools are important because of their high level of competence and are unique in helping to solve a wide range of public learning problems, making it easier for them to acquire knowledge. The creativity in these areas is enormous.
