Remarks by Samdech Techo Hun Sen Presenting Diplomas to Nearly 3,000 Western University Students
(Phnom Penh): Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, on December 18, 2019, presented diplomas to approximately 2,831 students of Western University, including 1,614 females. Today's graduating students have associate degrees, bachelor's and master's degrees, graduated in 2017-2018 and 2018-2019 academic year.
The graduation ceremony took place at the Koh Pich Convention and Exhibition Center. Mr. Te Lorin, Chairman of the Board of Directors of Western University, told Fresh News that the noble presence of Samdech Techo Hun Sen is a great honor for the University, especially for the graduates.
Key remarks of Samdech Techo Hun Sen:
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that today there are two exercises, including disaster relief exercises in the event of a plane crash in Siem Reap and disaster relief exercises on the border with Vietnam.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen requested that there be no slander on social media related to the exercise in Siem Reap, such as the plane crash, because this exercise is related to rescue in the event of a plane crash.
* Samdech Techo stated that this afternoon there will be a meeting with the Association of Higher Education Institutions. The meeting will discuss many issues related to education, such as improving the quality of education and budget issues.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that without human resources can not develop the nation. Samdech Techo Hun Sen said that Cambodia is very poor because of political mistakes from one generation to another.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that the genocidal regime of Pol Pot killed human resources, causing Cambodia to lack human resources after the liberation of the country.
* Samdech Techo stated that Singapore can not find fresh water to drink, but why is this country growing? Progress because of the right policy and rich human resources.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that after the genocidal regime of Pol Pot, Cambodia made efforts to replant people.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that planting people is very difficult, not as easy as planting trees.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen praised Western University for helping to train human resources. Samdech Techo also congratulated all the winning students.
* In addition to congratulating Samdech Techo Hun Sen, he called on students to further develop their knowledge and ability. Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that there is no end to education and knowledge.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that the three main factors that lead to a successful work include: planning, implementation and random factors. Good planning achieves 30%, good implementation assignments achieve 30% and another 40% depends on the random factors that will sink (random factors reflect the ability to solve).
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that the King has already signed the Financial Law for 2020.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that officials who are good at reporting and blaming the lower level must be put in the warehouse and not be allowed to work. Samdech Techo Hun Sen expressed his satisfaction and wanted officials who are good at solving problems on the spot.
Building problems in Sihanoukville In the past, Samdech Techo Hun Sen has blamed national officials for lack of control and mobilization to solve problems while local officials are doing a good job.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that because some ministries were slow to transfer power to the sub-national level, Samdech decided directly to sign the decision to remove the power to sub-national officials.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that some ministers embraced the work and did not want to drop it to the sub-national level.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen recalled that he had reminded the French government to strengthen French language training in Cambodia in 1982, but France ignored it, leading to a decline in the use of the French language in Cambodia.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that the historical events of December 2 were three: including December 2, 1978, the establishment of the United Front for National Salvation, December 2, 1987, the first round of talks between Samdech and Samdech Norodom Sihanouk in France. . Samdech Techo considered this December 2, which lasted 32 years, as the beginning of a turning point in the history of political negotiations in Cambodia. December 2, 1998, the year Samdech set out the Triangle Strategy.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that the three angles of this triangular strategy include: the first angle, the internalization of the country, the second angle, the fastest integration into the international community, and the third angle is the concentration of efforts. All to reduce poverty.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that the negotiation process to end the war between Samdech and His Majesty Norodom Sihanouk was very difficult because some countries did not want to have a negotiation meeting.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that the process of finding peace in Cambodia is not easy. Samdech Techo Hun Sen recalled that during the negotiations, the Cambodian, tripartite and Cambodian states could not even sit at the same table, which is why the Japanese Foreign Minister, as a facilitator, had to change the table.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that there are four factors that led Cambodia to decide to join ASEAN. The first factor is the principle of non-interference in the internal affairs of member countries; Of Cambodian diplomacy.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen urged those who succeeded him to continue to work in a consular manner for ASEAN.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen regrets the failure to attend the ASEAN-ROK and Mekong-Republic of Korea Summits.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that Samdech will issue a circular instructing government institutions to make adequate human rights reports.
It should be noted that although the process of overthrowing the President has never been successful or will not be successful, it will have a significant impact on Donald Trump ahead of the upcoming presidential election. Going during November 2020.
