(Phnom Penh): Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, on Wednesday, December 18, 2019, presented diplomas to 2,831 Western University students in Phnom Penh, Cambodia. There were 1,614 women. Today's graduating students have associate degrees, bachelor's and master's degrees, graduated in 2017-2018 and 2018-2019 academic year.
The Chairman of the Board claimed that the presence of Samdech Techo Hun Sen at the graduation ceremony was a wish of the students from his university.
Western University is a private university in Cambodia that has been working with the Royal Government to develop human resources. The University is training undergraduate and postgraduate students to implement their plans in order to participate in the implementation of education policies and strategic plans on ensuring high quality educational services.
The University also applies the principle of academic competition to select the best students of the year, in which students ranked 1st to 3rd place will receive certificates and additional scholarships in the next academic year and apply the principle of "Students learn better Pay less. ”
Please note that Western University has another educational institution as its annex, Western International School, which has been training students from Kindergarten to Grade 12 in 16 locations, including 14 locations in Phnom Penh, Sihanoukville. 1 location and Takhmao city, 1 study location in Khmer and English in accordance with national and international standards, with the permission of the Ministry of Education, Youth and Sports.
