Kandal Provincial Police Visits Former Kien Svay District Police Inspector in Hospital
(Kandal): After receiving the information that the former Kien Svay District Police Inspector, Mr. Pa Sam Et, was being treated at the Cho Ray Hospital in Phnom Penh, on the afternoon of December 17, 2019, Major General Eav Chamroeun, Kandal Provincial Police Commissioner, Assigned his delegation to visit and bring 2,150,000 Riels to support the treatment.
The delegation of Kandal Provincial Police led by Lt. Col. Seng Kimkhon, Deputy Commissioner for Human Resource Planning.
According to Mr. Pa Sam Et's family, Mr. Pa Sam Et was weak and tired and his hands and feet were sent to Choray Hospital in Phnom Penh on December 16, 2019. To date, his condition has improved, but He has not been released from the hospital yet.
Please note that Mr. Pa Sam Et is a former Kien Svay District Police Inspector who has been retired and currently serves as a Kien Svay District Councilor.
On behalf of Major General Eav Chamroeun, Kandal Provincial Police Commissioner, Mr. Seng Kimkhon wished Mr. Pa Sam Et a speedy recovery and that when he returned home, he should take care of his health. At the same time, the Deputy Commissioner also handed over 2,150,000 Riels to Mr. Pa Sam Et for medical treatment.
