DPM Yim Chhay Ly Presides Over the Closing Ceremony of a Project to Eliminate Cataracts in Kampong Cham Province
(Kampong Cham): Deputy Prime Minister Yim Chhay Ly, Chairman of the Council for Agricultural and Rural Development, representing Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, on the afternoon of December 17, 2019, presided over the official closing ceremony of the Project to Eliminate Illness. Cataracts, funded by the Asia Foundation for the Prevention of Blindness, is a grant from the People's Republic of China.
Prof. Mam Bunheng, Minister of Health, stated that the Memorandum of Understanding between the Ministry of Health of Cambodia and the Hong Kong Belt and Road Center and the Asia Foundation for the Prevention of Blindness will be signed on November 19, 2017. Successfully completed now.
The Minister emphasized that the successful implementation of the project, an outreach campaign was implemented by the National Center for Health Promotion of the Ministry of Health throughout Kampong Cham province for the first purpose: to raise the awareness of the people in the community about cataracts. And the benefits of cataracts; and secondly, increase the ability of people with cataracts to receive free cataract services at Kampong Cham Hospital.
The main activities carried out during the 18 months, including Guangxi Provincial Hospital, invited two ophthalmologists and six ophthalmologists to do a short internship at Guangxi Provincial Hospital and return. Participate in helping a group of volunteer doctors in Guangxi Province.
At the same time, Deputy Prime Minister Yim Chhay Ly said that eye disease is also a disease that needs urgent care. The eye is one of the most important organs for proper and timely care and treatment for everyone because eye health is very important for everyone.
