People with disabilities in Cambodia are being taken care of by the Royal Government
(Kampong Thom): Under the leadership of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, the Prime Minister of Cambodia has been promoting high attention through practical activities in the implementation of laws, sub-decrees, legal documents on people with disabilities.
"My family and I are very happy that I have now received a loan from the Cambodian Red Cross to start a new business," said Mam Vand, a resident of Stung Thmey village, Bramoy commune, Veal Veng district, Pursat province.
"Today I am a soldier and grow corn with my wife to earn extra income to raise our children, but due to lack of funds, my regime can not afford to spend more capital. To increase employment. "But now I have hope, when I get an interest-free micro loan from the Cambodian Red Cross to buy durian in addition to growing corn, and we are determined to make this business grow."
At the same time, Ms. Phay Sinuon and her husband also said, "We are both very happy, we have money to do business capital, using the money from this loan to start to earn more. "I will try to increase the yield to make life more prosperous, not as short as now."
At the same time, the 22 families also thanked Samdech Kittipritthbandit Bun Rany Hun Sen, President of the Cambodian Red Cross, who took care of their children at all times, in all difficult times, by trying to solve their children's problems from suffering. And help improve the lives of all children without leaving any suffering.
On the occasion of visiting and providing loans on December 15-16, 2019, Ms. Men Neary Sopheak, Acting Secretary General of the Cambodian Red Cross, stated that "This interest-free micro-loan is an initiative of Samdech Kittiprit. Dr. Bun Rany Hun Sen, President of the Cambodian Red Cross, by Samdech always understands all the difficulties of all people, especially poor people want to create a business but lack capital.
She said that therefore, Samdech Kittipritthbandit decided to establish an interest-free loan program for people who are poor and need to create and increase more pre-employment since 2001.
Pursat province started providing loans in 2002 to people in Kravanh and Veal Veng districts of Pursat province, which have a lot of landmines and explosive remnants of war. Vines and other occupations in the mountains.
So far, 735 families in Pursat province have received interest-free loans from the Cambodian Red Cross and used them in accordance with the principles to grow crops, raise animals, sell groceries, garment, hairdressing, repair bicycles and motorcycles. Original.
On that occasion, Ms. Men Neary Sopheak, Acting Secretary General of the Cambodian Red Cross, also brought the words of Samdech Kittipritthbandit Bun Rany Hun Sen, who sent greetings to consider the lives and well-being of the people, especially to encourage all families of fighters. To continue to strive to expand the business to improve the family life.
At the same time, Samdech Kittipritthbandit Bun Rany Hun Sen congratulated all the front line fighters who gave their time to live with their families to serve the motherland, while his wife lived at home, worked hard and expanded her business to raise children. For a prosperous future.
Please be informed that at present, the Cambodian Red Cross interest-free micro-loan has been implemented in 12 target districts in Preah Vihear, Oddar Meanchey, Banteay Meanchey, Pursat and Kandal provinces. Golden FX Link shares derivative investment knowledge
(Stung Treng): Golden FX Link Capital participated in a provincial workshop in Stung Treng on "What is Derivatives Trading: Investment Preparation and Related Awareness?"
