Mr. Long Samnang expressed the company's commitment to continue to develop the derivatives market in Cambodia as well as other developed countries.
(Phnom Penh): General Him Yan, Deputy Commissioner General of the National Police for Traffic Order, confirmed the traffic police's commitment to implement the plan to use security cameras at traffic lights to fine traffic offenders at home, despite some consequences. Such as not naming vehicles and relocating.
Speaking to Fresh News, General Him Yan confirmed that in order to carry out this work, technical training is required for traffic police officers to be able to operate. However, he could not confirm the exact time of the start of the enforcement of home fines for traffic offenders.
The general added that the two consequences that traffic police face in implementing the use of security cameras at traffic lights to fine the house are the same consequences that the police have experienced in the implementation of fines for speeding. The problem is that the vehicle owner does not have the correct name, making the issuance of a fine bill to the original owner and relocation, which makes it difficult for the police to find the vehicle owner.
Director General Him Yan confirmed that "we are committed to implement this work, no matter how many results we take, now our officials are training to be able to implement."
Please be informed that in addition to the plan to use security cameras equipped with traffic lights in Phnom Penh to fine the house, the police also warned to post criticism on Facebook for those who are fined for driving disrespecting traffic lights and parking disrespect the law. Also, this is done to awaken the perpetrator to be ashamed and change the habit to respect the law.
