(Phnom Penh): Samdech Krala Hom Sar Kheng, Deputy Prime Minister, Minister of Interior and Chairman of the National Committee for Sub-National Democratic Development (NCDD) this morning, December 17, 2019. Demonstrates the significant achievements made after the implementation of the "National Program for Democratic Development" for the past nine years related to public administration reform.
Notable achievements made by Prince Sar Kheng include:
Management systems of sub-national administrations have also been gradually implemented and improved, including planning systems, fund transfer and financial management systems, human resource management and development systems, inter-administrative communication systems, and control systems. Examine legitimacy, technical support systems and local dispute mediation systems.
At the beginning of 2019, about 62,000 staff of the Ministry of Interior working in the sub-national administration and staff of the Ministry of Social Affairs, Veterans and Youth Rehabilitation who work in the capital-provincial orphanages were also transferred to Already under the direct control of each sub-national administration.
In the past, functions in a number of priority areas, including environment and natural resources, social affairs, rural development, and more than 200 administrative service functions, have also been gradually transferred to sub-national administrations in the form of Deliver and delegate for test implementation as well.
* Fourth: Related to financial decentralization: So far, the Royal Government has transferred a total of more than 2.978 million US dollars to the sub-national administration for management and use under its discretion to meet the needs. Of the people in its jurisdiction.
Based on the sub-decree on the transfer of additional resources from the state budget to the commune / sangkat administration, which was issued in August 2019, in 2020, each commune / sangkat will receive an average total budget of approximately $ 122,000. That is for the average local development expenditure of more than $ 70,000, which is a double amount compared to 2019.
* Fifth: Relevant institutions to support decentralization and deconcentration reform: In accordance with the Law on the Administration of Capital, Provinces, Municipalities, Districts, Khans, NCDD has been established to guide and coordinate the preparation and implementation of decentralization and deconcentration reform programs.
At the same time, Samdech Krala Hom Sar Kheng also emphasized that the Royal Government has a long-term political will and vision for decentralization reform. Although the 10-year National Program will be completed by the end of 2020, based on the Rectangular Strategy Phase 4 and based on the lessons learned from the past implementation, the Royal Government will continue to design and implement the National Period Program. Another new length to be implemented from 2021 onwards.
