(Phnom Penh): Borey Leng Navatra Company would like to inform those who are looking for a job that Borey Leng Navatra needs to recruit 30 sales staff.
Three accounting staff work full time in both sexes.
The selection criteria are:
1: Honest 2: High responsibility 3: Able to work in a team 4: Able to complete missions in the province 5: Friendly, good communication skills.
The company has been operating in Cambodia for about 4 years. The company currently has a semi-finished factory in Kampong Cham city, Kampong Cham province, and another factory along National Road 6A in Muk Kampoul district, Kandal province.
Last week, the news production team of Fresh News visited the semi-finished factory in Kampong Cham to find out about the factory production process. Inside the factory, it was seen that the factory was actively involved in processing wood into plywood.
Mil Vuthy, general manager of the factory, told Fresh News that the factory in Kampong Cham had been operating for about four years. The factory is responsible for turning the wood into strips and drying it before sending it to the factory in Muk Kampoul district, Kandal province to produce the final finished product and release it on the market.
Mr. Mil Vuthy pointed out that in this factory, about 100 cubic meters of wood can be produced per day, and the wood used to make the board is rubber tree, acacia tree and acacia tree.
The general manager of the factory also said that due to the current high demand for the board in Cambodia, the production of the board does not have a problem in sales. But what is a problem for the factory is that it is difficult to find wood for processing.
According to Mr. Mil Vuthy, the company is currently collecting rubber trees and trees from people in Kampong Cham province to make this board. In that, the people's roots were collected by the company as well.
Deum Kor is a kind of plant that was not very popular in the beginning, people grow it only for cotton, but most of the trees are left behind. But now the origin of the people in Kampong Cham is being collected by the company with a reasonable price. Mr. Wutty said that the tree was collected by the company for more than $ 20 per cube.
Mr. Wutty claimed that the trees that people used to leave behind are now making people earn high profits, some of which can sell for tens of thousands of dollars.
In order to improve the livelihood of the people and its production line, Mr. Wutty called on the people who have vacant land to plant trees to sell to the company. Mr. Vuthy claimed that the company will collect all purchases with reasonable prices.
Answer the question, does the company collect when all the people grow more? The general manager of the company pointed out that there is a high demand for billboards in the market today, so no matter how many trees there are, the company collects.
The presence of a wood processing plant to make plywood is not only contributing to reducing the import of plywood from abroad and boosting the national economic growth. But also contributes to the employment and promotion of people in Kampong Cham.
According to Vuthy, the factory in Kampong Cham currently employs about 300 people with wages ranging from $ 250 to $ 1,000. Most of the workers are from Kampong Cham province.
People who have roots and want to sell to the company, please contact: 097 249 9889. General Hing Bun Heang: Without Country Peace, There Can Be No Democracy and Human Rights
(Kandal): Honorary General Dr. Hing Bun Heang, Chairman of the National Task Force for Kandal Stung District, Kandal Province, inaugurated the Assembly Hall in Wat Po Andet, Doeum Rus Commune and met with about 2091 people in Kandal Stung District this morning. December 2019.
"If the country is not peaceful, there is no democracy and no human rights," said Honorary General Hing Bun Heang.
