(Kampong Speu): Mr. Veng Sakhon, Minister of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries, on December 17, 2019, instructed the Forestry Administration to promote the registration of more community forests in order to manage and protect the forest to survive. Descendants.
At the same time, the Minister also urged the Forestry Administration to make a proper title deed for community forest land to avoid illegal logging and encroachment on community forest land.
This introduction was made on the occasion of Minister Veng Sakhon and Senator Tycoon Ly Yong Phat on the morning of December 17, 2019 to meet with the community of eight forest in eight communes, Thpong district, Kampong Speu province.
The ceremony was also attended by the leadership of the Ministry of Delegation of the Royal Government of Cambodia in charge of Forestry Administration, government officials, local authorities and more than 300 people. The purpose of this event is to try to better connect the leadership with the local people and to better understand the well-being, daily problems, needs, requests or suggestions and solve those problems to the forest community gradually as needed.
Mr. Chheang Tola, Director of Kampong Speu Provincial Department of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries, said that Kampong Speu Province has 50 community forests, of which 34 communities are registered with the Ministry, covering an area of 13,745 hectares in six districts. Separately, Thpong district has 3 forest communities, including the eight-corner community, covering an area of 937 hectares with a total membership and registered with the Ministry in 2018.
He said that most of the eight-corner forest community is mainly engaged in agriculture and exploration of forest products and by-products on an area of more than 937 hectares, covered with a variety of trees that provide benefits for the livelihood of communities that depend in part on natural resources. This precious.
Minister Veng Sakhon and Tycoon Ly Yong Phat had a talk with the community, bringing the greetings of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister, Samdech Kittipritthbandit, Samdech President of the National Assembly, the President of the Senate and other top leaders to the community. After all, Samdech wished all the families happiness and prosperity.
The Minister praised the leadership of the Forestry Administration, the Department of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries, local authorities and communities for their joint efforts to establish this community forest in order to preserve and develop the forest as a natural resource.
The Minister instructed the Provincial Department of Agriculture of Kampong Speu to work hard to find projects to help develop the eight-corner forest community, change the image, change the livelihood, maintain the sustainability of forest conservation and development both now and in the future.
In order to alleviate the problems that hinder the development of the eight-corner forest community, Minister Veng Sakhon, Tycoon Ly Yong Phat and the Forestry Administration have donated an administrative building, a water tank for firefighting, a bathroom, a GPS and clothing. For forest patrol, equipped with solar water pump and community support 2 million Riels. Separately, for the community who came to participate, each received 20,000 Riels.
