Phnom Penh Municipal Court Holds a Meeting with Judicial Police Officers on "Inspection and Enforcement Process on Dispute and Dispute Resolution"
(Phnom Penh): In order to implement the legal mechanism more effectively to manage security, public order and social order in the era of a peaceful nation and the development of a process of monitoring and strengthening the implementation of laws and rules on dispute resolution is necessary. It is very important that all competent institutions and units must participate in the implementation effectively.
In response to this rule, the Phnom Penh Municipal Court on the morning of December 17, 2019 convened a meeting by inviting senior leaders of the Judicial Police from the Ministry of Interior, Phnom Penh Municipal Police, District Police Inspectorate, and Municipal Military Police officers. Khans under the theme "Strengthening law enforcement and solving challenges", especially on drug crimes, which are currently facing problems.
The meeting was chaired by Mr. Horm Mengse, Deputy Chief of the Court, Mr. Keo Sothea, Deputy Prosecutor of the Phnom Penh Municipal Court, General Mak Chito, Deputy Commissioner General of the National Police, and other senior judicial officers. From the capital-district.
The meeting focused on the problem of invading drugs, which are complex and complex issues.
The joint content of the meeting between the judiciary and the judiciary on "Monitoring and Enforcement of Law Enforcement and Rules on Dispute Resolution" this morning was decided by the meeting to set the direction for future implementation. To maintain better security and social order, especially drug crimes.
