Samdech Krala Hom Sar Kheng Disseminates and Implements 4 Sub-Decrees Related to Functions and Structure of Public Administration
(Phnom Penh): Samdech Krala Hom Sar Kheng, Deputy Prime Minister, Minister of Interior and Chairman of the National Committee for Sub-National Democratic Development (NCDD) this morning, December 17, 2019. Disseminate and implement the sub-decree on the functions and structure of the municipal, district and khan administration and the sub-decree on the assignment of management functions and the provision of health services to the capital-provincial administration.
The launching ceremony was held at the Ministry of Interior with the participation of the Senate, the National Assembly, representatives of ministries, institutions of the Royal Government, sub-national administrations, private sector development partners and civil society organizations. Visit Kampot province, join the 8th Sea Festival and enjoy new tourist resorts (Video inside)
(Phnom Penh): Kampot has become an attractive tourist destination in the south of Cambodia. This new destination has become a holiday destination for all kinds of national and international guests.
From December 20-22, 2019, Kampot Province will soon hold the 8th Sea Festival Round 2 to provide opportunities for people and tourists to visit.
Prior to the Sea Festival, the Ministry of Tourism introduced tourists and residents to a number of tourist attractions in the province, including:
* Dang Prek Park: Located in Bot Kbal Damrey village, Snom Prampi commune, about 8 km from Kampot city. The resort is located next to the Kampong Bay canal, which is full of nature and fresh air. You can take a cable car, cross a canal, take a kayak, ride a fridge and enjoy delicious food there.
* Doung Ter Resort: Located in Snom Prampi village, Mak Prang commune, Teuk Chhou district, about 7 km from the new bridge, Kampot city. The resort is located next to the Kampong Bay canal, which is full of nature and fresh air. You can bathe, enjoy kayaking, boating, duck skating and many more delicious food.
* Trapeang Sangke Tourism Community: Located in Kampong Kes Village, Trapeang Sangke Commune, Teuk Chhou District, 7 km from Kampot City, on National Road 33 from Kampot to Kep. This community is a natural community, a large mangrove conservation area in Kampot province. In the community, there are services such as accommodation, community food, canoeing, mangrove forest, and mangrove trees for sale for guests to plant as a souvenir.
Boating area along Kampong Bay canal is located in Tvi Khang Tbong village, Sangkat Andong Khmer, Kampot city. You can enjoy the fresh air, enjoy the scenery, watch the sunset, see the tamarind and eat delicious food there.
