(Phnom Penh): Ms. Mar Amara, Executive Vice President and Chairman of the Financial Committee of ACLEDA Bank, confirmed to Fresh News in a weekly special guest interview that as planned, the first IPO (IPO) of ACLEDA Bank is expected to enter the Cambodia Securities Exchange in the first quarter of 2020.
ACLEDA Bank will be the first bank to issue IPOs on the Cambodia Securities Exchange after the issuance of five previous IPOs.
"Of course, we hope and believe that ACLEDA Bank's entry into the Cambodia Securities Exchange now will help make the Cambodia Securities Exchange more active and prosperous in the future to contribute to the development of the financial banking sector," said Amara. Investment and securities in Cambodia.
After ACLEDA received permission from the National Bank of Cambodia to conduct the initial public offering (IPO) process, ACLEDA is now applying for listing on the Cambodia Securities Exchange. Authorized to be listed on the Cambodia Securities Exchange, the Bank will apply to the Securities and Exchange Commission of Cambodia (SECC) for an IPO.
As for the capital that ACLEDA Bank plans to collect from the public through the issuance of the equity securities, Ms. Mar Amara has not yet confirmed, as it has not yet received permission from the authorities.
Ms. Mar Amara stated that the issuance of equity securities is very important for ACLEDA Bank because the issuance of equity or shares may contribute to ACLEDA Bank's more successful, sustainable growth and prosperity. Good governance and financial inclusiveness to contribute to the socio-economic development of Cambodia, especially through:
 Second: The continuous development of financial technology as well as the diversification and innovation of the services and operations of ACLEDA Bank to serve the customers and the public better and better.
Third, gaining more trust and confidence by providing opportunities for customers, investors and the general public to invest in ACLEDA Bank by purchasing shares at their own resource level and becoming a shareholder of ACLEDA Bank. Will benefit through annual dividend distribution and increase in share price.
