(Phnom Penh): The National Assembly Expert Committee held a meeting with representatives of the Royal Government to discuss six draft laws related to the payment guarantee of the Royal Government of the Kingdom of Cambodia to some companies to develop the electricity sector.
In the morning meeting on December 16, 2019 at the National Assembly, Dr. Cheam Yeap, Chairman of the Commission, stated that the six draft laws are divided into two blocks, the first is the electricity used by light. The solar project has four projects with a total capacity of 140 megawatts, and the other uses coal power that we bought from the Lao People's Democratic Republic, with two projects with a total capacity of 2,400 megawatts.
He added that the state has already passed many laws requested by the Royal Government regarding electricity, but today discussed the following six draft laws:
1. Draft Law on the Approval of the Payment Guarantee of the Royal Government of the Kingdom of Cambodia to Green Steven Neil Venture (Cambodia) Co., Ltd. for the Construction of a 20 MW Solar Power Plant in Svay Rieng Province.
2. Draft Law on the Approval of the Payment Guarantee of the Royal Government of the Kingdom of Cambodia to Rice Power Supply Co., Ltd. for the Construction of a 30 MW Solar Power Plant in Banteay Meanchey Province.
3-Draft Law on the Approval of the Payment Guarantee of the Royal Government of the Kingdom of Cambodia to Rice Energy (Cambodia) Battambang Private Company for the Construction of a 60 MW Solar Power Station in Battambang Province.
4: Draft Law on the Approval of the Payment Guarantee of the Royal Government of the Kingdom of Cambodia to Snettek Infinite Co., Ltd. for the Construction Project of a 30 MW Solar Power Plant in Pursat Province.
5. Draft Law on the Approval of the Payment Guarantee of the Royal Government of the Kingdom of Cambodia to TSBP Seacon Power and Investment Company Limited of the Lao People's Democratic Republic.
6. Draft Law on the Approval of the Payment Guarantee of the Royal Government of the Kingdom of Cambodia to Sekong Semmal Power Plant Company Limited of the Lao People's Democratic Republic.
Mr. Suy Sem, Minister of Rice and Energy, said that the Royal Government of Cambodia has made efforts to supply electricity to our people to use enough water by 2020 or 2021 and continue to promote the development of the country in all fields. In particular, to ensure economic growth, ensure the livelihood of our people even more prosperous.
(Phnom Penh): Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, announced the completion of receiving funds from philanthropists for the construction of a hospital building and equipment at Calmette Hospital at 7 pm on December 16, 2019. Funds received from philanthropists and the state budget of 30 million, bringing the total budget for the construction and equipment of Calmette Hospital to more than 104 million US dollars.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen thanked the philanthropists who donated money to save lives by modernizing Calmette Hospital to become a modern and multi-specialized national referral hospital.
Please be reminded that on November 23, 2019, Samdech Techo Hun Sen decided to release the national budget of about 30 million US dollars for the construction of a hospital building at Calmette Hospital, which is under construction. The 12-storey hospital building is now about 17 percent complete. The hospital building is expected to cost about $ 39.7 million.
In addition to the $ 30 million national budget for the construction of the building, the Prime Minister also called on philanthropists to donate funds to equip new and old buildings. The purpose of Samdech Techo is to make this hospital a modern referral hospital of the Cambodian nation to save the lives of the people.
(Phnom Penh): Samdech Techo Hun Sen, the Prime Minister of Cambodia, said that he clearly understands the feelings of people with eye problems and that helping people with eye problems to regain their eyesight is a noble humanitarian work, according to the Dharma of the Buddha. Helping people to regain their sight is very rewarding.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen made the remarks while allowing Mr. Loeung Chunying, Vice Chairman of the National Committee of the Chinese People's Political Consultative Conference and Chairman of the Hong Kong Belt and Road Center, to pay a courtesy call on the President. Peace on the afternoon of December 16, 2019.
Mr. Loeung Chun Ying has traveled to Cambodia many times and in the last two years he has brought volunteer doctors to help Cambodians with eye problems in Kampong Cham province. Seeing that Cambodians have a lot of cataracts and many other eye problems, he decided to set up a center in Kampong Cham to help people with eye problems to heal.
Mr. Loeung Chun Ying informed the Prime Minister that the treatment of cataracts is very easy, safe and painless. He said that this treatment should not be afraid, should not worry, instead it is a job that doctors have done a lot and is almost 100 percent successful.
In this meeting, Mr. Loeung Chun Ying also informed Samdech Techo about the surgery to treat cataract in an old man. After the operation, his eyesight was restored and he was happy because he had been blind for seven years.
After opening an eye treatment center in Kampong Cham province, for the past 19 months, a team of 12 Chinese ophthalmologists have been stationed to treat eye diseases. Mr. Chun Yeung confirmed that his team's eye treatment mission was over and about 6,208 patients in Kampong Cham province underwent surgery and were completely cured.
Mr. Loeung Chun Ying said that after completing his mission in Kampong Cham, he will continue his mission to Prey Veng. He will bring new equipment and new surgeries to Prey Veng to help the people of Prey Veng.
Mr. Chun Ying emphasized his intention that the treatment of the cataracts of the Cambodian people to serve the humanitarian work as a kind heart to help the Cambodian people and promote the relationship between the Cambodian people and the Chinese people in accordance with the principles. China's one-way belt politics.
