(Kampot): Located in the southern part of the Kingdom of Cambodia, Kampot Province has become an attractive tourist destination with a favorable climate, a destination for tourists to relax in all seasons.
While tourism is booming, Kampot also has a wide range of accommodation and services, including hotels, bungalows and guesthouses, with a total of 265 rooms with 3,585 rooms. Properly arranged to meet the needs of national and international guests.
Currently, most tourist accommodation services in Kampot have been reaching out to their business ventures in the context of "clean and green" in addition to environmental protection, social responsibility and equitable distribution.
Accommodation service businesses in Kampot province have taken into account the aesthetics, order and hygiene, as well as exhibited a list of services, attention on service quality improvement and environmental hygiene. Inside and outside the special business premises have also strengthened hospitality for tourists.
In addition, all businesses also pay close attention to security, safety of accommodation, providing various benefits to employees and uniforms for all employees.
Watch the video showing the accommodation services in Kampot province as follows: Thailand: 15 years after the tsunami disaster, hundreds of victims still can not be identified
BANGKOK: Fifteen years after the Indian Ocean tsunami that killed more than 230,000 people, Thai authorities have yet to identify hundreds of victims. This was released by Reuters on Monday, December 16, 2019.
On December 26, 2004, a tsunami caused by a magnitude 9.1 earthquake killed more than 230,000 people, with waves up to 17.4 meters high hitting many countries. In the region, including Thailand. In Thailand, more than 5,000 people have died, while Thai and foreign experts from 30 countries have been able to identify more than 3,600 victims.
