Authorities continue to install main canal sewer restoration equipment as part of environmental and aesthetic improvement in Sen Sok district
(Phnom Penh): Mr. Mov Manit, Governor of Sen Sok District, on December 16, 2019, led the team to remove the machinery to restore the mud, solid waste from the canal to drain the sewage quickly, which is part of Protect the environment and local hygiene.
Arriving at the mouth of the canal where the machinery is moving, the governor of Sen Sok district told the people living near the canal that you must take care of the environment together, especially do not throw garbage into the sewer, do not pour soil Go to the mouth of the canal and do not throw garbage in the sewer, such as plastic bags, plastic, solid waste and so on.
Please note that the delivery of machinery to restore the drainage system is located at the end of Street 1003, Tumnup Village, Sangkat Phnom Penh Thmey, Khan Sen Sok, Phnom Penh.
District Governor Mov Manit confirmed that the rehabilitation of sewers and sewers in order to help release water from the village, which is congested, especially in the area of Tumnup and adjacent villages in Sangkat Phnom Penh Thmey, Khan Sen Sok, Phnom Penh. Phnom Penh and to release water from that area to the pumping station. He added that the work of rehabilitating the drainage canal will be done regularly without setting a date.
