Doctors from Siem Reap Provincial Health Department visit and treat people in Kralanh district for free
(Siem Reap): A team of volunteer doctors from the Siem Reap Provincial Health Department collaborated with a team of Chinese doctors from the Angkor Hospital for Children and the Union of Youth Federations of Cambodia (UYFC) on December 15. In 2019, free medical check-ups were provided to thousands of people in Snoul commune, Kralanh district, Siem Reap province.
Mr. Pin Prak, Deputy Governor of Siem Reap Province, emphasized that the activities of the volunteer doctors to check and treat the general public everywhere in Siem Reap is to help improve the well-being of local people and avoid Various diseases, in particular, help reduce the cost of medical services.
He added that the humanitarian team showed that the Royal Government of Cambodia cares about the health of the people. Although there are health centers and operational districts near people's homes. He also thanked the Chinese doctors and all the volunteer doctors who participated in humanitarian activities for the health of the people today.
