Kampong Cham Provincial Governor: 67% of people have access to toilets and 72% have access to clean water
Mr. Un Chanda's remarks were made this morning, December 16, 2019, to chair the first annual conference on outstanding leaders for sustainable water and sanitation in Kampong Cham province. The ceremony was held at UME University of Management and Economics, Kampong Cham Province.
Mr. Un Chanda continued that the sanitation sector is still 33% lacking and the water supply sector is still lacking 28%, so he urged the local authorities in the next 6 years to do so. From 2020 to 2025, let the backs of people's houses have toilets and 100% clean water.
At the same time, the provincial governor also urged the provincial Department of Rural Development to continue to promote the repair of pump wells and plan for the construction of water wells and toilets on a regular basis. The district and commune chiefs must include water and sanitation work in their annual plans from 2020.
Separately, for each commune chief, village chief must update water wells and toilets clearly every month and must cooperate regularly between the provincial administration, district, commune, specialized departments and partner organizations. In addition, district, commune and village authorities must regularly promote and monitor the construction of toilets and water wells in each village and must report to the Department of Rural Development every month.
Takhmao City Authority Posting Land Judgment Document for Citizens to Check and Verify Properly
(Kandal): Judgment documents of 3 villages in Prek Samrong 1, Prek Samrong 2 and Thmei 2 villages, with a total of 1,845 plots in Sangkat Takhmao, Takhmao City, Kandal Province, have been posted to the public. The land owner must check and verify properly on December 16, 2019.
Mr. Phim Madonna, Deputy Governor of Takhmao City, informed all landowners that the public posting of the judgment documents at this time reflects the high attention of the Royal Government under the wise leadership. Dr. Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, until the issuance of legal land titles to the people to improve living standards, welfare and poverty reduction, as well as contribute to the strengthening of justice and social stability.
(Preah Vihear): A dilapidated two-room primary school in a remote area in the village of Antil, Yeang commune, Choam Ksan district, Preah Vihear province received attention and support from Mr. Chea Kimseng, Governor of Choam Ksan District, Preah Vihear Province, after leading a team to inspect on December 15, 2019.
Mr. Chea Kimseng said that during his visit to the above primary school, he saw that the school building that the students are studying today is a kind of auditorium with two rooms made of corrugated iron sheets and a corrugated iron roof. There were also cracks, and the walls were old and in some places crumbling.
At the same time, the governor of Choam Ksan district also instructed the school leaders and the community, who are the guardians of the students, to renovate the old auditorium building to make it easier for students to study.
He donated 2 million Riels and 300 new galvanized sheets for the roof of the old building. Due to the increase in the number of students, Mr. Chea Kimseng announced the construction of a new building, which is 7 meters wide and 24 meters long. It is planned to spend about 20 million riels.
