Senior Minister Ly Thuch told the authorities to be very careful, forbid the people from taking the seeds for processing and to confiscate them immediately
(Ratanakkiri): Senior Minister Ly Thuch, First Deputy Chief of the Mine Authority, on December 16, 2019, requested the Armed Forces and authorities at all levels to pay close attention to prohibiting people from processing ammunition. Others will be confiscated immediately.
The proposal was made on the occasion of Senior Minister Ly Thuch presiding over the installation of an educational awareness banner in Yatung commune, O'Yadao district, Ratanakkiri province. The ceremony was attended by provincial authorities, relevant departments, competent forces, MAG, NPA, about 400 people and students this morning, December 16, 2019.
On that occasion, on behalf of Samdech Techo Prime Minister and Chairman of the Mine Authority, Senior Minister Ly Thuch asked the people, students to be very careful of the bullets, it can cause us to fall, cripple, injury and death at any time.
In addition, Senior Minister Ly Thuch also advised not to use the bullets to process them when they see them to report to the village chief, commune, district or demining operator nearby on the billboard already have a phone number to Take to crush.
At the same time, Senior Minister Ly Thuch asked the Armed Forces and authorities at all levels to take great care to prohibit people from taking ammunition to be processed into other tools and to be confiscated immediately.
The Senior Minister added that Samdech Techo Prime Minister always pays close attention to the well-being of the people and students. We are all victims of war, we are not miners and explosive remnants of war. Samdech Techo Prime Minister is always shocked when he receives information that there are casualties from time to time.
On behalf of the Royal Government of Cambodia, Senior Minister Ly Thuch thanked UNICEF for joining the Royal Government of Cambodia in disseminating awareness of landmines and explosive remnants of war and contributing to the reduction of landmine and mine casualties.
The Senior Minister requested that UNICEF continue to assist the Mine Action Authority in disseminating this awareness to all mine-affected areas. This is the first time that Ratanakkiri province has installed such educational billboards, and the Mine Authority will continue to install them in Battambang province, and is ready to install them in all areas facing landmines and explosive remnants of war throughout the country.
Authorities set December 17 to resolve land disputes for 38 families in Tuol Pong village, Por Sen Chey district, after the owner of a company split a plot of land to prevent them from using it.
(Phnom Penh): 38 families who bought a plot of land to build a house for many years were upset with the company that split the plot and filed a complaint to the Por Sen Chey District Court to seek justice. It is alleged that the company split the lot and left the road for them to enter and exit the house properly, but has now banned the use of that road.
Not only that, when buying the land, the company has already transferred the ownership of the land in the commune to them, but now they need to exchange, but the company forbids them to sell, and if they sell, they have to pay the company $ 300 to $ 500. Sold and alleged that all 38 families borrowed land from the company to build houses and even cut off water for some of them to use.
After receiving the complaints from the people on the morning of December 16, 2019, Mr. Pang Lida, Deputy Governor of Por Senchey District, together with Mr. Kang Vong, Chief of Sangkat 1, inspected the actual situation on the disputed site in Toul Pong Village, Sangkat. Chom Chao I. However, the authorities have not resolved the issue yet, as Mr. Pang Lida said that he will gather the people to meet with the company owner on December 17, 2019 at the Por Sen Chey district hall.
