(Kampot): Major General Mao Chanthurith, Kampot Provincial Police Commissioner, this morning, December 16, 2019, continued to chair the meeting to review the security and safety plan during the 8th round of the Sea Festival in Kampot City. Held for 3 days from December 20 to 22, 2019.
The General Commissioner also instructed the force to strengthen the security of the runways, hotels, guesthouses where the delegation was staying and to protect the safety of the roads and to maintain good traffic order to facilitate the travel of the delegation and guests. Tourists.
In addition, Major General Mao Chanthurith reminded the force to increase good cooperation with the relevant authorities by using all essential measures and using all available means to maintain security, safety and public order.
Forces at all levels must ensure adequate force in operations by promoting a sense of responsibility, respect and strict compliance with orders while on duty. At the same time, there must be a proper uniform, appropriate and polite attitude.
At the graduation ceremony for medical students after their successful graduation, Samdech Techo Hun Sen expressed the expectation that the Armed Forces and officials of other ministries and institutions will not be jealous of doctors and teachers because they all have children. Learn and also have sick relatives need to seek medical treatment.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen said, "Now, please confirm that there are only two divisions, the highest is the medical framework and the teaching framework is the same, more soldiers, more police, more than any other framework." "But I hope that soldiers, police and other civil servants will not be jealous of doctors and teachers because everyone needs a doctor to treat their children."
