Syrian president accuses US of stealing oil from Syria to sell to Turkey
Assad has said the United States sells oil from the occupied territories in Syria to Turkey, and even US President Donald Trump has stated that he has decided to withdraw troops from northern Syria. He will maintain a military presence in Syria to protect the oil fields, as they are not under US ownership.
In late October 2019, the Russian military released a detailed report on US oil smuggling activities in Syria, based on satellite data. According to the report, the Department of Defense and the US Central Intelligence Agency (CIA) have agreed to participate in oil sales activities with Kurdish and US oil companies, resulting in more than 30 monthly profits. Million dollars.
In 2011, Syria's oil production capacity was 375,000 barrels per day, but it has declined rapidly since the outbreak of civil war. Later, the situation worsened when ISIS terrorists took over part of Syria's oil-rich eastern region and used the proceeds from oil sales to serve their campaign.
