General Department of Taxation issues guidelines on the use of exchange rates for taxpayers under the self-declaration regime
(Phnom Penh): The General Department of Taxation has issued a new guideline on the use of exchange rates for taxpayers under the self-declaration regime.
According to the guidelines received by Fresh News on December 15, the guidelines are intended to provide more convenience and timeliness, as well as to ensure a clearer billing verification mechanism as well as facilitate Implement the online application for refund and use of value-added tax credit more effectively from January 2020 onwards.
The instructions of the General Department of Taxation are as follows:
1. Daily official exchange rate: Taxpayers must use the official daily exchange rate issued by the National Bank of Cambodia to highlight the riel currency on the total value of the invoice. In case of holiday or before the time when the National Bank of Cambodia has not yet issued the official exchange rate, the taxpayer must use the official exchange rate of the National Bank of Cambodia issued one day before the holiday.
2. Official exchange rate for payroll tax: Taxpayers must use the official exchange rate issued by the National Bank of Cambodia on the 15th day of each month to calculate the payroll tax. In case of the 15th day of each month on a holiday when the National Bank of Cambodia does not issue the official exchange rate, the taxpayer shall use the official exchange rate of the National Bank of Cambodia issued one day before the holiday.
3. Official Monthly Exchange Rate: Stakeholders must use the official exchange rate issued by the National Bank of Cambodia on the last day of each month to calculate the monthly tax payable.
4. Annual official exchange rate: Stakeholders must use the official exchange rate issued by the National Bank of Cambodia on the last day of December of each year to calculate the annual interest rate.
