Key Remarks by Samdech Techo Hun Sen on the Occasion of the Opening Ceremony of Cambodia Products and Import-Export of Cambodia
(Phnom Penh): On Sunday afternoon, December 15, 2019, Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, presided over the opening of an exhibition of Cambodian products and Cambodian exports and imports. The opening ceremony took place at the Koh Pich Convention and Exhibition Center.
The 14th Cambodia International Export and Import Fair of Cambodian Products 2019 was organized with the active support and participation of regional friendly countries such as China, Japan, Indonesia, Thailand, Malaysia, Myanmar, Vietnam and Laos. The 25 Departments of Commerce, Capital-Provinces, the Cambodian Chamber of Commerce, the Rice Federation, business associations, local companies and foreign companies operating in Cambodia.
The following are the main contents of Samdech Techo Hun Sen:
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen is pleased to attend the inauguration ceremony of the 14th Cambodian Products and Import Export Fair 2019 at the international level, which is now held with great pomp and circumstance.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen would like to express his appreciation and appreciation for the efforts of the leaders and officials at all levels of the Ministry of Commerce who have actively participated in organizing the successful exhibition of Cambodian products and Cambodian exports and imports. Continuing in the past and now.
* The Prime Minister said that the continuous inflow of foreign investment into Cambodia has given Cambodia access to financial resources, technology, skills, knowledge of using modern technology, entrepreneurial experience, creating new jobs for the people, expanding domestic production. Comprehensively with the quality and availability of economic resources available to build capacity for transparent development and investment, both now and in the future.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen says that the trade sector has made a significant contribution to providing employment to the people of Cambodia with the promotion of national economic growth through the export of goods and services to the markets of member countries of the Trade Organization. 147 countries will import goods and services to meet the economic needs of 135 countries, increasing the international trade volume to more than 30 billion dollars in 2018.
* Samdech Techo Prime Minister said that at the same time, Cambodia has achieved an average annual economic growth of around 7.7% over the last two decades, as well as achieving a historic milestone, passing the status of a country that Low-income countries officially became low-middle-income countries in 2015 with continued efforts to become high-middle-income countries by 2030 and high-income countries by 2050.
* Meanwhile, the government has been preparing new investment laws and laws on special economic zones in order to establish an open, transparent, predictable, favorable and efficient legal framework for investment, modernization and industrial production. District with the strengthening of connectivity into the regional and global supply chain through the growth of capital inflows and the transfer of technology, knowledge and know-how.
* Samdech Techo hopes that through today's international exhibition event, businessmen, entrepreneurs, investors, businessmen, both domestic and foreign, will better understand the investment potential in Cambodia and will seize the opportunity to make full use of the priority concessions provided by the Royal Government for its successful investment and business, both now and in the future.
Mr. HUN Manet: Khmer youth represent the Khmer nation, so be able to show your national identity to the world
(Phnom Penh): Lt. Gen. Hun Manet, Deputy Commander of the Royal Cambodian Armed Forces and Commander of the Army, stated that in foreign lands, every Cambodian youth represents the whole Cambodian nation, so it is necessary to strive for cultural activities in order to Show the national identity to the world and continue to strive to become a human resource and unite to help build a nation for future generations.
Mr. Hun Manet made this statement during a meeting with Cambodian students studying in Australia and New Zealand on December 13, 2019.
Mr. HUN Manet and the above Khmer students considered this happy event as an annual meeting organized in order to connect more closely, share experiences and help each other between students and alumni. Study in Australia and New Zealand, as well as students who are preparing to continue their studies there.
Mr. Hun Manet said that studying abroad away from home and family is always a lot of challenges, but it is important for Cambodian students to overcome the goal of absorbing knowledge to increase capacity, increase potential and increase their success, family and Of the nation.
He urged students to keep this goal in mind, not to give up, because having the right knowledge and skills is the basis for our success, especially in the context of a competitive free market economy.
In addition, Cambodian students also need to pay attention to the meticulous attention to the performance of small tasks well before being able to achieve large tasks, and also to constantly learn from the non-school environment to understand how to live. Manage the way of working and the mindset of foreign friends, complementing what you learn in school and which will bring new ideas and new approaches to a more successful life.
