Ministry of Mines Calls on Petroleum and Gas Station Owners Who Do Not Have Technical Safety Permits to Apply Now
(Phnom Penh): The Ministry of Mines and Energy has appealed to all petrol and gas station owners who have not yet sought permission from the Ministry to apply for a permit to ensure the safety and control of the oil sector. Effective. This was confirmed by Mr. Sok Khavan, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Mines and Energy, which was received by Fresh News on December 16, 2019.
The Secretary of State said that the Ministry of Mines, which is the staff of the Royal Government, has been building and issuing a number of legal documents and technical standards to ensure the safety and effective management of the oil sector. The laws and regulations related to this work are as follows:
* Law on the Management of Petroleum and Petroleum Products * Circular on Safety for the Preparation of Petroleum and Gas Stations * Prakas on the Procedures for the Management of Safety Techniques for Establishment of Petroleum and Gas Stations as a Legal Basis for Management and as a Basic Technical Safety for Establish a new station and renovate the old station to make it safer in order to reduce the risk of fire.
He said that the Ministry of Mines and Energy, through the inspection and inspection activities in the oil sector will monitor compliance with laws, regulations and relevant technical regulations in force. Legal measures to prevent illegal activities and crimes in the oil sector will be strictly enforced by inspectors who are qualified as judicial police.
