MOSCOW (Reuters) - The administration of US President Donald Trump will announce the withdrawal of 4,000 US troops from Afghanistan next week as peace talks between the United States and the Taliban resume. This is according to the release by CNN on Sunday, December 15, 2019.
CNN made the report based on a source from a senior US official on condition of anonymity. The official added that after the withdrawal of 4,000 troops, between 8,000 and 9,000 US troops will continue to be stationed in Afghanistan, and that the withdrawal could take place in stages. For months.
The White House has not yet commented on the CNN report, but Donald Trump has repeatedly stated that he intends to withdraw thousands of US troops from Afghanistan. Between 12,000 and 13,000 people are standing to help the Kabul government fight Taliban militants in the war, which has been raging for more than 18 years.
