Ex-military officer dies of stroke near Wat Beng, Pailin province
The military officer of the 5th Army Division said that the military officer who was found dead near the pagoda and posted on social media that he had no relatives, he was not without relatives. He had just been disbanded about three months ago. This military officer named Yot Kay, formerly served in the 523rd Battalion under the 52nd Infantry Brigade, 5th Army Division.
The same source confirmed that the military officer lives in Battambang province, but these days he came to stay at his son's house in Pailin province to receive medical treatment. Until this morning, his son took him on a motorbike to go to the hospital for a check-up. When he arrived near Wat Beng, the motorbike ran out of gas. Immediately, his son put the military officer above to sit and wait near the pagoda to drive his motorcycle to the store.
According to the source, when his son drove away on a motorcycle, he suddenly died near the pagoda, much to the surprise of the people and the authorities, and posted and shared online. Society says a military officer was found dead near a pagoda without relatives and his body was taken to Wat Beng.
However, until now, the 523rd Battalion (former military officer above) is preparing to bury the body of military officer Yot Kay according to tradition in Wat Beng. Chinese kidnapping case in Kandal province found that victims and accomplices conspired to defraud family in China
(Kandal): A case of kidnapping of Chinese and Chinese nationals in Koh Thom district, Kandal province, where the police cracked down on one victim and three perpetrators on December 11, 2019, after completing the investigation and A careful investigation found that the victim and the perpetrator were friends and created a kidnapping story to defraud the family in China.
In the report of Kandal Provincial Police, which was received by Fresh News on the morning of December 15, 2019, it was claimed that after completing the 48-hour preliminary investigation, the authorities can conclude that:
* First: It is an arrangement to establish the facts of the kidnapping crime * Second: The victim and the suspect conspired to create this case to take money from their parents in China to spend. Have fun together * Third: spend all the money, no money to sleep in a guesthouse, sleep on the car until the police suspect to arrest.
Now, after completing the actual criminal procedure of the investigation, with the coordination of the Kandal Provincial Prosecutor and Major General Eav Chamroeun, Kandal Provincial Police Commissioner, the authorities sent the four Chinese nationals to the General Department of Immigration to continue. Proceed with the procedure on the evening of December 14, 2019.
