PRASAC Inaugurates 4 Library Buildings on the Same Day in Kampong Thom Province
(Kampong Thom): In order to continue to contribute to the promotion of students' reading culture and human resource development in Cambodia, four standard library buildings built and equipped with books and facilities using the funds of PRASAC MFI have been inaugurated. Officially, on the afternoon of December 13, 2019, presided over by Mr. Chea Chanto, Governor-General of the National Bank of Cambodia.
The inauguration ceremony took place on the campus of Kampong Thmor High School in Santuk District, Kampong Thom Province to symbolize the official opening of the four library buildings located at different school locations, including the library at Kampong Thmor High School, Hun Sen Sandan High School, Hun Sen Rong Roeung High School and Chea Sim Pralay High School are located in Kampong Thom province with a lot of library facilities and about 12,000 books.
Mr. Khim Sarin, Representative of the Ministry of Education, Youth and Sports, expressed his deep appreciation and gratitude to PRASAC for building 41 library buildings throughout the country to contribute to the promotion of education and human resources in Cambodia.
PRASAC has responded to the Ministry's need for separate standard library buildings in schools equipped with adequate textbooks and facilities, which in the past required schools to use part of their classrooms or office buildings as existing libraries. The narrow nature is not conducive to reading.
Mr. Prem Ratha, Deputy Governor of Kampong Thom Provincial Board of Governors, also thanked PRASAC for providing up to 7 library buildings to Kampong Thom province.
He hopes that all students in these schools will work hard to improve their skills and knowledge through reading in the library as well as borrowing books to read at home, and he called on students to take care. Keep this library good and last forever.
Speaking at the event, Mr. Chea Chanto, Governor-General of the National Bank of Cambodia, expressed his deep gratitude to PRASAC for providing these library buildings, which are an important part of education because national development is based on Human resource development is essential.
