President of the Association of Travel Agents of Cambodia condemns a foreigner who filmed a small dirty place scaring tourists from coming to Cambodia
(Phnom Penh): After a foreign man came to visit Cambodia and recorded a few dirty videos posted to scare tourists not to visit Cambodia, on December 15, 2019, Ms. Chhay Sivlin, President of the Association The Cambodian travel agency strongly condemned the foreigner and considered that the foreigner's actions because he could not seek sexual services did not do so.
At the same time, Ms. Siv Lin asked the authorities to find the foreigner to apologize to the Cambodian people all over the country and warned to send photos of the person to ASEAN countries not to allow the foreigner to enter their country.
At the same time, the president of the association stressed, "I ask the competent authorities to find the identity of this person to apologize to Cambodians across the country. "I will send this personal image to the countries in ASEAN so that they are careful in allowing them to enter their respective countries."
Ms. Chhay Sivlin said that there are countless tourist sites in Cambodia, but this foreigner did not mention even one place.
At the same time, Mr. Heng Ratana, Director General of the Cambodian Mine Action Center (CMAC), considered the actions of the foreigner as a terrorist who intends to destroy the Cambodian economy by scaring foreign tourists not to come to visit.
Minister encourages business owners to promote national tourism and warns businesses that destroy national tourism destinations
(Phnom Penh): The Minister of Tourism, Mr. Thong Khon, encouraged all business owners who are willing to contribute to the promotion of tourism and national tourism destinations, but must take decisive action against businesses that deceive visitors for profit for a while. And affect tourism destinations in Cambodia.
Such encouragement and warning by Minister Thong Khon was made during the opening ceremony of Chan Kim Ty Jewelry Shop along Mao Tse Toung Blvd (west of Bokor traffic light) on December 15, 2019.
On the occasion of the opening of the above jewelry shop, Minister Thong Khon expressed his optimism about Chan Kim Ty Jewelry Shop, which can serve all the needs of national and international guests and also participate in promoting national tourism.
He said that about 25% of the total tourists in the world, as well as in Cambodia, always like to buy jewelry, souvenirs and other art sculptures, he urged businesses operating in this area to improve the quality of quality assurance services. Special hospitality must not deceive guests.
He said that when visiting Cambodia, especially in the destination Siem Reap-Angkor, European tourists like to buy souvenirs and sculptures of Cambodia, while Asian tourists, especially Chinese tourists like to buy jewelry such as gold, diamonds, precious stones and jewelry. Other. This is a potential that Cambodia must meet the needs of those tourists and must ensure the quality of its products, not to deceive customers or cut prices beyond the actual price.
He added that in addition to providing a variety of needs to customers and customers, business owners must also consider the staff to provide warmth, good service, safety and hospitality to guests, because this point also contributes to the promotion of Cambodia's good reputation to Foreign visitors and other customers of the store as well, in line with the campaign "Cambodia: Kingdom of Wonder: Warmth."
At the same time, Minister Thong Khon also mentioned the strict implementation of the law on tourism businesses that sell products or goods of poor quality or counterfeit to customers. The minister warned that "the new law that has just been implemented could lead to the closure of the entire business."
Ms. Chan Kimty, the founder and owner of this jewelry store, said that she had a history as a blacksmith, and the opening of this jewelry business is to promote the national prestige in the field of jewelry as well as to promote national tourism. Well.
She is committed to ensuring the quality of jewelry, providing a variety of services, safety and hospitality to guests and customers, especially this new jewelry store also sells jewelry designed in the traditional Khmer art. Also. Mr. Thong Khon and the people of Baray district applauded for the restoration of a canal with a length of more than 12,000 meters
(Kampong Thom): Mr. Thong Khon, Minister of Tourism and Chairman of the Central Working Group for Baray and Taing Kork Districts, as well as hundreds of people in Baray District, expressed their great joy for the restoration and expansion of Ta Suong Canal. Larger, deeper and holds more water.
The total length of the canal to be rehabilitated is 12,500 meters, including the rehabilitation of 4,850 meters of main canal with red gravel dam on both sides and the restoration of 7,650 meters of sub-canal with red gravel dam on both sides. .
The groundbreaking ceremony for the canal was held on the morning of December 14, 2019 in the presence of Minister Thong Khon and was attended by Mr. Yin Nguon Kolenin, Undersecretary of State, Ministry of Water Resources and Meteorology, Kampong Thom Provincial Administrative Representative and government officials. And hundreds of other Baray residents.
Mr. Yin Nguon Kolinin urged the cooperation of the people living along the canal as well as the people who benefit from this sub-project and to be careful about safety when traveling through the construction site and ask for forgiveness for Distractions.
Minister Thong Khon expressed optimism that the canal system would provide more irrigation to the people living along the canal with rice and other crops. Facilitate the transportation and transportation of agricultural products by building roads on both sides of the canal, as well as increase the yield of rice, fish and improve the livelihood of the people along the canal.
The head of the popular local relief team suggested that once the project is completed and operational, the three district and commune administrations should work together to properly manage and distribute water. Clear turn to ensure adequate water supply and distribution to local people's rice crops.
He continued to call on the people to work together to protect and use this new achievement for a long time, because it comes from the efforts of the Royal Government led by Samdech Techo Hun Sen, who always thinks about life and Agricultural activities of farmers.
It was observed that the civil servants, the police and the people in Baray district expressed their great joy for the restoration of the Ta Suong canal, which is more than 12,000 meters long, and showed closeness with Minister Thong Khon during the visit. Inspect Ta Suong canal after the groundbreaking ceremony is completed.
