Recently, the drought has affected rice in five communes, equivalent to 360 hectares, including 150 hectares in Roka commune, 100 hectares in Rolling Ken commune, 50 hectares in Thmey commune, 50 hectares in Trea commune and 10 hectares in Trapeang Veng commune.
