(Phnom Penh): Prof. Yit Sunnara, Undersecretary of State of the Ministry of Health and President of the Cambodian Pediatric Association, urged pediatricians from all provincial and municipal hospitals to pay close attention to adhering to Medical professional ethics and to bring new knowledge to participate in the provision of pediatric services more effectively, quality and safety with real knowledge and skills.
This morning, December 14, 2019, Prof. Yit Sunnara made this statement on the occasion that he and Prof. Thea Kruy, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Health, presided over the 22nd Cambodian Pediatric Medicine Day, which was organized in Cambodia. Up at the Phnom Penh Hotel and with the participation of more than 300 professors, doctors, doctors who are members of the Cambodian Medical Association.
Prof. Yit Sinnara urged all conference members, pediatricians from hospitals from the provinces and cities, to adhere to adhere to medical professional ethics and to bring new knowledge. Disseminate to other cooperatives to improve the provision of health services to the people in accordance with the policy of the Royal Government.
Please note that the Cambodian Pediatric Association regularly celebrates this Pediatric Medicine Day once a year in order to provide a forum for pediatricians across the country to share and exchange experiences with each other, as well as Help provide new knowledge related to these pediatric diseases so that all participants can extract the importance for use in the care and treatment of Cambodian children as well.
Minister: In 2020, the Ministry of Commerce will promote the implementation of e-commerce.
(Phnom Penh): Mr. Pan Sosak, Minister of Commerce, said that in 2020, the Ministry of Commerce has a number of priority tasks to be implemented, especially the Ministry will promote e-commerce to keep up. Context of the Industrial Revolution 4.0.
This statement was made by Minister Pan Sosak at the opening ceremony of the 14th Cambodia Products and Import-Export Fair on December 15, 2019 at the Koh Pich Convention and Exhibition Center, which was presided over by Samdech Techo Hun. Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia.
The Minister said that in the past, the Ministry of Commerce has set up an automated system for business registration, trademark and trademark registration, application for Certificate of Origin (C / O) and delegated authority to sub-national levels. Take public services closer and closer to the people.
The next step is to ensure the security and ownership of the data and the system, the Ministry of Commerce will transfer the data to the Ministry's own system to avoid data loss and unauthorized interference into the system.
Mr. Pan Sosak stated that in 2020, the Ministry of Commerce will also have some priority tasks to be implemented, including:
1. Promote the implementation of e-commerce through the organization of agricultural market price information programs in the provinces under the technology nursery, which allows farmers to receive up-to-date information on agricultural prices and to assist in business communication between farmers. And merchants and the creation of business and business online marketing aimed at promoting cross-border e-commerce.
2. Establish production centers for products such as Snon Chhnang in Kampong Chhnang, stone carving in Pursat and silk in Siem Reap, with a full range of production lines that not only help create jobs and income for local people, but also attract tourists and lift. Promote Khmer culture and traditions.
3. Establish more cultural and business centers in China and invite Chinese companies to visit Cambodia to discuss trade and network with potential Cambodian companies for e-commerce and online trading. Traditional.
The Minister of Commerce added that this trade fair is an annual international trade event of Cambodia, designed to promote trade activities, create market opportunities, show the business environment and better investment potential, and show Investment and business protection policy in Cambodia. Through this trade event, consumers will get to know and support local goods as well as quality imported goods.
Along with the exhibition of export-import goods and rich potential goods from provinces across the country, this important trade event also organizes a number of accompanying events such as trade meetings, business and investment forums, seminars and events. Sign business and investment projects to attract exhibition visitors and provide opportunities for businesses and investors to connect with Cambodia.
