This morning, the Chairman of the delegation informed that the purpose of the visit to Cambodia now and especially to meet the Minister now:
First: Participate in the inauguration of a new dormitory building at Ta Saang Agricultural Training and Extension Center, Svay Rieng Province. Second: Want to learn more about Cambodia's agricultural potential. Third: Learn about the needs that the Korean side can help to develop this sector. More in the future through cooperation between the two sides.
KIM reiterated to the Minister that the post-Korean War crisis is over and that the Korean people and government have worked hard to build and develop the country until now, and especially in the agricultural sector, which has reached the level of smart agriculture. Use modern technology on the farm from A to Z.
Mr. KIM continued that the situation of construction and development of Cambodia is similar to Korea and this is the reason why the Korean side wants to share everything that is a valuable experience for the development of the country and especially Cambodian agricultural sector.
The Minister welcomed and supported the willingness to establish cooperation between the two sides in the field of agriculture and human resource training, as it coincided with the Ministry of Agriculture and Human Resources development policy in line with the Rectangular Strategy. The fourth phase of the Royal Government.
The policy aims to focus on research, training and dissemination of modern agricultural technologies to producers to ensure quantity, quality, value added, competitive processing and export markets, and in particular training human resources. They apply their knowledge of intelligent agricultural technology to the development of their farms, crops and animals.
In conclusion, Minister Veng Sakhon gave hope and confidence to the delegation that the Ministry will look forward to providing full cooperation in all forms to make the cooperation between the two sides a success.
