Immediately after the murder, Kratie Provincial Police Commissioner Major General Lon Sophat ordered a criminal and district police force to launch an immediate search for the perpetrators. After careful questioning and research this afternoon, the assailant was arrested by the police.
Chan Sophalla, Prek Prosop District Police Inspector, told Fresh News that after a thorough investigation, we identified the suspect, 32-year-old Yang Nak, at O'Angkunh point, Rokar Thom village, Chroy Banteay commune, but he escaped. At 15:30, our special forces made an arrest at O'Angkunh point, Rokar Thom village, Chroy Banteay commune, and confiscated the following items: a pair of the victim's earrings and 560,000 riels.
According to the Prek Prosop District Police Inspector, the body of the victim, 39-year-old Chhum Nai Sim, was found yesterday afternoon. The victim was married and had a child living in the commune.
The inspector continued that on December 12, 2019, a 6-year-old girl named Thai Vary went to tell the name of Chhean Lim Hour, 47 years old, that is, her father, Bun Pheng, to carry firewood while his mother was carrying it. The cow went to the back of the house but could not find it. The bag at the back of the house is about 150 meters.
He added that the autopsy found bruises and hard objects with bruises on both jaws, broken chin, broken mouth, broken upper teeth, three broken left earlobes and bruises on the chest. After an examination, the body was handed over to the relatives for a traditional ceremony.
