The Senate and stakeholders open a forum to orient young women to leadership for about 200 female students from Pursat High School
(Pursat): The Senate and stakeholders held a forum to orient young women towards leadership to about 200 female students from Pursat High School at the Bun Rany Hun Sen Development Center in Pursat.
The forum was held on December 12, 2019 in the presence of Ms. Mean Sam An, Permanent Member of the Senate and Vice Chairman of the Central Committee of the Cambodian Women's Association for Peace and Development, Ms. Hun Chanthy Mao Thunin, Honorary President of the Cambodian Women's Association Branch. Peace and Development, Ms. Em Ponna, Member of the National Assembly and Executive Member of the Cambodian Women's Association, and Ms. Chan Pheary, President of Revlon Company in Cambodia.
Twelfth grade students of Pursat High School listened to the advice, ideas, knowledge and good experiences from the speakers, as well as questions, answers and commitment.
Ms. Mean Sam An said that the forum is to find more girls involved in politics with the support of aunts and uncles. Aunts and uncles and teachers want to cultivate the mind of all of you must have a real dream, want to be a leader like men, so requires you to have the courage to dare to overcome all difficulties to do Let your dreams come true.
She suggested that the children learn from and follow the example of older women politicians about their personal political life experiences over the years. She said that women are now highly regarded by the Royal Government of Cambodia, led by Samdech Techo Hun Sen, to improve the status of women in politics.
Ms. Mean Sam An continued that many women have become leaders at all levels from the national level to the grassroots level, and from year to year the number of women in leadership is increasing in line with the strategy. The Royal Government's rectangle considers women to be the backbone of the national economy. Although the number of women in leadership positions has increased, that number has not yet met our needs and needs.
He added that after gaining good knowledge, ideas and experiences, please use them to think carefully to improve and increase their new ideas and spread to friends to contribute to improving the status of women in politics. More comprehensive.
