This afternoon, the Supreme Court held a swearing-in ceremony for 44 foreigners.
(Phnom Penh): 44 foreigners were allowed to enter the place of oath to take the oath of allegiance as Cambodian citizens. The swearing-in ceremony took place after the 44 foreigners had properly met the qualifications set by Cambodian law.
The swearing-in ceremony took place on the afternoon of December 13, 2019 in the Supreme Court of the Kingdom of Cambodia. The Royal Decree is prepared to be sworn in before the Supreme Court to fulfill the legal status of a Cambodian citizen in accordance with the principles and procedures set by the Nationality Law.
The push came as Samdech Techo met with Vietnamese Deputy Prime Minister Choeung Hor Binh at the Peace Palace.
Mr. Eang Sophalleth, Assistant to Samdech Techo Hun Sen, told reporters after the meeting that during the meeting, Mr. Choeung Hor Binh paid a courtesy call on the Head of State and Prime Minister of Vietnam to Samdech Techo and invited Samdech Techo to visit. In Vietnam as well.
He also briefed Samdech Techo on the progress made in Vietnam, saying that Vietnam is well developed, the 12 goals set by the Vietnamese government have been achieved and are being promoted. In line with UN development goals. Vietnam's economy is currently growing at about 7 percent and inflation is as low as 2 percent.
He also expressed satisfaction with the bilateral relations and cooperation between Cambodia and Vietnam in all fields, especially in the field of defense, security, border order, economy as well as trade. In this regard, Choeung Hor Binh said that trade between Cambodia and Vietnam could reach the $ 5 billion limit by 2020.
The Deputy Prime Minister also praised the cooperation between the two countries in the international arena, saying that Vietnam will host the ASEAN Summit next year and will also become a non-permanent member of the organization. United Nations as well.
Mr. Choeung Her Binh asked Cambodia to support and cooperate to make the cooperation between the two countries grow more and more successful.
In response, Samdech Techo Hun Sen expressed his gratitude for the greetings of the Vietnamese Head of State and Prime Minister and for his invitation to visit Vietnam. Samdech Techo said he would visit Vietnam at an appropriate time.
He said that Vietnam's economic development is contributing to the region's economic stability. In this regard, the prince encouraged the promotion of cooperation, especially to facilitate trade on the border between the two peoples even better.
Regarding the trade volume between the two countries is set to reach 5 billion dollars in 2020, Samdech Techo said that in fact the trade volume between Cambodia and Vietnam may already be greater than 5 billion dollars because The trade volume is on the list, there are different figures, and we also have unregistered trade, such as rice exports to Vietnam, etc. There is no clear record.
He also congratulated Vietnam on chairing ASEAN next year and being a non-permanent member of the United Nations next year.
He said Cambodia would host the Asia-Europe Summit next year. In this regard, the two countries should cooperate to help each other make the meeting in Vietnam and Cambodia a success, and the cooperation between the two countries has grown even more.
