(Central): Mr. Heng Chanthuon, Undersecretary of State, Ministry of Mines and Energy, warned and told all mining companies to comply with legal standards, especially not to harm the people.
Heng Chanthuon made this warning on December 12, 2019, when he went to warn Ang Taing Lay, a dredging and sand dredging company, located in Prey Sleng village, Siem Reap commune, Kandal Steung district, province. Central.
The warning comes after residents complained that the company was affecting their daily lives.
Mr. Heng Chanthuon said, "The company must comply with the license, especially in the transport must comply with Article 03/10 of the law on mineral transport properly, such as not to overcrowd and pack properly. "And there must be no falls and runoff on the road that could endanger the passengers, and the road must be repaired and watered regularly so that the smoke does not affect the health of the people."
In addition, he also recommended to stop blocking water for farmers to use and stop draining water from washing sand into public canals, which leads to shallow land and farmers can not take that water to irrigate crops. The canal must be restored to the people. If the next time it is found that it is still affecting the people, there will be no exception, and if it is serious, the business license will be revoked.
It should be informed that recently, the Kandal Provincial Administration has reminded the Director of the Department of Mines and Energy to take responsibility for the problems that occur in Kandal province, but the impact is still there.
