(Phnom Penh): According to the instruction of the Governor of Phnom Penh, on the morning of December 13, 2019, the Phnom Penh Forestry Administration brought all kinds of seedlings to be planted in the National Children's Hospital to join Phnom Penh as a city. There is a special green color for the hospital premises to have a fresh environment to increase the good environment for patients to relax and breathe the fresh air of the trees.
The tree planting ceremony was also attended by Mr. Koam Seiha, Director of Phnom Penh Forestry Administration, and Mr. Nhep Angka Bos, Director of the National Children's Hospital, and the working group of the Cambodian People's Youth Organization in Washington, DC, USA, as well as Phnom Penh Forestry Administration staff. Of the National Children's Hospital as well.
Mr. Koam Seiha said that the planting of trees now for the main purpose to help preserve the environment around the hospital to be more green and beautiful, especially to reduce climate change on the planet and help get rid of Toxins in the hospital premises as well as in Phnom Penh.
At the same time, Mr. Koam Seiha also requested all people to plant trees and take care of the trees that have been planted to grow well so that our hospital grounds are green and beautiful, contribute to Phnom Penh as a green cover, provide shade and lift. The beauty of our city, too. So we must all work together to plant trees and take good care of them, just as we love our children, and to destroy them is to destroy ourselves.
"Trees are very important for human life, animals and all kinds of biodiversity, especially as wind barriers, flood barriers and bring rainfall to increase human livelihoods," he said. Therefore, all of us who are the beneficiaries of this tree should participate in planting, caring, protecting and loving the tree and the natural environment for the benefit of ourselves, all kinds of wildlife and biodiversity. Also mixed.
At the same time, Mr. Nheb Angkar Bos also called on doctors, civil servants and hospital staff to take care of watering and protect the trees planted now, because trees are very beneficial for the environment and humanity.
It should be noted that the National Children's Hospital is a public administration located along the Russian Federation Road in Sangkat Toek Laak 1, Khan Toul Kork, Phnom Penh.
