Mr. Sok Sokretya was appointed by the King as Personal Adviser to Samdech Techo
(Phnom Penh): The King of Cambodia, His Majesty King Norodom Sihamoni, has agreed to appoint Mr. Sok Sokretya as his personal adviser to the Prime Minister of Cambodia, Samdech Techo Hun Sen.
According to the Royal Decree obtained by Fresh News on December 12, 2019, the appointment of the King of Cambodia took place on November 9, 2019. Please note that Mr. Sok Sokretya is the son of Mr. Sok Isan, Senator and spokesman for the Cambodian People's Party.
Mr. Sok Sokretya is currently the Undersecretary of State at the Ministry of Tourism. Mr. Sokretya holds a Bachelor of Science in Political Science, a Master of Management, a Master of Political Economy and a Master of Communication Arts from Thailand. He also holds a PhD in Public Affairs from a US university. Daily Summary of National and International News on December 12, 2019
