Senior Minister Ly Thuch Chairs a Meeting of the Royal Government's Joint Technical Working Group with Mine Development Partners to Discuss Funding and Resources to Support Mine Action for a Mine-Free Cambodia by 2025
(Phnom Penh): Senior Minister Ly Thuch, First Deputy Chairman of the Mine Authority, representing the Prime Minister and Chairman of the Mine Authority, chaired a meeting of the Royal Government's Joint Technical Working Group on Mine Development Partners with the participation of representatives of development partners, relevant ministries and institutions. Ambassadors to Cambodia as well as national and international demining operators.
The Senior Minister said that the Royal Government of Cambodia under the leadership of Samdech Techo Hun Sen has worked hard to bring peace and prosperity to the Cambodian people. With this, the Senior Minister presented the results of the 4th review conference in Oslo, Norway last November to the meeting that Cambodia has approved the document to postpone demining until 2025.
On behalf of the Prime Minister of Cambodia, the Senior Minister thanked all the donors and development partners for providing technical and financial support to enable Cambodia to fulfill its life-saving demining obligation. Citizens will increase development.
On that occasion, representatives of donor countries and development partners praised Cambodia's achievements in the field of mines in the past and pledged to work with the Royal Government of Cambodia to achieve the goal of a landmine-free Cambodia by 2025 to save lives. People will build peace.
