A Deputy Commissioner of Kampong Thom Province complained to his superiors and asked the General Commissioner to send an inspection team to investigate, the Commissioner said that he would investigate and solve this case
(Kampong Thom): A Deputy Provincial Police Commissioner of Kampong Thom Province has filed a complaint with Samdech Krala Hom Sar Kheng, Deputy Prime Minister and Minister of Interior regarding irregularities in his work, especially requesting the removal of any police officers. Not its offspring.
Brigadier General Im Sokoeun, deputy police chief in charge of human resource planning, has been accused by subordinate police officers of disrupting the internal unity of Kampong Thom's national police force, which they do not want to work on.
At the same time, these police officers also insisted that General Santebandit Neth Savoeun, the National Police Commissioner General, help send an inspection team to investigate this irregularity so that the police force will not be discouraged from working.
According to the complaint, the police officer who was addicted to drugs was asked to be fired from the unit, but the deputy commissioner ran to the upper level to help keep the three police officers changed to apply the discipline to reduce the rank by one level. That inactive work.
But Major General Ouk Kosal claimed that he would look into the case.
The commissioner-general confirmed that he had not yet received the complaint officially, but if there was a complaint, he would resolve it fairly, that is, there would be no disunity in the unit.
Responding to this accusation, Brigadier General Im Sokoeun confirmed that he dared to be responsible before the law and the leadership and welcomed the inspection team to visit the work of the Kampong Thom Provincial Police.
The brigadier general also said that for appointing, changing or punishing any police officer, he, the deputy commissioner, has no decision, it is up to the superiors, so he completely rejects these allegations.
According to another source, Brigadier General Im Sokoeun also disobeyed the instructions and orders of the provincial commissioner, which led to difficulties in working in the commission.
