The statement stated that in accordance with EU procedures, the Royal Government of Cambodia is tasked with submitting to the European Commission on 12 December 2019 its final response to the EU Commission's findings and conclusions. Concerning the procedure for the temporary removal of the preferential tariff system provided to the Kingdom of Cambodia under the "All Weapons Exemption -EBA" program.
The Ministry of Foreign Affairs continued that the latest response is a comprehensive report on the actions and measures taken by the Royal Government in response to issues of concern to the European Commission, including respect for the right to freedom of expression. Participate in politics, land rights, freedom of expression and freedom of association.
It should be noted that the European Union sent its report to the Cambodian government on November 12, 2019 and left one month for the Cambodian side to respond. After Cambodia responds, the European Union will make a decision in February 2020 on whether to temporarily withdraw Cambodia's tariff preferences. The decision was made by a majority vote of the 27 members of the European Commission.
If the European Commission decides not to suspend the system, the procedure will be closed. On the other hand, if the European Commission decides to suspend the preferential treatment, it will not be able to take effect immediately because the European Commission's decision to follow the procedure of delegation of authority is effective. Only if there is no objection from the Parliament or the Council of Europe.
