Regarding the allegation that the authorities and land officials were chased by the company not to measure the border, the company representative also denied and waited to welcome when the officials went to redefine the land.
It should be noted that the authority and the representative of the company came out after a resident, Mr. Chim Phal, 53 years old, a resident of Tuol Pong village, Sangkat Choam Chao I, told that the company started to encroach on his land before the festival. Om Touk ago, when he went to complain to the intervention of the authorities of Po Sen Chey district to help, but the district authorities were not busy to stop, let the company pour land on his land at will.
However, after receiving the information of pouring soil to encroach on the canal and land of the above people, on the morning of December 11, 2019, the authorities of Khan Por Sen Chey and Sangkat Choam Chao I, with the participation of Khan Land Office officials under Led by Mr. Pang Lida, Deputy Governor went to measure the disputed land.
Minister of Agriculture urges students and professors of Prek Leap Agricultural School to study and research to keep pace with global developments in the context of the Fourth Industrial Revolution and Digitalization
(Phnom Penh): Mr. Veng Sakhon, Minister of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries, this morning, December 12, 2019, urged students and professors of Prek Leap Agricultural School to study and research to keep pace with global developments in the context of the Industrial Revolution. Fourth, and digitalization.
The Minister's push came as he presided over the graduation ceremony for undergraduate students of the Prek Leap National Institute of Agriculture. The ceremony was held at the Ministry of Agriculture.
The event was also attended by Mr. and Mrs. Ministry leaders, directors of institutes, professors, teachers, national and international guests and about 1,330 students.
Speaking at the ceremony, Minister Veng Sakhon emphasized that due to the peace, social and political stability, efforts have been made to accelerate the implementation of key programs and policies within the framework of the Royal Government's in-depth reforms in human resource development.
He added that the promotion of the agricultural sector, focusing on increasing productivity, diversification and trade so that Cambodia has the ability to develop this sector effectively, progress and prosperity as expected to ensure equitable economic growth and sustainable competition. International market.
The Minister of Agriculture added that according to the context of economic growth, population and market demand, both the quantity, quality and safety of agricultural products require human resources that are full of potential, knowledge, skills, experience and professional ethics.
And, of course, it can not happen by accident, as long as every student has to take the knowledge, skills and experience gained from this institute to develop and innovate themselves to become good individuals, good officials or valuable citizens. Give yourself, especially the society of the future. This is the additional confirmation of Minister Veng Sakhon.
In addition, Minister Veng Sakhon added that at the same time, the three agricultural higher education institutions must strive to strengthen and expand leadership, management, both administrative and technical and cooperation.
At the same time, Minister Veng Sakhon recommended some good tips to be the basis for the leadership of the Institute, professors and students to consider and implement consistently to get good results, which are as follows:
1: To strive to strengthen and expand the capacity and quality of research, technology and science, innovation, focus on modern technology, intelligence, sustainability and environment to contribute to the development of the agricultural sector. Efforts must be made to build laboratory capacity and enhance the capacity of scientific resources.
2: Efforts must be made to reform the education system, improve and develop curricula, teaching methods and teaching materials to be more appropriate and appropriate to respond to the policy of agricultural development in the fourth generation industrial age, the era of digital technology.
3. Must pay attention to improving the capacity and quality of education, research, administration, management, officials, professors and students, strengthen and expand national and international cooperation, agricultural communities, private sector development partners, universities.
4: You must strive to fulfill their duties better by applying the knowledge they have in their profession successfully and must adhere to the attitude of an employee or a good officer with discipline, dignity, diligence and Have good morals.
5. In order to keep up with global developments in the context of the Fourth Industrial Revolution and digitalization, you need to continue to learn and research to strengthen and expand your capabilities even better.
Cambodia tells the world that chemical, biological, radioactive and nuclear weapons are dangerous and seriously affect human health, environment and society as a whole
(Indonesia): Lt. Gen. Dr. Sao Sovanny, Deputy Secretary General of the General Secretariat of the National Authority for Chemical Weapons, said that chemical, biological, radioactive and nuclear weapons (CBRN) are dangerous and seriously affect the health of human life, the environment and society as a whole.
He said that if all the substances were illegally traded, distributed and manufactured by terrorists and perpetrators, it would be a risk of causing instability and insecurity for countries in Southeast Asia as well as the world. Also.
The meeting was attended by Major General Dr. Oeur Channa, Deputy Secretary General of the Secretariat for Chemical Weapons Authority in charge of International Affairs and Colonel Dr. I Ratana, Assistant Secretary General of the National Authority for Chemical Weapons in charge of CBRN.
Lt. Gen. Dr. Sao Sovanny continued, "The purpose of this project is to address the issue of safety and security, which is a hot topic, requiring countries in Southeast Asia and the world to implement UN Res 1540 national and international law, which Provisions of conventions and treaties for participation, protection, prevention, detection, preparedness and response.
The project will not only properly regulate risk (CBRN), but also address the ongoing CBRN issues in some countries around the world in order to enforce laws, respect national and international laws, conventions and treaties.
He said pandemics could be used as weapons to destroy health and kill people, such as Ebola, Anthrax and Sars, while natural disasters were a risk that could affect nuclear power plants or substances. Chemistry, etc. And it affects public health, human life, the environment and society as a whole, so it is necessary for each country to be vigilant and pay attention to preventive measures.
(Phnom Penh): Responding to concerns that the creation of a village for Vietnamese immigrants moving from the Tonle Sap to the mainland in Kampong Chhnang province could lead to the loss of land or possibly an independent living area of Vietnamese people, Mr. Phay Siphan Claimed that the area is still under the rule of Cambodian law, never lose land as a concern.
At a press conference to present the plan to relocate people including Vietnamese, Khmer and Khmer-Muslims from living on floating houses on the Tonle Sap River to live on an area of about 40 hectares in Kampong Chhnang province on the morning of December 12. This year 2019, Mr. Phay Siphan firmly stated that the relocation here will never be the day that Cambodia cuts off land to Vietnamese immigrants.
Government spokesman Phay Siphan said: "Concerns about national security that we have created villages for immigrants will not affect national security because they are governed by the Cambodian legal system and you are in control of Cambodia. Let the people feel relieved. ”
Mr. Phay Siphan further explained that when the authorities set up a place for immigrants to live, all immigrants must abide by Cambodian law, including land and nationality laws, and the authorities there are not Cambodians. Not an immigrant.
In addition, the spokesperson of the Royal Government also thanked the Cambodian people for paying attention and following up on this issue. He believes that after today's press conference, people will be more aware of what the Royal Government and the Kampong Chhnang Provincial Administration are continuously implementing the work of moving people living on floating houses to live on land.
It should be informed that the Kampong Chhnang provincial authorities have been preparing Khmer people, Khmer Muslims and Vietnamese immigrants, as well as other businesses, a total of 3,851 houses, equivalent to 4,563 families living on the Tonle Sap River as a type of floating house. Water in 9 communes / sangkats to live on land instead. Authorities have prepared about 40 hectares of land in Dambok Kak village, Svay Chrum commune, Rolea Bier district for these people to live.
In response to the reactions of some Cambodians, the Kampong Chhnang provincial authorities claimed that the relocation was aimed at conserving the Tonle Sap River, conserving the aquatic environment, preserving biodiversity and natural resources.
