Senior Minister Kun Kim will accept the homeless veterans' requests and concerns to be addressed in a timely manner
(Phnom Penh): General Kun Kim, Senior Minister and Secretary General of the Cambodian Veterans Association, announced in front of more than 600 veterans that, as Secretary General, he will take the request of homeless veterans to face livelihood problems. And concerns to find solutions to help them according to the actual situation as much as possible and in a timely manner.
This confirmation of Senior Minister Kun Kim's efforts was made this morning, December 11, 2019, on the occasion that the Senior Minister and the ASEAN Veterans Delegation distributed gifts from the ASEAN Veterans Federation to Cambodian Veterans. 600 people from Phnom Penh, Kandal and Kampong Speu at the win-win monument.
Senior Minister Kun Kim stated that in his five-year term, he will work to solve problems for all Cambodian veterans, especially veterans who lack land and have many children to give them land to grow crops to Livelihood. Veterans present today, on the other hand, all have ID cards to go for check-ups and medical treatment at hospitals for a fee.
Senior Minister Kun Kim continued that, looking at the shortcomings of the Veterans, the Cambodian Veterans Association has made efforts to mobilize member countries to bring humanitarian aid to distribute to the disabled veterans in the country. Cambodia.
In addition, Senior Minister Kun Kim stated that on the occasion of Cambodia hosting the meeting, member countries helped build houses for 16 Cambodian veterans, each worth more than $ 2,000, and provided Funds to buy food for distribution to Cambodian veterans as well.
Senior Minister Kun Kim added that in 2019, the Cambodian Veterans Association mobilized 900 houses from philanthropists, but now Cambodia needs 4,000 more houses to help homeless Cambodian veterans. Stay decent.
