Workers at a pig farm in Kampong Chhnang province are lucky to win 100 million Riel from Echitan green tea
(Kampong Chhnang): A worker working on a pig farm in Damnak Key village, Cheung Kreav commune, Rolea Bier district, Kampong Chhnang province, named Nguon Srey Pov, 26 years old, was lucky to win a grand prize of 100 million Riels from Egyptian green tea. After buying a bottle last weekend.
Speaking to the team that handed over the grand prize to the place, Ms. Nguon Srey Pov described that she was born in Banteay Meanchey province, but due to family difficulties and living in poverty and have two small children. In addition, she also decided to leave her hometown to live in Kampong Chhnang province, asking them to stay in a pig farm and help feed the pigs on the farm to earn some income.
She also confirmed with excitement that this 100 million Riel is very important, after receiving this big prize money, she will take some to pay off debts and leave some to create a business to support family life in the future. .
A residential and commercial development company launches "East Siem Reap" project and offers sale on Borey Bakong project
(Phnom Penh): Eben Living Solutions, a leading company in the field of residential and commercial development, has partnered with Pointer, a real estate development company, to celebrate the official launch of the "East Siem Reap" project and special offers. On sale of Borey Bakong project.
The event took place at Sofitel Phnom Penh Phuket on the night of December 10, 2019 with the participation of more than 300 guests, most of whom were interested in booking a house in Borey Bakong and want to learn more about urban development. New satellite around the area along the 60-meter road in Siem Reap.
Seeing the movement towards the east of Siem Reap, Eben Living Solutions has been developing a new satellite city of 215 hectares, called "East Siem Reap", located in Ampil commune, Prasat district. Bakong, Siem Reap, about 10 minutes from the city and 5 minutes from the administrative city.
The development phase focuses on creating more tourist destinations and re-attracting national and international visitors, transforming Siem Reap into one of the most desirable cities in Southeast Asia.
For sustainable development, the company decided to expand on four factors:
1: Business sector in the area of 60 meters of road 2: Expand tourism beyond the temple area 3: International education 4: Create a modern community living and surrounded by green nature.
In fact, the Borey Bakong project is one of the four initiatives in the "East Siem Reap" area, with many clients appreciating the project's master plan, which transforms a 4.7-hectare site into a gathering place. Live like a community like never before. The principle of not allowing vehicles to drive through and replace with pedestrians applies to residents of the Bakong area.
The project is highly valued for its resemblance to a new city, with a natural environment, mountain scenery not far from the city, a 2-hectare park, a school, a market, a parking lot, and the first pedestrian flyover. In Siem Reap.
Mr. Tony Socheat Saktisunly, Project Manager of Borey Phum Bakong, said, “East Siem Reap will be very positive for customers who buy on these Borey Phum Bakong projects, which is the most correct investment step in the real estate sector and innovation. The quality of construction as well as the promotion of tourism in Siem Reap. Pakistan invites Cambodian parliament speaker to pay official and friendly visit to his country
