General Ith Sarath thanks Thailand for helping prevent illegal rebels from seizing Thai land and causing insecurity in Cambodia
(Phnom Penh): General Ith Sarath, Deputy Commander-in-Chief and Joint Chief of Staff of the Royal Cambodian Armed Forces, praised the cooperation between the two countries' armed forces, Cambodia and Thailand, as well as the people and people living along the border. Especially thanks to the prevention of illegal rebels who want to take Thai land to cause insecurity in Cambodia.
General Ith Sarath's assessment was made on December 11, 2019, on the occasion of the visit of Lt. Gen. Piroach Vilailug, Director of the Royal Thai Army Border Affairs Department. Paying a courtesy call and discussing the work at the meeting room of the Royal Cambodian Armed Forces General Command on the occasion of leading a delegation on a working visit to Cambodia.
During the meeting, General Ith Sarath, on behalf of the leadership of the Ministry of National Defense and the Commander-in-Chief of the Royal Cambodian Armed Forces, welcomed and briefed on the general situation in Cambodia, especially Cambodia-Thailand, which had just been successfully elected. And transparency.
Regarding the issue of Sam Rainsy prisoners, General Ith Sarath also confirmed this principle that Sam Rainsy prisoners have crossed the red line of democracy, and on the political side, Sam Rainsy prisoners are showing their true nature in their attempts. Coup d'état to overthrow Cambodia's constitutional monarchy, a prisoner of treason, cannot be pardoned.
General Ith Sarath expressed his gratitude to the Royal Government, the people and the Royal Thai Army for providing good cooperation with Cambodia for not giving territory to Sam Rainsy prisoners and the opposition to create a chaotic movement. Which led to a catastrophe to the construction and development of Cambodia.
General Ith Sarath said that in the past, Cambodian trainees have been accepted to train in counter-terrorism skills in Thailand through the Joint Chiefs of Staff Meeting between the Joint Chiefs of Staff and the Commander-in-Chief of the Royal Cambodian Armed Forces. In the past, the Joint Chiefs of Staff of the Royal Thai Army in Siem Reap province have achieved successful results and mutual understanding.
Lt. Gen. Phiroch Villaluk also praised the good cooperation between the Prime Ministers of the two countries, as well as the commanders-in-chief of the two armies, Thailand and Cambodia.
Lt. Gen. Phiroch Vilailuk also requested the advice and approval of the Deputy Commander-in-Chief of the Joint Chiefs of Staff of the Royal Cambodian Armed Forces on the organization of the Thai-Cambodian Joint Chiefs of Staff Meeting, which we held every year. One by one, take turns hosting the host to advance to the rank of Commander-in-Chief before attending the GBA meeting of officials.
At the same time, Mr. Phiroch Vilailuk also requested to General Ith Sarath that every annual meeting be strengthened, expanded and exchanged with each other, including programs on culture, performing arts and sports, including Celebrating the annual Flower or Kathina Festival to Thailand or Cambodia, as Cambodia has done with Vietnam and Laos.
