(Phnom Penh): Cambodia and the United Arab Emirates or the United Arab Emirates will sign a memorandum of understanding on employment and vocational training in the near future to increase cooperation in this field and prepare to send-receive Cambodian workers to work in The United Arab Emirates, as it is claimed, is now living and working in the country in good harmony.
Prior to the above meeting, a draft memorandum of understanding on employment and vocational training has been sent from the UAE side to the Cambodian side, and now the Cambodian side's expert working group is jointly reviewing. Carefully too.
Mr. Ith Sam Heng expressed his appreciation for the close relations and cooperation between the Kingdom of Cambodia and the United Arab Emirates and also welcomed the efforts to promote the new Memorandum of Understanding, which is going well.
"Once the memorandum is signed, it will provide more new opportunities for Cambodians who want to find work abroad and earn high incomes," he said. In Cambodia, there are many jobs and some places lack labor, but the Royal Government of Cambodia still provides opportunities and job search abroad for more people.
The minister added that by going abroad to work, the workers have been able to earn an income as well as gain professional experience.
In addition, in 2019, the United Arab Emirates government has introduced a policy to protect the rights, freedoms and interests of people living, doing business and doing business in their country to make life in this country more secure. .
Please be informed that there are currently no Cambodian workers to work in the United Arab Emirates through companies licensed by the Royal Government of Cambodia and the United Arab Emirates Government, but some Cambodian workers may go to work there on their own. Ministry of Public Works Holds Training Course on Rules for Rescueing Traffic Accident Victims and Risks of Driving Under the Influence of Alcohol
(Banteay Meanchey): The Ministry of Public Works and Transport (MPWT) has launched a training course on safe driving, rescue rules for victims and the risk of driving under the influence of alcohol. This training course was held on December 11, 2019 at Mongkul Borey High School in Chamkar Ta Dok village, Russey Krok commune, Mongkul Borey district, Banteay Meanchey province.
Mr. Sen Cheat Visoth, Deputy Director of the Department of Road Safety said that the same training course will be held in Battambang from 12 to 14 December 2019.
He added that traffic safety is a major public health and development issue that needs to be addressed urgently. The global traffic accident death toll remains high and continues to rise sharply, reaching 1.35 million annually.
He added that traffic accidents have become the number one problem in the world, claiming the lives of people between the ages of 5 and 29. About 50% of all fatalities are motorcyclists, pedestrians and cyclists.
According to the report of the National Road Safety Committee, in the third quarter of 2019, there were 988 traffic accidents on the roads of the Kingdom of Cambodia, resulting in 488 deaths and 1 injury. , 494 people.
As of October 2019, traffic accidents have caused 100 deaths and 129 serious injuries in Banteay Meanchey province. In Battambang province, 101 people died (an increase of 15%) and 177 others were seriously injured.
