Leaders of the Ministry of Women's Affairs and the Ministry of Tourism visit Siem Reap to study the situation of women in tourism
The visit was organized by the Ministry of Tourism with the aim of studying the situation of women in tourism and the role of women in contributing to the development of society through their professional skills and work activities to promote economic empowerment. Height.
The visit also reflected the attention of the Ministry of Tourism, which has the close support of the Ministry of Women's Affairs in an indispensable partnership to improve the quality and value of women's work. Contributed to the development of tourism in Cambodia to grow steadily.
This is also a new step in the cooperation of the two ministries in promoting gender equality in response to the fourth phase of the Royal Government's Rectangular Policy and Strategy "For Employment Growth, Equity and Efficiency", which provided employment opportunities for women. Emphasis on strengthening ownership, contributing to the family economy and promoting Cambodia's economic growth, proving that women are the backbone of the economy and society.
Taking the opportunity of this visit, the delegation of both Ministries also met with the sisters of Kampong Phluk Tourism Community to encourage them and connect good relations between women leaders and women in the community. In addition, we bring memories of the visit from Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister and Samdech Kittiprittbandit Bun Rany Hun Sen, as well as some gifts to you.
As a result of this visit, the analysis of policies and strategic plans to promote gender equality in both sectors (Women's Affairs and Tourism) has been very fruitful, turning the challenges into solutions and strengthening the role of women. Better to participate in the development of society, reduce poverty.
It should be noted that tourism has created a lot of job opportunities for women. According to the World Tourism Organization, there are more women service providers and business managers in the sector than men compared to other sectors of the economic cluster at 60-70% in the context of countries and regions. .
In Cambodia, in particular, women, who are the workforce in this sector, make up about 60% of all services in tourism activities. In this sense, women have a potential contribution to providing quality services to support tourism as well as attract more tourists to visit Cambodia.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen thanks all the benefactors who have supported Calmette Hospital (Video inside) (Phnom Penh): Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, on December 11, 2019, thanked All the philanthropists who helped to build the building and equip Calmette Hospital to become a modern and multi-specialized national referral hospital.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen confirmed that so far, philanthropists have donated more than $ 72 million to build and equip Calmette Hospital. Adding the state budget of $ 30 million, the total amount is more than $ 102 million.
This statement was made on the occasion of Samdech Techo Hun Sen handing over diplomas to nearly 7,000 CUS students at the Koh Pich Convention and Exhibition Center in Phnom Penh this morning, December 11, 2019.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen pointed out that in the past, Calmette Hospital built the building by buying new and expensive equipment from abroad, and the hospital paid for the equipment in stages with a laser machine. Nearly 4 million dollars, so people who went to seek medical treatment in the past, please understand the shortcomings.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen added that now Cambodians who can afford them have rushed to seek medical treatment abroad. Therefore, when Calmette Hospital is ready to be Calmette Hospital built and equipped with modern technical equipment, Samdech will consider stopping to go abroad for medical examination.
At the same time, Samdech Techo Hun Sen also mentioned that Cambodians who have poor card, equity card, National Social Security Fund card will receive treatment at Calmette Hospital free of charge. Separately, you can afford to pay for treatment.
It should be noted that Samdech Techo Hun Sen called on his compatriots and foreign friends to donate to Calmette Hospital to become a modern and multi-specialized national referral hospital.
According to the list of philanthropists, the amount of dollars is 72,425,871 dollars and 237,664,700 riels, including the state budget of 30 million dollars, so the budget to support Calmette Hospital is More than $ 102 million.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen used to say, "Compatriots as well as foreign friends who want to donate to Calmette Hospital, please contact Mr. Chheang Ra, Director of Calmette Hospital, Tel: 012 877 877. "Every philanthropist will have a thank you card signed by me, the Prime Minister himself." Singapore Philanthropist and Cambodia International Cooperation Institute Distribute Donations to 300 Students in Udong District, Kampong Speu Province
