Cambodia's real estate sector will continue to grow strongly in the future due to political stability, macroeconomic stability and population growth. The 2019 Cambodian Census shows that the total population in 2019 was 15.28 million, up 14 percent from 13.39 million in 2008. This growth reflects the growing demand for housing and commercial buildings.
According to the World Bank's Cambodia Economic Update released on November 27, 2019, the Cambodian economy will remain strong and grow at 7% in 2019. The World Bank indicates that the construction sector is still in a state of disarray, reflecting that there is no sign of fatigue in investing in the sector. As a result, construction steel imports rose sharply to 63.5 percent in June 2019 from 27.7 percent in 2018.
"It reflects that we are a professional company and a member of the world's most famous Century 21 family," he said. It is an important message to property owners in Cambodia to be aware of the importance of an internationally recognized, legitimate, legitimate agency that is properly registered in Cambodia and will be an active contributor to taxation and state revenue. "
According to data from the Ministry of Land Management, Urban Planning and Construction, from January to November 2019, the ministry approved investment projects in the construction sector with a total investment of more than 8.75 billion US dollars, an increase of 67 percent. Compared to the same 11 months in 2018.
There are 1,081 registered and valid companies doing construction and study projects in Cambodia, including 485 foreign companies from China, Korea, Japan, Thailand, Vietnam, Singapore, Malaysia, France, USA, Indonesia, Australia, Canada and Many other countries.
