The graduation ceremony for CUS students this morning took place at the Koh Pich Convention and Exhibition Center. Mr. Steung Sokhom, Chairman of the Board of Universities of Cambodia, said that a total of 6,762 students graduated, including 2,761 females. Students who receive this degree have associate degrees, bachelor's degrees, master's degrees and doctoral degrees.
They graduated in the 2017-2018 academic year and the previous 2018-2019 academic year at university locations in Phnom Penh and branches in six provinces, including Kampong Cham, Kampong Thom, Siem Reap, Battambang, Banteay Meanchey and Kampot. .
The University of Specialties of Cambodia is one of the leading higher education institutions in Cambodia and has been highly successful in training the resources to generate energy for national economic development with the Royal Government of Cambodia. To meet the growing demand of students from year to year, the University has expanded more branches both in Phnom Penh and in the provinces.
Currently, the University of Specialties of Cambodia has two locations in Phnom Penh and 6 branches in the provinces, including: Kampong Cham, Kampong Thom, Siem Reap, Banteay Meanchey, Battambang and Kampot. The university has a board of directors, management, staff and 1,205 professors, of which 198 are women.
The University has been training at five faculties: the Faculty of Arts, Humanities and Languages, the Faculty of Science and Technology, the Faculty of Business Administration and Economics, the Faculty of Engineering, and the Faculty of Social Sciences and Law.
Mr. Steng Sokhom emphasized that in order to build human resources with quality, value and success for the society, the University has set the basic principles in the implementation of its daily work, namely students, professors, academic staff must learn, teach, research and Provide quality service, professional ability and good personality. In other words, having good human resources means having everything that is good and better.
He also mentioned that the results and achievements of the past 17 years clearly show the ability, possibility and experience that the University of Specialties of Cambodia combined with the resources to teach, learn, research and experiment. Add to the job requirements from physical infrastructure, materials, technology, hard-soft documents that are richer and better qualified.
In order to strengthen and take advantage of the flow of knowledge and the practice of practical skills, the University has always invited experts in the field of labor to give lectures, conferences, seminars to students regularly and also send students to internships to the actual work site. Specific software.
The University cooperates and signs MoUs with 52 foreign universities and institutions from South Korea, China, Japan, Thailand, the United Kingdom, the Philippines, Bangladesh, Malaysia, India, Indonesia, Germany, Vietnam and Israel, sending professors and students to study. Long courses and short internships, as well as accepting foreign students to exchange studies with students of specialized universities of Cambodia.
