A group of disabled people received more than 8 million riels from philanthropists
(Phnom Penh): Under the full support and support of Samdech Mey, Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia and Samdech Kittipritthbandit Bun Rany Hun Sen, President of the Cambodian Red Cross, people with disabilities have been paying close attention. From the entire population.
In fact, on December 9, 2019, yesterday, Ms. Thour Samphors led a philanthropist to attend a reception and provide food and water to people with disabilities and distribute gifts to more than 200 people with disabilities in Samneang Music Association for more than 8 Million Riels.
On that occasion, Mr. Chap To, President of Samneang Music Association for the Disabled, made a report on the progress and challenges of the association. He said that the association was established on August 17, 2012, initially there were only more than 20 people with disabilities, but to date, the association has more than 250 members, all of whom are visually impaired. And fitness.
He added that from 2012 to 2017, the association had already rented eight houses. In 2016, after receiving the care of Samdech Mey, he donated 36,000 US dollars to buy land and build a shelter and training center for the disabled.
In addition, Samdech Katiprit Bun Rany Hun Sen has provided financial support and food from 2014 to the present. In addition, Samdech Kith Prith Bundith also donated money for the purchase of land and the construction of a residential center.
According to Mr. Chap To, Samdech Katipritbandit recently donated a 30-seat bus and an additional concrete road. He reminded that Samdech Techo Hun Sen and Samdech Katipritbandit in 2017 also donated a large set of musical instruments to the association.
Mr. Taing Sokhy described that the Samneang Music Association for the Disabled was initially formed with bare hands until the association had its own dormitory. The struggle of people with disabilities makes success as desired.
At the same time, the representative of the philanthropist sent a message to all people with disabilities, "I am physically disabled, but my heart and mind are not disabled." People with disabilities must continue to strive for greater capacity and employment, both now and in the future.
The participation of philanthropists also to celebrate the 21st Cambodian Day of Persons with Disabilities and the 37th International Day of Persons with Disabilities on December 3, 2019 under the presidency of Samdech Krala Hom Sar Kheng, Deputy Prime Minister and Minister of Interior on behalf of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia and also a representative of Samdech Katiprit Bun Rany Hun Sen.
On that occasion, the philanthropist donated 8 million riels and 1,000 kilograms of rice, orange juice, pure water, and 10 cases of noodles from monks and 150,000 riels. In addition, Tycoon Taing Sokhy and his family donated 1 million Riels, while Miss Duong Surida, President of the Cambodian Model Association, donated 530,000 Riels.
This blind man would like to prostrate and bless Samdech Yeay, Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Samdech Kittipritthbandit Bun Rany Hun Sen, all benefactors, may he live to be over a hundred years old and bless God. Physical fitness and good health are always abundant.
Please be informed that the Samneang Music Association for the Disabled was established in 2013 by Mr. Chap To, a blind person. The association is located in Chumral Village, Sangkat Kork Roka, Khan Prek Pnov, Phnom Penh and is also recognized by the Ministry of Interior.
A one-story L-shaped building for the disabled is beginning to hit the ground, with 15 dormitories and a capacity of 60 to 80 people. According to the plan, the building will have four specialized rooms for teaching contemporary music, classical music and classical music, as well as a massage room, a kitchen, a kitchen, a performance room, a reception area and so on.
The completed building will provide benefits for the blind, not only in this center, but people with disabilities in the provinces can also come to stay and learn skills to earn a living. The 4th China-Cambodia Mobile Film Screening in Prey Veng
(Prey Veng): With the agreement between the two countries of the Ministry of Culture and Fine Arts, the 4th China-Cambodia Mobile Film Festival was screened for the people, government officials, students in the plot of land near Samdech Chea Sim Park, Prey Veng City. Prey Veng Province.
This screening is for people, government officials and students to visit and learn more about the culture, art and film of the two countries. Also in the screening are two stories, "Hello, Millionaire!" And the Khmer drama entitled "The Owner of the Brown Knife" on the night of December 9, 2019, which was attended by about 500 people.
Mr. Ouk Sereyvuth, Director of Prey Veng Provincial Department of Culture and Fine Arts, expressed his happiness, considering that this morning brought entertainment and encouraged cultural and artistic exchanges between the people of Cambodia and China. He said that movies play an important role in imparting knowledge about the culture, traditions, customs, lifestyle of the people and the development of each country.
He considered that the 4th China-Cambodia Mobile Film Festival 2019 was held at the same time as the Cambodian-Chinese government considered it as a year of cultural and tourism exchanges between the two countries, as well as helping to promote Strengthen the cooperation in the field of culture, film and cinema between Cambodia and China to deepen and have a stronger relationship from one city to another.
At the same time, the young people who came to see this movie have expressed their great satisfaction and wish for such an event in the future.
According to Ratana Rayuth, director of the China-Cambodia Film Screening Team of the Cambodia-China Friendship Radio, the 2019 "Best China-Cambodia Mobile Film Tour" will bring famous films. Many stories to be screened in Takeo, Kampot and Kandal provinces.
He added that after screening in Pailin, Oddar Meanchey, Kratie and Tbong Khmum, to achieve the goal of being screened across the country, while the event has already been held in 24 provinces with an audience. More than 100,000 people attended.
Cambodia, Thailand hold joint meeting to prevent cross-border drug trafficking
(Koh Kong): In order to strengthen friendship, solidarity and alliance to prevent cross-border drug trafficking and use between Cambodia and Thailand, Koh Kong Provincial Authority and Trat Provincial Authority held a meeting at a resort in Peam Krasop Commune, Mondul Seima District, Koh Kong Province. .
The meeting was chaired by Mr. Phay Thun Plamkes, Deputy Governor of Koh Kong Province, Mr. Prak Vichet, Governor of Mondul Seima District, and his subordinates. The Thai side was led by Mr. Sophmit Chhin Si, Deputy Governor of Trat Province, and Mr. Phirak Karun, Governor of Khlong Yai District. This meeting was held on December 9, 2019.
Mr. Sopheth Mith Chinsy, Deputy Governor of Thailand, said that the Cambodian authorities should take strong measures to prevent drug problems with criminals smuggled across the border on the Cambodian-Thai border. Therefore, he asked the Cambodian authorities to have a stronger and more transparent control in drug trafficking through international gates or corridors, etc., which the perpetrators use in all forms to cross-border traffic.
The Thai side also requested the authorities to put pressure on the group of workers hauling cross-border carts and transporting workers of cross-border tourists or the luggage of the people in and out of the country. The luggage came later, because some time ago, the perpetrator used all the above-mentioned images, and when the police found drugs, the perpetrator escaped.
Mr. Sophim Chhin Si asked the authorities on both sides to have a thorough inspection before allowing tourists or luggage owners to cross the border, if this problem occurs, the authorities on both sides to provide information to each other quickly.
Mr. Phay Thuon Plam Keson said that the two authorities work together to prevent cross-border drug trafficking to reduce drug users, and the two authorities to exchange experiences for each other for the two provinces. He stressed that Cambodia is always willing to cooperate in the work of promoting Thailand.
He asked the Thai side to provide information to the Cambodian authorities as soon as possible to facilitate the crackdown on suspects arrested from Thailand who fled into the territory of Koh Kong province, asked the Thai authorities not to hide the information. Provide information quickly to the Cambodian authorities to search for the perpetrators and punish them according to the law.
