(Banteay Meanchey): As desired for a long time, now the people living in Khtom Chrum village, Rohat Teuk commune, Mongkul Borei district, Banteay Meanchey province, get a new road to travel again after a road encroachment by a woman More than 100 meters and 4 meters wide.
The return of the land after requesting the intervention of Deputy Prime Minister Ke Kim Yan, Chairman of the National Working Group to assist Banteay Meanchey province and coordinated by Mr. Ou Rathrey, Provincial Governor, with the participation of the Board of Governors of Mongkul Borei District, authorities and Relevant authorities.
Mongkul Borei district governor told Fresh News this morning, December 10, 2019 that yesterday, the provincial governor, he and the relevant local authorities resumed the mediation, and now both sides have agreed to Make another detour for travel.
"This solution, the Governor of Banteay Meanchey and his team decided to help clear a new road for the people with paving stones 86 meters long and 4 meters wide, which HE Governor and I helped out."
At the same time, the people also expressed their deep gratitude to Deputy Prime Minister Ke Kim Yan, who introduced the provincial administration and relevant authorities until a new solution was found for them at this time, and also thanked the provincial and district governors for their immediate intervention. Also.
It should be informed that the villagers used to say that this road, which is 120 meters long and 4 meters wide, has been a road since ancient times. The car passes daily into their home.
At the same time, the district governor and officials also brought some gifts and money to give to a woman who fell into the hospital because of this protest.
Keo Sok Pheng thanked the fans for their encouragement and commitment to do well for Myanmar
(Phnom Penh): One of Cambodia's best attacking midfielders, Keo Sok Pheng, came out to thank the Cambodian people and sports fans for sending messages of encouragement and encouragement to him. After some verbal pressure, after the Vietnamese Association in Cambodia tried to open up their history, the Vietnamese mother.
On the day when the Cambodian U22 national football team competed for the final seat with the Vietnamese national team in the 30th SEA Games in the Philippines on December 7, the Vietnamese Association in Cambodia Through its Facebook page, it reveals the background of Keo Sok Pheng, who has a Vietnamese mother in Tay Ninh province, the former Rong Damrey province of Kampuchea Krom.
Breaking the background of the Vietnamese Association has made some Cambodians who have a tendency to hate the Vietnamese appear some bad words to become emotional pressure for Keo Sok Pheng. Even worried that the best player of Cambodia to resign from this field because of the pressure of those words.
But at the same time, many Cambodians and football fans came out to encourage by writing many encouraging messages, regardless of the background of Keo Sok Pheng, who has a Vietnamese mother. Fans see that through football and as a national player of Cambodia, Keo Sok Pheng has brought a lot of honor for Cambodia and also contributed to the promotion of football in Cambodia.
After receiving many encouraging messages from Cambodians and football fans, on December 9, 2019, Keo Sok Pheng came out to thank those encouragement. Keo Sok Pheng called this encouragement in the spirit of the "Great Khmer Family", an invaluable sympathy.
Keo Sok Pheng added that this encouragement will make him strive to improve himself in the field of Cambodian football. "Your enthusiasm has driven me to work harder and more self-disciplined for future career advancement."
At the same time, Keo Sok Pheng also vowed to cooperate with his national teammates to improve in the bronze medal match with the Myanmar national team in the 30th SEA Games on December 10, 2019.
The 27-year-old Cambodian Cambodian midfielder also wrote a statement confirming his firm stance on continuing to work with Cambodian football to make Cambodian football better. "We will move forward together to win and develop our national football!"
Keo Sok Pheng was born on March 3, 1992 in Rokar Kandal Village, Sangkat Rokar Kandal, Kratie City, Kratie Province. Sok Pheng is currently playing for Visakha Club. Keo Sok Pheng is the younger brother of Keo Sok Ngon, a former national team player.
Keo Sok Pheng has played for the national team since 2015, scoring three goals in his four matches at the 2015 SEA Games. Then in 2018, Sok Pheng was called to help the national team in the World Cup qualifiers.
Mr. Veng Sakhon requested the people to continue to maintain peace, good social order and to support the Royal Government in leading the country's development
(Kampong Cham): Mr. Veng Sakhon, Chairman of the National Task Force for Kampong Siem and Cheung Prey Districts, Kampong Cham Province and Tambor District, Tbong Khmum Province, on December 10, 2019, requested the people to continue to maintain peace, social order and Participate in supporting the Royal Government in leading the country's development.
Mr. Veng Sakhon made this remark on the occasion of presiding over a public forum held at Wat Russey Chroy in Ta Sen village, Sotip commune, Cheung Prey district.
The forum was attended by the Chairman, Deputy Chairman of the Commune Assistance Team, District Governor, District Councilor, Commune Chairman, Deputy Chairman of the District Office and about 450 people from 8 villages: Boeung Chroy Daun Dom Sotip Ngong Thmey, Ta Sen Pana and Skun village.
The purpose of this event is to monitor the implementation of the fourth phase of the Royal Government's Rectangular Policy and Strategy Program, in particular to strengthen the relationship between the leadership and the local people to be closer and deeper, which is a good opportunity for the leadership to monitor the well-being. , Daily problems, needs, requests or suggestions and solve those problems for citizens gradually.
Mr. Veng Sakhon informed that today is Human Rights Day, please use your time to exercise your rights and ask questions about the leadership of the Royal Government to get more knowledge and information about the country's development. The real nation today avoids misunderstandings, misrepresentations, incitement, painting, polluting the environment in society by illegal rebels.
He added that based on all these needs, the Royal Government has set out the fourth phase of the Rectangular Policy and Strategy, which needs to be developed in all areas step by step in accordance with the time and resources of our nation.
He stated that in order to solve all the needs of the people in a timely and effective manner, he would like to send the members of the national working group to help the districts, communes and villages, local authorities and the armed forces at all levels, especially the people. Citizens, please continue to maintain peace and good social order, continue to support the Royal Government in leading the country and strongly oppose any movement to overthrow the legitimate Royal Government.
He requested the working group and sub-national authorities to pay attention to and implement the recommendations of Samdech Techo consistently, timely and effectively, especially to continue to provide better and more efficient services to all people. Figure.
During the ceremony, the people asked questions and requests such as rehabilitation of canals, sewers, repairing roads, red stones for repairing roads and protective clothing.
In order to alleviate the difficulties of sharing and resolving the request, Mr. Veng Sakhon and his colleagues decided to support all the requests, including the donation of 4 million Riels for the construction of Russey Chroy pagoda's abbot for construction, and each participant received 2 budgets. Ten thousand riel as well.
