34 farming communities in Preah Vihear province sell more than 20,000 tons of organic rice to 3 companies under contract in 2019
(Preah Vihear): In 2019, 34 farming communities in Preah Vihear province with a total production of 5,341 families on a total area of 14,769 hectares sold organic rice to three companies under contract for a total of 22,461 tons.
"As of December 8, 2019, these three companies have collected a total of 22,461 tons of organic rice from all agricultural communities," said the director of the provincial agriculture department. "Golden Rice collected 3,129 tons of rice 100% of the plan, Amro Rice collected 12,841 tons of rice, about 75%, while Sikh Netchor Asia collected 1,000 tons of rice, about 70%."
Mr. Peng Trida pointed out that the price of rice was satisfactory to the farmers, with wet rice fragrant flowers sold for 1,260 to 1,320 riels per kilogram, dried rice fragrant flowers sold for 1,500 to 15 riels. 90 riel per kilogram, while Neang Ok Neang Amneang glass, brown rice sells for 1,140 riel per kilogram. He said that selling rice to companies under contract gets a higher price compared to we sell to middlemen.
