It should be noted that Cambodia's best jujitsu fighter Khan Chesa added another gold medal to Cambodia after defeating the host Philippines in the 30th SEA Games on December 9, 2019 .
This is the fourth gold medal for Cambodia in the 30th SEA Games. The gold medal won by the Cambodian-American athlete lifted Cambodia to seventh place in the provisional medal table with 41 medals (4 gold, 6 silver and 31 bronze).
Please note that Khan Chesa is now 18 years old, has a Cambodian father and a Mexican mother, but has the same American citizenship. Currently living in the United States.
Chesa has been involved in jujitsu since she was a child under the tutelage of her father, and a few years later she won several gold medals before she won an Asian Games gold medal. A gold medal from the 2018 Asian Games in Indonesia broke Cambodia's 64-year history of never winning a gold medal.
