(Phnom Penh): Samdech Pich Sena Tea Banh, Deputy Prime Minister and Minister of National Defense, urged Cambodian-Chinese military inspectors to continue to strengthen cooperation and increase ties in the future.
The Cambodian defense chief made the call on the afternoon of December 9, 2019, during a courtesy call on Lt. Gen. Jiang Hong Jun, Director General of the Inspection Department of the Chinese People's Liberation Army. At the Friendship Building, Office of the Council of Ministers.
Samdech Pich Sena Tea Banh welcomed the delegation of the General Inspection Department of the People's Liberation Army of China led by Major General Jiang Hongjun, calling it a further strengthening of cooperation between the People's Armed Forces of the two countries. Both Cambodia and China, especially in the field of military inspection skills of both countries.
The General also informed about the fruitful results of the bilateral working meeting between the General Inspection Department of the People's Liberation Army of China and the Inspection Department of the Ministry of National Defense of Cambodia.
Lt. Gen. Jiang Hongjun stressed that the Chinese side, focusing on Sino-Cambodian relations, has established a common destiny to contribute to the region's economic and security sectors. The lieutenant general understood that now the relationship between the two armies is based on a new history, in line with the core needs and interests of the two countries.
