(Phnom Penh): Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia and President of the Cambodian Veterans Association, this morning, December 10, 2019, presided over the opening ceremony of the 19th General Assembly of the ASEAN Veterans Federation. The ceremony was held at the Peace Palace with the participation of senior officials of the Royal Government of Cambodia, leaders of the Cambodian Veterans Association and leaders of the Association of Veterans from ASEAN member countries.
The following is the full text of Samdech Techo Hun Sen's speech at the opening ceremony of the 19th General Assembly of the ASEAN Veterans Federation:
Samdech Akka Moha Sena Padei Techo, General of the Golden Star 5, Hun Sen, Prime Minister of the Kingdom of Cambodia and President of the Cambodian Veterans Association, speaks on the occasion of the 19th General Assembly of the ASEAN Veterans Union on Tuesday, March 14, 2012. 2563, Phnom Penh, December 10, 2019.
Samdech, Excellencies, Lok Chumteavs, Ladies and Gentlemen, Distinguished National and International Guests, Members of the General Assembly!
Today, I am pleased to attend the opening ceremony of the 19th General Assembly of the ASEAN Veterans Federation, which is now held solemnly. I would like to welcome and thank His Excellency Lok Chumteav, President-Vice President of the ASEAN Veterans Federation, as well as the leaders of the Veterans Association of the Commonwealth Member States for their participation in this important General Assembly.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen Appreciates and Appreciates the Efforts of the Executive Committee of the ASEAN Veterans Federation to Work Together to Make the General Assembly Conformity and Agenda The goal is its priority.
Cambodia is honored to host and chair the rotating ASEAN Veterans Federation in accordance with the activities and objectives planned through the high attention paid by the representatives from the ASEAN Veterans Federation member countries in the field of Veterans Affairs. Fighters recognized by ASEAN member countries as part of ASEAN humanitarian work, both now and in the future.
In fact, the history of war veterans is very similar in every country in the world, in this sense, the group of people who sacrificed for their homeland is a symbol of high spirit with a patriotic conscience. Its inscribed in the history of each nation.
In fact, veterans of the war in Cambodia went through the tragedy and devastation of the war from generation to generation, from the Indochina War of 1970 to 1975 and the genocidal regime of Pol Pot from 1975 to 1979, and continued to face many challenges. Cambodia has to deal with economic, social, political and diplomatic issues, especially the struggle with the country's ongoing civil war.
After Cambodia achieved peace in late 1998 through the introduction of a "win-win policy", Cambodia gained full territorial unity, all armed forces and all stakeholders of the war veterans were integrated. Under the roof of the Royal Government of Cambodia alone. This is the foundation of political stability with the bringing of complete peace throughout the country.
All of these are noble traditions of the Cambodian people that have existed from ancient times to the present in helping each other to raise the patriotic consciousness of the younger generation to war veterans who have sacrificed and sacrificed their lives. In the cause of nation, religion, and the king.
The ASEAN Veterans Federation, an ASEAN humanitarian entity, has been active in paying close attention to veterans in ASEAN member states as part of the ASEAN Framework. Therefore, in order for this federation to achieve more new achievements within the framework of the ASEAN Action Plan, I would like to share some of the following opinions:
1: The ASEAN Veterans Federation must continue to promote the promotion of life luxury and prevent the impact of war-affected life on veterans' health through the protection of legitimate rights for the common benefit of war veterans. And their families with the legal recognition of the Veterans Association of the Federal Member States issue.
Finally, with the announcement of the opening of the 19th General Assembly of the ASEAN Veterans Federation, I would like to wish Samdech, Excellencies, Lok Chumteavs, Ladies and Gentlemen, Members of the General Assembly, national and international guests, good health and happiness. Progress and success in all tasks. China sells top smartphones in Japan
