(Phnom Penh): Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia and President of the Cambodian Veterans Association, on Tuesday, December 10, 2019, presided over the opening ceremony of the General Assembly. 19th ASEAN Veterans Federation.
The opening ceremony of the General Assembly was held at the Peace Palace with the participation of senior officials of the Royal Government of Cambodia, leaders of the Cambodian Veterans Association and leaders of the Association of Veterans from ASEAN member countries.
It should be noted that in 2019, Cambodia was hosted and chaired by Laos in organizing the 32nd Executive Committee Meeting and the 19th General Assembly of the ASEAN Veterans Federation, which was planned to The agenda of the meeting lasted for 5 days, from 08 to 12 December 2019.
The federation was established to promote the luxury of life, the impact of age and the impact of war on the health and social well-being of war victims, and to raise awareness among the people in order to achieve advanced cooperation. Towards harmony, social justice and peace.
The federation also has a mission to promote a global understanding of the views, values, praises and interests of countries in the region and to promote the legitimacy of the interests of war veterans and war victims with the legal recognition of Veterans Association of Federal Member States.
In addition, promote the exchange of veterans and victims of regional warfare by organizing development programs, seminars, information sharing and other activities that benefit members, and the federation will strengthen the scope of incentives and participation. From the leaders of each member country to protect the right to life, solidarity and personal safety.
The activities and efforts of the ASEAN Veterans Federation are recognized by ASEAN as a humanitarian entity that has been working directly with war veterans and their families. At the same time, ASEAN has been reviewing the qualifications of the federation to include the ASEAN Veterans Federation as part of ASEAN activities.
