(Phnom Penh): On the morning of Monday, March 13, 2019, on December 9, 2019, the Cambodian Red Cross and Red Crescent Branch of Kandal Province celebrated the 5th International Day of Volunteers. December 2019 under the theme "Volunteering for an Environmental Future".
The ceremony was presided over by Ms. Men Neary Sopheak, Acting Secretary General of KRK and Dr. Mao Phirun, Honorary President of KRK Branch, Kandal Province, and was attended by leaders, officials of Kandal Branch, officials and volunteers. About 500 people at the branch office in Kandal province.
Speaking on that occasion, the Acting Secretary General brought the remarks of Samdech Kittipritthbandit Bun Rany Hun Sen, President of the Cambodian Red Cross, who sent a message of thanks and deep appreciation to the leading forces of all volunteers who donated. Resources, time, physical and mental strength from the heart, purely humanitarian to contribute to helping the most vulnerable and vulnerable people in the community and in educational institutions.
At the same time, she emphasized the value of volunteer work, and that the International Day of Volunteers is to promote the voluntary participation in the humanitarian work of the International Red Cross and Red Crescent Movement, which now has a national association. In 192 countries, there are more than 12 million volunteers, a potential human resource, the backbone of the movement and an effective and timely humanitarian operator.
In fact, the Cambodian Red Cross has strengthened and expanded the force of more than 40,000 volunteers across the country, which is an indispensable force in providing hope and warmth to the most vulnerable in a timely and complete manner. Location.
Representatives of 2 volunteers and 3 poor youths expressed their interest and expressed their high commitment to fulfill their role as the leading force following the heroic example of Samdech Kittipritthbandit Bun Rany Hun Sen to participate in further activities as Cambodian Red Cross volunteers for the benefit of the vulnerable and disaster victims in the community.
To encourage the 343 volunteers who participated in the event, the Cambodian Red Cross provided a certificate of appreciation and a budget of 50,000 Riels each.
Separately, Kandal Provincial Branch received additional support, each received 1 sarong, 5 T-shirts and 20,000 Riels. For 50 poor people, the Cambodian Red Cross provided 20,000 Riels to each of them, 2 notebooks and 1 pen and another 20,000 Riels belonging to Kandal Provincial Branch.
At the same time, Kandal Provincial Branch also organized a solidarity meal for all volunteers and young people who participated in this event.
Please note that the Cambodian Red Cross has celebrated the International Day of Volunteers every year, in 2012 and 2013 in Kampong Thom, 2014 in Preah Vihear, 2015 in Prey Veng, 2016 in Svay Rieng, 2017 In Takeo and Battambang provinces, 2018 in Kampong Cham and Kratie provinces.
For this year 2019, the head office participated in organizing this day celebration in Kampong Speu, Kandal and Pursat provinces. Separately, other branches will celebrate according to their actual capabilities.
