The Republic of Korea continues to provide grants to Cambodia through the Ministry of Water Resources related to the climate monitoring system
(Phnom Penh): The Ministry of Water Resources and Meteorology on the afternoon of December 9, 2019 held a meeting to discuss and sign a Memorandum of Understanding on the project "Installation of automatic climate monitoring system in Cambodia for forecasting and Pre-Disclosure of Natural Disasters in Cambodia ”is a grant provided by the Meteorological Administration of the Republic of Korea.
The grants currently provided by the Meteorological Administration of the Republic of Korea to the Ministry of Water Resources and Meteorology are as follows:
* First, install 27 automatic meteorological stations in the provinces that do not have enough meteorological stations to monitor the weather to get more comprehensive information enough for forecasting, researching and using other fields.
* Second, equip some other meteorological equipment to support the weather forecast and early warning system on natural disasters in Cambodia. Sending Korean technicians to help train in the country and provide additional training in Korea to strengthen the capacity of Cambodian meteorological officials to forecast the weather more accurately.
* Third: In addition, the Korea Meteorological Administration and the Korea Meteorological Institute and the Cambodian Ministry of Water Resources and Meteorology will continue to discuss the possibility of providing additional grant projects on access to meteorological information from new meteorological satellites. GK-2A of the Republic of Korea for use in analyzing and monitoring the status of elements in Cambodia.
