(Phnom Penh): About 8 out of 77 families who have land in Russey Keo development area and have not yet received land according to the authority's distribution, insist that the National Authority expedite the distribution of plots of land to them and ask for the division The plot is transparent.
Please be reminded that land disputes in the Russey Keo development area in Spean Khpos village, Sangkat Kilometer 6 and Sangkat Toul Sangke, Khan Russey Keo have been going on for many years. Recently, the authorities decided to divide the land in the disputed area to the people, with each family getting about 20 meters by 30 meters. But the eight families refused to accept the authorities' decision, claiming it was unfair to them.
The eight families claim that the division of land is not transparent and unfair to them. Unfair because some of them have documents to occupy up to 23 plots, get land from the authorities to divide only 5 plots and some occupy up to 11 plots, the authorities split into 3 plots and some others occupy 3 plots and get a decision From the authorities only 1 lot.
Although the case has been referred to Samdech Techo's cabinet for resolution, the relevant authorities have not yet come forward to resolve the case at the request of the eight families.
The eight families requested the relevant authorities to help resolve and distribute plots of land to them in a transparent and fair manner.
The Royal Academy of Cambodia Techo Sen Russey Park is looking for a distributor of milk in the provinces.
(Phnom Penh): The Royal Academy of Cambodia Techo Sen Russey Park has announced the recruitment of fresh milk distributors in the provinces to expand the distribution of fresh milk made by Khmer children for the first time.
Please note that the fresh milk produced at the Royal Academy of Cambodia Techo Sen Russey Trup Park, the first fresh milk produced by Cambodian children, has been distributed on the market for many months. But this distribution takes place only in Phnom Penh.
The official of the Royal Academy of Cambodia, who distributes fresh milk, emphasized that Techo Sen Russey Trup fresh milk is 100% pure milk without any added chemicals or preservatives that can affect the health of consumers. No. This milk is full of protein and high in calcium, it promotes health, promotes growth, nourishes the bones, and makes you smarter.
The Royal Academy of Cambodia Techo Sen Russey Trip Park in Preah Vihear province's Chep district was discovered as Cambodia's largest steel industry site 1,000 years ago. In modern times, this area has also been transformed into a food industry in Cambodia in order to improve the lives of the people.
Those who drank fresh Cambodian milk praised the taste as more delicious than some fresh milk imported from neighboring countries.
The official who distributes the fresh milk called on the Cambodian people to support Cambodian products to boost production and help people live by encouraging them to raise dairy cows.
The price is also cheaper than imported milk, a liter capacity of only 10,000 riel.
