Cambodia International Cooperation Lawyers Hold 2019 Annual Meeting on "Development Plan 2020"
(Phnom Penh): The Cambodian Bar Association for International Cooperation organized its 2019 Annual Meeting and Excursion in Siem Reap from December 7 to 10, 2019, and on December 08, 2019, the Bar Association organized 2019 Annual Meeting on "Preparation for Self-Development Plan 2020" at Regency Angkor Hotel.
Lawyer Ly Raththy, President of the Cambodia International Cooperation Lawyer Group, said at the opening of the meeting that the Cambodia International Cooperation Lawyer Group was established on March 24, 2015, which until now is For almost five years.
In the last five years, the lawyers have held four annual meetings, including this year, the first and the second being held in Siem Reap, the third in Mondulkiri, and the second annual meeting. 4 For 2019, this will also take place in Siem Reap.
Annual meetings are an important activity for lawyers to reflect on strengths, weaknesses, opportunities, as well as barriers to the performance of lawyers, and the results of those reflections provide an important input for lawyers. Develop a plan as well as a strategy to carry out tasks more effectively.
Mr. Ly Raththy added that over the past five years, the Cambodian International Cooperation Lawyers Group has grown in all areas, evolving from the beginning with 2 lawyers and 5 members, a total of 7 members. Until there are 08 lawyers, 20 members, a total of 28 at present.
Lawyers, Heads of Staff, Members of the Bar Association are highly qualified, experienced and committed to working for clients as well as ethical lawyers. Teamwork, sharing and mutual assistance are important mechanisms for lawyers and motivate them to work effectively and efficiently.
However, through the constant evolution of the socio-economic sector, education and globalization, including technological modernization, etc., the lawyers of all members must continue to develop themselves to push the legal team towards the goal. Assigned.
That is why the 2019 Annual Meeting of the Bar Association now focuses on the preparation of its own development plan for 2020 of the lawyers and members, which is an indispensable input in the preparation of their own development plan. The Bar Association for 2020, as well as the three-year plan of the Bar Association from 2020 to 2022, this is further confirmed by the President of the Bar Association.
After welcoming and opening the program of the President of the Bar Association, the meeting proceeded with a series of agendas, such as the 11-month report from January to November 2019 of the four divisions of the Bar Association, including the Administration Division. Legal, financial and accounting services, including inspection and discipline.
Divide into discussion groups to reflect on the work activities of the legal team using the SWOT & BEEM tool. The next step of the meeting was to present the personal development plan of the four divisions and the personal development plan of the lawyers, the division chief and all members of the bar team for 2020.
