(Phnom Penh): In general, the individual is guaranteed full rights and freedoms by the law, not to be violated or forcibly or illegally confiscated.
The law protects the life, honor and dignity of the people. All charges, arrests, detentions or detentions of any person will be applicable only if the law is properly followed. Therefore, what are the legal guarantees for those arrested or detained?
This week, the Cambodian Lawyers for International Cooperation in collaboration with FRESH NEWS would like to raise the topic of "Rights of Perpetrators and Suspects in Arrest" to share with the following citizens and students:
According to Cambodian law, anyone arrested or detained by a judicial police officer has certain rights to defend themselves, which are important rights and cannot be violated or revoked. When a perpetrator is arrested or a suspect is arrested by a judicial police officer, the perpetrator and the suspect have certain rights, such as:
1. Right to know the reason for arrest or detention: When detaining a person, the judicial police officer must immediately inform his / her decision of the reason for the decision to detain, the right to have a lawyer and the right to an interpreter. .
5. Detained juvenile: When a detainee is a juvenile, the judicial police officer must inform by all means the parents, the legal representative or the person in charge of the juvenile.
6. The right to remain silent: Detainees have the right to remain silent, not to answer questions from judicial police officers until they have the help of a lawyer and no one can force them to answer.
7. Right not to confess: A person who has been arrested or detained must not answer what he or she did not do, or can answer or not confess until there is a defense lawyer without anyone being able to force him or her to confess to the crime. Any offense by threats, beatings, torture. All confessions arising out of physical, psychological, threatening, beatings, or torture shall not be considered as evidence of guilt.
8. Rights brought to court: After arrest, the perpetrator and the suspect must be charged or sent to court as soon as possible. And the court must check the regularity of the procedure of judicial police officers in the arrest or detention is done in accordance with the law? And to expedite procedural action and ensure the right to a fair trial of the accused.
9. Right to file a complaint against a misdemeanor of a judicial police officer: If any rights guaranteed by law to the perpetrator or suspect at the time of arrest are violated or denied by the judicial police officer, that person may file a complaint of violation or protest. Deny that directly or through its attorney to the prosecution or the investigating judge or the competent court.
In summary, all arrests or detentions of offenders or suspects, judicial police officers and prosecutors must respect the above basic rights, and if there is any violation, the perpetrators or suspects can file a complaint. Time, too.
