Article 31 of the Constitution of the Kingdom of Cambodia reaffirms these principles by recognizing and respecting human rights as enshrined in international treaties, stating that all Cambodian citizens have "equal rights before the law, rights and freedoms." All cases are the same "regardless of social status and" have the right to participate actively in the political, economic, social and cultural life of the nation "(Article 35).
A new 400 MW power plant generator ready to supply electricity in Phnom Penh in the dry season has gradually arrived (Video inside) (Phnom Penh): Construction of a new 400 MW power plant The location in Lvea Em district, Kandal province, is actively working to complete the plan to release energy into the national grid before mid-2020.
