Minister of Tourism supports 50,000 big motorcycle racing teams to help promote sports, tourism, traffic and environment in Cambodia
After three days, the event closed on the night of December 7, 2019 in Siem Reap under the presidency of Mr. Thong Khon, Minister of Tourism, Mr. Net Pheaktra, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Environment, Mr. Tea Seiha, Governor of Siem Reap, Mr. Oknha Tea Vichet. U Bun Reth represents the motorcycle assembly team and has a representative of the Motor Sports Federation of Cambodia.
Mr. Ou Bun Reth said that on an area of more than 8 hectares in Angkor Khyong Yoo, along the 60-meter road of Siem Reap, the event of Angkor Festivol has gathered tens of thousands of big motorcycle lovers from ASEAN countries. These include: Cambodia, Thailand, Vietnam, Laos, Singapore, Malaysia, China, Sri Lanka, Iran, the Philippines, Indonesia and more.
Mr. Bun Reth said that the event was organized to promote the sport of motor vehicles, especially motorcyclists of all kinds, and to promote traffic safety, ethics in the use of the road together and share technical experience between big motorcycle enthusiasts. Etc., especially to promote tourism in Cambodia to other countries in the region as well as globally.
He added that part of the proceeds from the event will be used to support humanitarian activities, such as the renovation of a school in Siem Reap.
At the same time, Minister Thong Khon said that this event is a diversification of new tourism products that contribute to attracting tourists and sustainable development of tourism, especially to meet the needs of national and international visitors to visit the province. Siem Reap, which is also part of the master plan for integrated development in the Siem Reap-Angkor area and surrounding areas.
The Minister added that through this event, players and tourists also participated in sports and visited Cambodia's heritage sites. What contributes to the attraction in this heritage tourism area is the clean and green, which is an important foundation for tourism development.
While the Royal Government has been carefully preparing the "Siem Reap Tourism Development Master Plan", Minister Thong Khon has encouraged people across the country to continue to participate in maintaining cleanliness, environment, cleanliness and greenery. Because without the participation of the people, the development of tourism will not be successful.
Please be informed that with the closing of the big international motorcycle racing event tonight, Siem Reap will also have another big international event on the 8th tomorrow, the 24th Inter-Half Marathon with national tourists - More than 12,000 international participants from 85 countries participated.
