(Siem Reap): In the near future, Angkor Resort will have a road for tourists to ride a bicycle with a width of 2 meters, 23 kilometers long, from the old checkpoint after Angkor Wat to Kravan Temple south. Banteay Kdei temple turns north of Ta Prohm towards the bridge of Takeo temple.
The main ring road is from Srah Srang to the gate of the pot.
Currently, the 300-meter-long bicycle track, which is still in the pilot project, has been completed and will continue after the plenary meeting of the International Committee for the Coordination of Protection and Conservation of Angkor Resort in mid-December.
APSARA Authority built this road in order to facilitate the traffic for people, students, as well as facilitate traffic for tourism, cycling and reduce traffic congestion and accidents on the main road.
This road is built in the direction parallel to the existing rubber road and about 25 meters away from the rubber road, depending on the location and soil conditions.
While the team is building the bike lane, on the morning of December 7, 2019, a team of experts from the ICC-Angkor Committee, or ADHOC, visited the bike lane construction site in the Angkor resort.
During the visit, the experts praised the initiative of the APSARA Authority to prepare the bike path and even considered the safety of safe travel for people, students, tourists as well as Pay close attention to environmental issues.
