Mr. Keo Remy: Cambodians have all the rights under the shadow of peace and political stability
(Phnom Penh): Mr. Keo Remy, Minister Delegate to the Prime Minister and Chairman of the Cambodian Human Rights Committee, said that now all Cambodians live happily and enjoy all the rights protected by law under the shadow of peace. Political stability brought by Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia.
On that occasion, he also recalled the tragedy of the fire of war, which deprived all people of all rights and suffered physical and mental torture, especially men, women, young and old were killed. Most brutally.
"The right to life is the first and foremost human right for humanity around the world, so the leaders of many countries declare December 10 every year as Human Rights Day," he said. People in Cambodia, if we look at the past, are suffering because of the flames of war, the people have lost all their rights, only in the Techo era did the Cambodian people get all their rights.
Mr. Keo Remy added that Cambodia, the leaders and the people of Cambodia have a sacred sword that can not be forgotten, the right to life, which is the foundation and the first right brought by Samdech Techo Hun Sen and The government leaders he has strived to sacrifice fresh flesh, blood and sacrifice for the cause of the nation, especially demanding respect for human rights.
Cracked down on 2 cockfighting venues in Kampong Cham and Cheung Prey districts, confiscated 48 motorcycles and a car
(Kampong Cham): Police in Kampong Cham province on December 7, 2019, launched an operation to crack down on a cockfighting betting place in the forest behind Boeung Bassac village, Sangkat Sambour Meas, Kampong Cham city and at the forest burial ground. Boeung Chroy, So Tip Commune, Cheung Prey District, Kampong Cham Province.
Kampong Cham Provincial Police Commissioner Major General Em Kosal said that the operation took place immediately after receiving information from the people and he ordered the Kampong Cham Municipal Police Inspectorate to cooperate with the four police forces and the intervention office led by him. Lieutenant Colonel Ing Bun, Police Inspector of Kampong Cham City.
Currently, the above exhibits have been brought by the competent authorities to be kept at the Police Inspectorate of Kampong Cham City to research and build the case according to the procedure.
As for the crackdown in Cheung Prey district, as a result of the difficult road situation from the village, when the police arrived, the players fled, leaving behind some exhibits, including 27 motorcycles and 2 roosters. Currently, the above exhibits have been taken and stored at the Cheung Prey District Police Inspectorate for further research.
(Phnom Penh): Khmer people who always like to make prahok for food, in a few days start to rush to make prahok fish as usual last year along the Tonle Sap River in Kampong Lang commune, Ponhea Leu district, Kandal province.
At the prahok cutting site, which is held every year, a large number of people are observed to cut prahok by means of cars, motorbikes and tuk-tuks. However, this year's prahok fish is more expensive than previous years, with small fish costing 2,000 riel per kilo and slightly larger fish costing up to 7,000 or 8,000 riel.
The rising price of prahok fish has caused some people to complain and others to reduce the weight of the prahok fish.
On December 7, 2019, Mr. Veng Sakhon, Minister of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries, inspected the fishing in each dike. The minister pointed out that this year's fish are scarcer than last year because in this year's rainy season, the water rises slowly and when it recedes, which makes it less spawning.
According to Minister Veng Sakhon, this fish shortage is the reason why the price of prahok this year is higher than last year.
