China allows 18 more Cambodian rice mills to process, process and supply directly to Chinese market
(Phnom Penh): The Chinese government, through the General Administration of Quality Inspection and Inspection (AQSIQ), has just decided to authorize 18 more Cambodian companies and mills to grind, process and supply rice directly to the market. Its country.
The addition of 18 rice mills brings the total number of Cambodian rice mills with export rights to China to 44, reaching a quota of 400,000 tonnes of rice exported to China. Give to Cambodia.
The Chinese Embassy in Cambodia considers that granting additional rights to the 18 participating companies will help achieve the goal of exporting 400,000 tons of rice to China every year.
The Cambodian Rice Federation congratulates China's AQSIQ administration on its decision to add 18 new rice mills to the right to supply directly to China. A total of 44 mills have been licensed.
At the same time, the Rice Federation of Cambodia would like to thank the General Department of Agriculture of the Ministry of Agriculture, Forestry and Agriculture and all professional officials who have worked hard and encouraged cooperation with Chinese professional institutions to put more mills. Get this good result.
The Rice Federation considers that through this additional decision, it will help the Cambodian rice sector to be more able to increase the amount of milling supply to China.
Please be informed that in the first 11 months of 2019, Cambodia exported more than 510,000 tons of rice to 60 countries and regions in the world, and China is still the largest import market. Cambodia exported more than 200,000 tons of rice to China, an increase of 53% compared to the same period in 2018. Construction site to open at the end of 2019
