(Phnom Penh): Dr. Chhiv Yi Xian, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Foreign Affairs and International Cooperation, President of the Institute of Diplomacy and International Relations, affirmed that the current Cambodian-Chinese relations are friendly, cooperative, traditional, historical and strategic in all aspects. Equally, there is mutual trust for the common good.
This confirmation by Dr. Chhiv Yi Xian was made on December 7, 2019, when he, together with Dr. Sok Touch, President of the Royal Academy of Cambodia and Mr. Gao Piyong, Vice President of the Royal Academy of Social Sciences of China, opened the cooperation. The first annual Cambodia-China operation on "Comprehensive Strategic Partnership Towards a Community with a Future Together, Let Us Grow Together in Siem Reap"
He said that Cambodia has adhered to the one-China policy, while China has strictly respected Cambodia's independence and sovereignty.
