The Japanese Ambassador to Cambodia expressed his admiration: "I came to Cambodia as an Ambassador on September 1, 2019 and my life here has been three months. "I visited Phnom Penh 17 years ago, but the landscape of Phnom Penh today is very different from then, and I am very impressed with Cambodia's remarkable economic development."
On that occasion, Mr. Mikami Masahiro said that under this economic development, Cambodians are visiting Japan more than ever. As you know, Japan has four seasons: spring, summer, autumn and winter. He said that many Cambodians, in particular, visit Japan during the cherry blossom season.
According to Mikami Masahiro, in March and April, this year's sakura season, about 8,000 Cambodians visited Japan, an increase of 36% compared to the same period last year. In this year's Japan Tourism Fair, we have put together two sakura trees to serve as a photo booth for visitors, so you can experience the beauty of Japanese sakura flowers here in Phnom Penh.
