(Central): A fire broke out at a cigarette factory due to an explosion of a drying machine in contact with a nearby aromatic gasoline, which caused the fire to intensify, damaging a factory and other equipment.
This incident happened at 13:20 at the cigarette factory in Bonna village, Preah Puth commune, Kandal Steung district, Kandal province on December 6, 2019.
Sources from the police said that the fire did not injure any workers, because at the time of the incident, all the staff ran out in time, while the fire truck also rushed to intervene. From receiving information on this fire case.
The source added that the fire brigade involved:
* Kandal Stung District Fire Brigade and 1 fire truck * Kandal Provincial Fire Brigade and 3 fire trucks * Phnom Penh Fire Brigade and 4 fire trucks * Ministry of Interior Fire Brigade and Fire Truck 5 units. A total of 13 fire trucks.
Preliminary information on the assessment of the damage included: a factory fire, about 100 meters long and 50 meters wide, 100 percent zinc roof, and a large number of equipment, but not yet clear.
