Ministry of Environment launches measures to prevent and prevent wildfires in protected areas and biodiversity corridors
(Phnom Penh): The Ministry of Environment on December 6, 2019 issued a notification setting out measures to prevent and prevent wildfires in protected areas and biodiversity corridors that often occur in Cambodia every year, especially In the dry season.
The Ministry of Environment notes that the main causes of forest fires during the dry season are: deforestation, deforestation for agricultural crops, nomadic farming, and new settlements. And forest fires to catch wildlife and human neglect.
In order to prevent and prevent wildfires, the Ministry of Environment would like to instruct the sub-national administrative units of the Department of Environment, the competent authorities, including local communities and all stakeholders to implement the following measures:
1: Educate, disseminate and advise people to be very careful about using fire as a means of cooking, burning grass and forest, intercepting animals and harvesting non-timber forest products.
2. Prevent deforestation, clearing, burning of forests and flooded forests for other purposes, which are clearly illegal activities and cause forest fires, flooded forests and spread to people's homes, public administration areas and physical infrastructure in In and around protected areas and biodiversity corridors.
3: Be very careful in using fire as a means to burn debris in protected areas and biodiversity corridors.
4: Prepare a railway to prevent the fire from spreading from one place to another.
5. Capital-Provincial Departments of Environment shall instruct the relevant parties to implement appropriate technical measures that can ensure the safety of wildfires by extinguishing all fires as necessary before leaving the fire place.
6. Capital-Provincial Departments of Environment and sub-national authorities must take measures to maintain good water supply to supply for daily use and use in case of wildfire.
7: In case of severe wildfires, the relevant authorities should take immediate action to prevent it by declaring a state of emergency by requesting the Capital-Provincial Unity Command to direct the use of mixed forces, including people, communities, monks, civil servants. The armed forces and all those involved in the base work together to effectively prevent and extinguish wildfires.
