The complaint filed by Mr. Kem Sokha's lawyers comes after the Phnom Penh Municipal Court on December 2, 2019 decided to send the case of "Peace with Foreigners" by Mr. Kem Sokha, former President of the Cambodia National Rescue Party, to trial. After closing the investigation in mid-November.
Lim Chea Vutha: Regarding the appeal of Mr. Kem Sokha's lawyers against the order to send the case to the trial of the Phnom Penh Municipal Court, what is the opinion of the Royal Government's lawyers who are the representatives of the Civil Parties in this case?
Lim Chea Vutha: Did this appeal lead to the suspension of court proceedings related to Kem Sokha's case?
Defendants and Civil Party lawyers believe that the Defense for Kem Sokha should set aside time to study the case file and to seek acquittal on the charges that the Prosecutor and Investigating Judge used for two years. To research and gather evidence of this serious burden, and it is better to make such an illegal appeal.
Defense lawyers and civil party representatives found that the investigating judge had strong evidence that Kem Sokha had committed a peace offense with a foreign state under Article 443 of the Criminal Code of the Kingdom of Cambodia. We support the decision of the investigating judge to send this case to trial and be prepared to present this case before the court at the next hearing.
Please be informed that on November 10, 2019, the Phnom Penh Municipal Court issued a press release deciding to place Mr. Kem Sokha under the same judicial supervision, but with the relaxation of the official inspection conditions.
The release of duty is now due to the fact that the accused, Mr. Kem Sokha, in the past has properly complied with the obligation to be placed under judicial supervision, as well as good cooperation in the court proceedings. In particular, the health problems of the accused who need to be examined and treated. Defendant Kem Sokha was remanded in custody by the investigating judge with the following obligations:
A: Do not go outside the territory of the Kingdom of Cambodia. B: Do not engage in political activities. C: Must respond to summons from all authorities.
On December 2, 2019, the Investigating Judge of the Phnom Penh Municipal Court, Mr. Ky Rithy, decided to send the case of "Peace with Foreigners" of Mr. Kem Sokha, former President of the National Rescue Party to trial after closing The investigation took place on November 15, 2019.
