International Expert: Angkor Wat North Pond Must Be Completely Renovated
(Siem Reap): International experts of the ICC-Angkor Committee assess that the implementation of the project to renovate the structure of the northern pond of Angkor Wat is a lot of research and will be repaired in accordance with the technical specifications, but in the future the pond This must be completely repaired.
The renovation is to prevent damage from the inflow of soil into the pond structure.
This assessment was made while the international team of ICC-Angkor Committee monitored the implementation of the project to renovate the northern pond structure of Angkor temple on the morning of December 4, 2019.
Mr. Srun Tech, Head of North Pond Rehabilitation Project, said that it is a matter of great pride for Cambodian experts to carry out the restoration, research and strengthening of the structure of the pond structure in accordance with the recommendations of international experts, including Technically to understand the structure of the pond to avoid losing the value of the ancient pond and the architectural structure of the pond.
International experts also requested the APSARA Authority to pay more attention to researching the history of the pond, including expanding the repair site and closing it to tourists to allow access to the research and repair team easily.
Mr. Srun Tech said that the project to repair the northern pond of Angkor Wat, which started piloting on a 15-meter length and began studying excavations from March 2019 until now, has been completed, including the preparation Decorate the pond by planting grass.
In the past, this northern pond was important for the benefit of the gods, but now it is a beautiful place for tourists to take pictures of the top of Angkor Wat that reflects in the water.
