(Pursat): The military police in cooperation with the Kandieng District Unity Command raided a house, found many wild animals and confiscated them to be released back into the Pursat River.
The above transaction took place at 2:00 pm on December 5, 2019, yesterday at the point of sale of non-fishery products in Thla Ampil village, Sre Sdok commune, Kandieng district, Pursat province.
Mr. Chhay Kimmong, Governor of Kandeang District and Chairman of the District Unity Command, said that the operation was coordinated by the Provincial Prosecutor of the Provincial Court to buy and sell non-fishery products owned by Kong Kunna. 30-year-old Cambodian man and his wife Horn Sina, 34-year-old Cambodian man currently living in the commune.
The district governor said that during the operation to suppress the above case, the force confiscated 17 exhibits, including: 12 turtles weighing 12.04 kg, 8 endangered snakes weighing 12 kg, and 5 vipers. Weighing 07.30 kg, 1 cat weighing 9 kg, snake fish weighing 26 kg and 2 vipers totaling 58.06 kg.
For the couple, the owner of the house was handed over to the professional officer of Kandeang Fisheries Administration Sangkat to continue the procedure, while all the wildlife exhibits were released into the Pursat River.
