(Preah Vihear): On the morning of December 6, 2019, Preah Vihear Provincial Administration celebrated the World AIDS Day and called for non-discrimination against people living with HIV and the reduction of HIV / AIDS. .
The ceremony was attended by Mr. Kor Som Bunsoeut, Acting Provincial Governor, Mr. Prak Sovann, Deputy Governor of Preah Vihear Province, and Mr. Samleang Try, Deputy Chairman of the Provincial Committee of the Cambodian Red Cross, Dr. Kuong Lo, Director of Preah Vihear Provincial Health Department and Director of the Department. Units around the province, the three armed forces, youth, scouts, students and many more people.
After listening to the speech of Samdech Kittipritthbandit Bun Rany Hun Sen, President of the Cambodian Red Cross, which was read by Mr. Samleang Try, Dr. Kuong Lo said that on December 1, every year, the world celebrates Celebrate AIDS Day, especially in Cambodia, in all provinces, this ceremony is just a different day from province to province.
He said that the purpose of celebrating the World AIDS Day is to show the public that the world can prevent AIDS, especially Cambodia, which can reduce the spread of infection. AIDS up to 0.06% is due to the support of all levels from all development partners from all institutions involved in the fight against HIV, the results have been achieved to this day.
Kuong Lo said the day was a celebration of the support of all partners involved in preventing the spread of HIV. Another purpose is to emphasize that people living with HIV are not isolated, there is no discrimination against people living with HIV, people living with HIV can work like people who do not have the same HIV.
Mr. Ko Bunsoeut said that the situation of the HIV epidemic in Cambodia is still fragile, if neglected, the disease could re-emerge. He said that all people living with HIV are destined to receive global funding because all medical expenses as well as prevention provided by the health department are free.
He said that the Royal Government of Cambodia under the leadership of Samdech Techo Hun Sen as Prime Minister has tried to increase the budget to contribute to the eradication of HIV / AIDS. In Cambodia, out of a population of 16 million, there are nearly 70,000 people living with HIV.
