Citizens and students affected by roadblocks in Rohat Teuk commune, Banteay Meanchey province, forced to walk on water because there is no sidewalk, the district governor declared protection to the end for the victims
(Banteay Meanchey): Due to the ancient violation of the road by a woman in Khtom Chrum village, Rohat Teuk commune, Mongkul Borei district, Banteay Meanchey province, some victims have been forced to rely on this road to get in and out of their houses. And especially sadly, young students are forced to walk on water during the rainy season and walk under their houses to go to school (picture below).
This kind of view was also expressed by the Governor of Mongkul Borei District, Banteay Meanchey Province, Mr. Rath Da Sinang, who is the joint supervisor of the local people, expressed his great sympathy. The house is crossed because a road since ancient times, more than 100 meters long and 4 meters wide, has been completely violated and closed.
The district governor, who came out in defense of the victims, nodded his head as the issue was not yet addressed to his citizens because someone was behind it, as well as the decision to block the road of another deputy prosecutor, but he will Try to solve for the people.
Victims who have no way to walk stated that they would be willing to go to jail if they were arrested for reopening the road because they said that if there was no way to get home, they would not be able to live. How? Especially when the child is sick, on the night of December 6, 2019, a child with dengue fever was forced to walk through the basement to take the child to the hospital.
The governor of Mongkul Borei district also came out to fully protect the victims. "This is a sad picture of students walking under their house and walking through the water during the rainy season," he said. "In this case, I am willing to protect these victims until the end until there is real justice," he said.
Mongkul Borei district governor Roth Dasinang acknowledged that some victims would have no way out of their homes if the ancient road was closed. He also cited the example that "If any of the victims are dead, it is not possible to carry or remove the body from the house because the road used to be completely violated." .
The district governor confirmed that he had solved the case of road violation since the beginning of 2019, by opening the road and repairing the road so that the victims could travel, but later, the violator complained to Suddenly, on December 3, 2019, a deputy provincial prosecutor led officers and police to the road and closed it.
The district governor expressed his sympathy for the victims if the road was closed and they could not leave their homes because the rapist had previously agreed to open a detour and he had prepared the bulldozers. The rapist refused to open the detour.
Some observers have questioned whether this is an ancient road, and that local people often travel to and from their homes and find that there is a real violation. Why do the authorities and officials not dare to release the iron fist to reopen, leaving the rapist and those behind it more powerful, or the authorities, which are the staff of the Royal Government, fear the merits and power of corrupt people?
One of the victims had a heart attack and was taken to hospital because she could not get out of the house.
