Chip Mong Inc. Cement Plant Inaugurates Industrial Waste Processing Project
(Touk Meas, Kampot Province): On December 05, 2019, Chip Mong Cement (CMIC) Cement Factory, one of the largest cement factories in Cambodia and one of the leading in the region, held a project inauguration ceremony. Recycling industrial waste in Chip Mong Inc. Cement Factory located in Banteay Meas District, Kampot Province in the presence of the Minister of Environment, the Governor of Kampot and the project partners, as well as many other distinguished guests.
Waste management has become a major issue in the Kingdom of Cambodia, with industrial waste management a challenge at a time of rapid economic growth. Chip Mong Inc.'s waste recycling project was established with the aim of recycling industrial waste in an environmentally friendly manner and with the full support of the Ministry of Environment.
Industrialists are showing greater responsibility when it comes to environmental responsibility. The new waste management is part of Chipmung Inc. Cement's commitment to promoting a cleaner environment at a time when the world is facing the challenges of global warming and climate change.
In addition, CMIC has demonstrated its commitment to the sustainable development of the cement industry. The waste recycling project has the capacity to process about 10 tons of industrial waste per hour, or about 7,000 tons per month. This waste management includes the collection and processing of solid waste that will provide solutions to garment and footwear factories, as well as other sectors.
