Samdech Krala Hom Sar Kheng Closes the National Workshop on NCDD's Action Plan and Budget 2020
(Phnom Penh): Samdech Krala Hom Sar Kheng, Deputy Prime Minister, Minister of Interior and Chairman of the National Committee for Sub-National Democratic Development (NCDD) on the afternoon of December 5, 2019. Closing the National Workshop on Action Plan and Budget 2020
The national workshop was held at the Ministry of Interior with the participation of nearly 500 representatives from ministries, sub-national administrative institutions, development partners and relevant civil society organizations.
Mr. Pich Bunthen, Minister of Public Works, said at the opening of the seminar this morning that the preliminary draft of the action plan and budget for 2020 was based on a total budget of more than 3.5 trillion riels or more. Nearly 900 million US dollars, of which the state budget is about 95% and the contribution from development partners is more than 5%.
The budget for the sub-national administration is more than 3.4 trillion riels or more than 855 million US dollars. Compared to 2019, the budget of the sub-national administration in 2020 will increase by nearly 1.1 trillion riels or more than 276 million US dollars due to the increase in the contribution of the state budget to the commune fund. Municipal funds and the creation of other sources of revenue for sub-national administrations.
