Cambodia, Vietnam to hold first joint disaster relief exercise in mid-December in Svay Rieng
(Phnom Penh): General Moeng Samphan, Secretary of State of the Ministry of National Defense and Chairman of the Cambodia-Vietnam Disaster Relief Training Commission, confirmed that more than 1,000 Cambodian and Vietnamese troops will conduct joint disaster relief exercises on December 18, 2019, in order to increase the capacity to rescue the people of the two countries affected by the disaster by any factor.
This statement was made by General Moeng Samphan on the morning of December 5, 2019, on the occasion that the General was invited to chair a meeting to prepare for the Cambodian-Vietnamese Army training exercise at the Ministry of National Defense.
According to General Moeng Samphan, the "Disaster Relief" exercise between the Cambodian and Vietnamese armies was conducted for the first time on Cambodian territory in Suosdey commune, Chantrea district, Svay Rieng province. On the border of Long An province, Vietnam.
The general said that the training exercise with the Vietnamese side is to prepare joint forces to help people along the border of the two countries when they face natural disasters or disasters for any reason. Up that.
