Enhancing relations between Cambodians and Chinese people under the Belt and Road Strategy
(Phnom Penh): If we look back to the past and take the geography, history and culture recorded by the Chinese to reveal, we will understand the role and importance of the people-to-people relations of our two nations, Cambodia. And China.
If we use Kaing Thai's arguments in the Funan period and the biography of Chiv Ta Kwan in the Angkorian period, we will know more clearly that the relationship between the Cambodian people and the Chinese people is no less than 2,000 years old.
Xi Jinping, President of the People's Republic of China, said at a conference on the Belt and Road Initiative in Beijing on May 14, 2017, "More than 2,000 years ago, our ancestors traveled through grasslands and fields. The vast expanse of sand formed the transit route between Asia, Europe, and Africa, known as the Silk Road today.
Our ancestors, who sailed the perilous seas, formed several sea lanes connecting the east to the west, called the Silk Road. The ancient Silk Road, which covers both the Silk Road on land and the Silk Road on the sea, has opened the way for friendly connections between nations, forming a great historical chapter of human progress. .
Xi Jinping said in a speech on April 17, 2016 in Beijing at the "Belt and Road Initiative" that "we should promote closer people-to-people contacts, and raise the spirit of the Silk Road." "Go ahead and promote cultural change as well as mutual learning."
By: Dr. Chea Monirith, President of the Cambodia-China Progress Researchers Association Experts: Traffic Accidents and Garbage in Phnom Penh Still a Challenge
According to Dr. Chan Sampov, Vice President of the Royal Academy of Cambodia, the current "congestion and road accidents and waste management" is a universally recognized challenge for all of us. In other words, the whole world has spent a lot of money in vain for the above issues, obviously in developing countries, including Cambodia.
During the last five years, the average amount of garbage was more than 2,800 tons per day, an increase of around 10 percent to 13 percent per year, he said. The amount of garbage in the city is projected to increase further, which requires effective management measures.
Lt. Gen. Chev Hak, Deputy Commissioner of the Phnom Penh Municipal Police Commissioner for Traffic Planning, said that the current traffic congestion in Phnom Penh is caused by a number of factors such as the increase in people and vehicles of all kinds has increased dramatically. Which also causes traffic congestion in Phnom Penh.
The lieutenant general confirmed that the construction of the factory to hold various ceremonies on the chest that does not listen to the call of the Phnom Penh administration, as well as the construction of high-rise buildings that require large trucks to enter Phnom Penh. Contribute to causing traffic congestion. He said that without the participation of traffic police officers to protect the districts, Phnom Penh will face serious traffic congestion.
The call from the Ministry of Agriculture was made during a press conference on "Mango Varieties and International Markets" at the Council of Ministers on the morning of December 5.
He said that both the General Department of Agriculture and the Ministry of Agriculture had already issued a notice calling for mango plantation owners to register with the General Department of Agriculture, but the number of registrants is still small, only about two or three farms. It may be difficult to export to China or other countries, as in the case of rice mills that had to export rice to China in the past.
Mr. Ngin Chhay instructed all mango growers and farmers to cooperate with the General Department of Agriculture as well as the Provincial Department of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries in all provinces to strictly implement the technical rules, otherwise the mango plantations of farmers will not Can register for export to China and other countries.
"Please understand that if you do not come to register, you can not export," he said. If your cultivation does not comply with technical and phytosanitary rules, it cannot be exported. "I do not force it on your decision, if you want to export to China, you have to respect China's conditions to export."
The senior official confirmed that for the market to export mangoes to South Korea, Cambodia has completed negotiations that can allow Cambodia to export from now on, while China expects to export. In April 2020, the negotiations are coming to an end in the near future.
At the same time, Mr. Ngin Chhay called on the private sector and development partners to invest in infrastructure processing and disinfection for mangoes so that Cambodia can achieve the goal of exporting mangoes at least 500,000 to 600,000 tons. 2023.
Please be informed that Cambodian mangoes are currently exported to Vietnam, Thailand, Singapore, France and Russia. In the first 11 months of 2019, Cambodia exported nearly 50,000 tons of mangoes. Australia Continues to Strengthen Cooperation with Cambodian Parliament and Government
(Phnom Penh): On the occasion of courtesy call and farewell to Samdech Akka Moha Ponhea Chakrei Heng Samrin, President of the National Assembly, Ms. Angela Corcoran, Ambassador of Australia to Cambodia, who is out of office, expressed her congratulations to Good cooperation between Cambodia and Australia, both in the legislative and executive branches, and Australia will continue to support Cambodia's development going forward.
At a meeting at the National Assembly on the morning of Thursday, December 5, 2019, Ms. Angela Kokoran informed the President of the National Assembly that since 1993, Australia has contributed to the development of Cambodia in many areas such as education, agriculture, cleaning. Mines and so on. Cambodia and Australia have good cooperation in the fight against terrorism, such as human trafficking and drugs.
The Ambassador pointed out that since 1994, 2,900 Cambodian students have studied in Australia. Of these, 850 Cambodian students received scholarships from the Australian Government. The two countries' trade volume reached 1.3 billion US dollars.
The President of the National Assembly hopes that even though Ms. Angela Kokoran has completed her mission in Cambodia, she will always have good feelings and good relations with the Cambodian people.
