Ministry of Public Works Considers Important Road Accident Data Collection Important
(Phnom Penh): After holding a workshop on improving the quality of road accident data collection, the Ministry of Public Works and Transport considers this road traffic data collection to be very important to find measures to prevent deaths and injuries due to road accidents.
Dr. Kol Hero, Director of Health Protection, said at the closing ceremony of the seminar on improving the quality of road traffic data collection on the afternoon of December 3, 2019 that the Ministry of Public Works and Transport considers road traffic data collection. Land in Cambodia is the key data to find measures to prevent deaths and injuries from traffic accidents in Cambodia.
He said that the workshop was organized to raise awareness about the collection of road accident data to be more effective.
He said that the current traffic accident situation has a tendency to increase the number of deaths and injuries caused by speeding, overtaking in dangerous situations, disrespecting the right of way, driving under the influence of alcohol and so on. Which leads to an increase in orphans, widows, the disabled, various tragedies and many consequences in Cambodian society.
He added that in order to reduce traffic accidents, it is necessary to have an effective action plan that is appropriate to the situation of the accident, and quality traffic accident data is an important input in building an effective action plan. On the other hand, we can also monitor and predict the danger situation as well as the effectiveness of the plan put forward through this important data.
"I would like to ask the members of the whole workshop to participate in the discussion to promote better road accident data collection," he said.
On this occasion, he also thanked UNDP for supporting the organization of this important workshop and considered that this activity shows the commitment to contribute to the Royal Government and the Committee. National Road Traffic Safety in Preventing and Reducing Traffic Accidents in Cambodia.
Please be informed that the two-day workshop was organized by the General Secretariat of the National Committee for Road Safety and the General Commission of the National Police under the auspices of UNDP. Samdech Techo Hun Sen will officially inaugurate the model market. Cambodia's first border market in Tbong Khmum province worth about 2 million dollars at the end of December
The meeting was also attended by Mr. Ben Rath, Provincial Police Commissioner, Mr. Va Sarith, Commander of the Provincial Gendarmerie, as well as the District Governor, Director of Departments around the province.
Mr. Hak Sok Makara stated that this market is the first model market on the Cambodia-Vietnam border, starting construction on January 16, 2018, which will be officially inaugurated on December 24, 2019. This page under the high presidency of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia after construction for about 23 months.
He added that the market was built on an area of nearly 2 hectares (19,628 square meters) with a market area of 1,600 square meters, as well as administrative buildings, warehouses, bathrooms, sewers and water storage. Original.
The Deputy Governor expressed strong hope that this market will serve the benefits for the people of Cambodia and for the sale of goods of the people of the two countries, especially to address the challenges and trade barriers that often block traffic. Goods and products on the Cambodian-Vietnamese border.
It should be reminded that this market was first approved in 2013 and was re-implemented in 2016 on an area of 19,628 square meters in the Tbong Khmum Special Economic Zone with a total investment of 44,761,411 Vietnam VND, or about 2 million US dollars, with assistance from the Vietnamese government.
