World AIDS Day, December 1, 2019 in Kampot under the theme "Together, a national trend to prevent the spread of HIV and AIDS"
(Kampot): Mr. Sim Kimsen, Deputy Director of the National AIDS Authority and Mr. Chiao Tai, Provincial Governor and Chairman of the Kampot Provincial Committee of the Cambodian Red Cross, on the afternoon of December 4, 2019, led about 1,000 stakeholders. World AIDS Day, December 1, 2019 under the theme "Together, a national trend to prevent the spread of HIV and AIDS" at Kampot Provincial Conference Hall.
Dr. Nhea Bunthorn, Director of the Provincial Health Department and Deputy Chairman of the Provincial AIDS Committee, said that currently, with the efforts of the Cambodian government as well as relevant departments, civil society and development partners have increased the rate of infection. AIDS is declining among the general population from 15 to 49 years old, from 2.8 percent in 1997 to 0.6 percent in 2018 in Kampot.
On that occasion, Mr. Sim Kimsen and Governor of Chiao Tai Province read out the speech of Samdech Kittipritthbandit Bun Rany Hun Sen, President of the Cambodian Red Cross, National Outstanding Leader of the Asia-Pacific Leadership Forum on HIV / AIDS in Cambodia. .
According to the report of the National AIDS Authority in 2019, Cambodia can reduce the number of new HIV infections from 2,300 in 2010 to about 880 in 2019, while the provision of antiretroviral drugs can It has reached 99% of the HIV-positive people in need of antiretroviral drugs and medical care, and as a result, the death rate from HIV / AIDS is declining every year.
