SECC Director General: As of October 2019, the investment volume in the derivatives market has exceeded 100 million USD, a new company in the derivatives marketing sector has been launched.
The emphasis was made on the occasion of Mr. Sou Socheat's inauguration and obtaining a license from the central counterpart of Global Liquidty Co., Ltd. under the presence of Deputy Prime Minister Yim Chhay Ly and Chairman of the Council for Agricultural Development and Rehabilitation. Rural on December 3, 2019.
Speaking at the ceremony, Mr. Sou Socheat said that through the clear vision and the right direction of the Securities and Exchange Commission of Cambodia, with Deputy Prime Minister Aun Porn Moniroth as the Chairman of the Securities and Exchange Commission of Cambodia, the size of investment in the derivatives market in 2019. Has increased significantly.
Mr. Sou Socheat stated that "during 2017, the amount of investment was only about 4 million US dollars. In contrast, in 2018, this size will increase to 82 million US dollars, a percentage of about 2,000%. In addition, as of October 2019, the investment has increased to more than 100 million US dollars.
By licensing its central counterparty to Global QDTX Chheng, another trading platform in the Cambodian derivatives market, Mr. Sou Socheat is hopeful and expects that the cash flow of investment in this market will continue to grow significantly. In addition, in 2020 and will continue to contribute to supporting Cambodia's economic growth.
Mr. Sou Socheat believes that Global Qty Co., Ltd. will continue to adhere to and abide by the license terms as well as other relevant requirements issued by the Securities and Exchange Commission of Cambodia, which is the regulator of the entire securities sector. Attract the trust of investors, which is the key to the success of the company's business.
San Chan Kompheak, CEO of Global QDT Trading (GLX), said the derivatives brokerage business has been booming in Cambodia. Therefore, the presence of Global QD Co., Ltd. is most suitable to establish a closer relationship between investors and provide better services to customers and business partners.
Mr. San Chankompheak added that these can help promote financial markets as well as derivatives trading in the securities sector in Cambodia to better manage risk for market participants, as well as provide convenience and transparency of trade.
The CEO added that GLX is very proud to be licensed to operate as one of the top five counterparties in Cambodia to provide support to existing derivatives brokers. And newly established companies.
Mr. San Chankompheak emphasized that GLX's unique vision is to transform the world's largest financial market through a process of high reliability, transparency, clarity and accuracy. GLX will continue to bring new technologies that can support the brokerage business, derivatives and partner clients.
