(Phnom Penh): Deputy Prime Minister Ke Kim Yan, Chairman of the National Authority for Combating Drugs, stated that all commune / sangkat authorities must have their own authority to manage the drug problem in their local area in accordance with the strategic plan. National submitted.
This confirmation by Deputy Prime Minister Ke Kim Yan was made this morning, December 4, 2019, on the occasion of the meeting to review and discuss the draft five-year national plan on drug control 2019-2023. Invitation from 25 ministries and institutions involved in the campaign against illegal drugs at the Ministry of Interior.
At this point, Deputy Prime Minister Ke Kim Yan pointed out that this is a long-term key vision for one term to ensure that the commune authorities take ownership of the local drug crackdown campaign. If the commune / sangkat authorities cannot be self-sufficient, the drug suppression strategy will fail, which is only theoretical but not practical.
Deputy Prime Minister Ke Kim Yan added that education in the Ministry of Education, which has already set out a national policy, requires a school to have a room to be a place for drug education for young people or the community as a whole. This activity is in the drug control campaign 2019-2023 to get good results.
