Minister of Labor Restricts Enterprise Hospitals to Have Adequate Medical Equipment and Health Workers
(Phnom Penh): All hospitals in the establishment must ensure good operation, adequate medical equipment and medical staff to work regularly as scheduled and professional, this is the message of Mr. Ith Sam Heng, Minister of Labor and Vocational Training Bio appeals to the owners of all enterprises in Cambodia.
Mr. Ith Sam Heng Yang's announcement was made at the opening ceremony of the workshop to share experiences on the establishment of the Enterprise Hospital at the Phnom Penh Hotel on December 4, 2019.
To ensure the safety and health of workers in the enterprise, Mr. Ith Sam Heng appealed as follows:
* For employers:
1. Prepare hospitals, enterprises and establishments appropriately and correctly in accordance with the rules and regulations set out in the Labor Law and the relevant relevant regulations, especially Joint Proclamation No. 330 and 139.
2. Ensure that the hospital, enterprise, and establishment are in good working condition, have adequate medical equipment, and have regular health workers on schedule.
3. Provide and maintain a clean and safe workplace.
4. Develop effective preventive measures or measures to prevent any risks.
5. Ensure that workers receive and use labor protection equipment properly and instruct them to take good care of it.
6. Educate and explain to workers to know the new rules or regulations issued by the competent institutions, especially the Ministry in charge of labor related to occupational safety and health of workers.
7. Inform the worker's illness and work accident to the National Social Security Fund in a timely manner and send him to the hospital as soon as possible according to the procedures and procedures of the National Social Security Fund.
* For workers to participate in the implementation and dissemination of rules and regulations related to occupational health and safety to be highly effective.
On behalf of the Ministry of Labor and Vocational Training, as well as the Royal Government, Minister Ith Sam Heng requested employers to better implement this guideline in setting up hospitals and health and safety services, which are the needs of workers in Its establishment.
