The Royal Government is preparing a plan for the multi-modal transportation system in Cambodia 2021-2030
This meeting was held on December 3, 2019 at the Ministry of Economy and Finance, with the participation of Senior Minister Sun Chanthol, Minister of Public Works and Transport, Mr. Say Sam Al, Minister of Environment, Mr. Sok Chenda Sophea, Minister Delegates accompanying the Prime Minister, senior leaders and technical officers of relevant ministries and institutions.
This "Draft Master Plan" is designed to promote Cambodia's connectivity, reduce transport and logistics costs, promote Cambodia's integration into the region and the world, increase competitiveness and diversify the Cambodian economy to ensure the sustainability of Cambodia. Economic growth at the peak level.
At the same time, the Royal Government of Cambodia also sees another important role of this master plan as a guide document, as well as defining the overall framework of the plan for the development of transportation infrastructure by all means, including the logistics system that will help increase the efficiency of public investment. Transportation infrastructure in Cambodia as well.
Through the presentation of the technical working group, the meeting highly appreciated the "draft master plan" that is comprehensive, cellular and consistent between the necessary means of transport, especially highly responsive to the current Cambodian facilities and The future.
This "Draft Master Plan" provides an alternative measure that by 2030, land transport will remain a priority for Cambodia, but focus on quality over quantity and continue to develop air transport, sea transport. And rehabilitate and strengthen infrastructure and transport links, railways and waterways.
The meeting also provided recommendations and guidance for additional input in improving this "Draft Master Plan", which the Technical Working Group will conduct further studies.
Dr. Aun Porn Moniroth, Deputy Prime Minister and Chairman of the Meeting, expressed his deep appreciation and deep gratitude to the Chinese technical team led by She Xiangyun, Project Director for the "Draft Master Plan" Efforts. All sides also thanked their Chinese friends for their financial support of the study.
