New road infrastructure is being built and expanded due to traffic congestion on roads like in other Southeast Asian capitals. This is because the living standards of the people have improved as Cambodia has achieved economic growth of 7.7% over the past two decades, which allows Cambodia to reduce the poverty rate to only 10% per year. 2018.
