Mr. Khuong Sreng told the AIMF General Assembly that due to the victorious policy of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Cambodia ended the long war and developed as it is now.
(Phnom Penh): In the 39th Annual General Assembly and the 40th Anniversary of the International Association of French-Speaking Mayors, hosted by Cambodia this morning, December 4, 2019, Mr. Khuong Sreng, Governor of Phnom Penh He said that due to the victorious policy of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Cambodia successfully ended the chronic war and developed as it is today.
Speaking in French, Mr. Khuong Sreng emphasized that in the 1970s, Phnom Penh suffered a bombing war and fell into a war between Cambodians and Cambodians. The Khmer Rouge genocidal regime lasted for almost three years, from 1975 to 1979, making the Cambodian capital an uninhabited ghost town with no respect for human rights.
The Governor of Phnom Penh continued that after the day of liberation on January 7, 1979, Phnom Penh was gradually restored in accordance with the evolution of each facility and now under the wise leadership of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia. Phnom Penh has once again recognized the development.
