General Vong Pisen: The United States Supports the Training of Cambodian Blue Hat Forces and Other Military Cooperation in the Future
During the meeting, General Vong Pisen praised the recent dialogue between Mr. Patrick Murphy and the Prime Minister of Cambodia Samdech Techo Hun Sen, which focused on further strengthening relations and cooperation between the two countries. To be better, especially the message of the President of the United States to Samdech Techo, which clearly states the policy of non-interference in the internal affairs of Cambodia.
The Commander-in-Chief affirmed his continued good cooperation with the United States through exchange visits as well as continued cooperation in the search for the remains of missing US soldiers in Cambodia.
The General also requested the US Ambassador to assist in the training of human resources in the Royal Cambodian Armed Forces, including strengthening the operation of the Cambodian Blue Hat Forces to carry out humanitarian missions under the auspices of the United Nations.
In response, W. Patrick Murphy agreed with the Commander-in-Chief to strengthen the relationship between the two countries. In particular, in the military field, the United States has supported the training of Cambodian Blue Hat forces, along with many other military cooperation in the future.
The US Ambassador also cited previous reports that Cambodia had allowed Chinese military bases on its territory, which the Royal Government of Cambodia had repeatedly denied. It also allows many national and international journalists to visit the suspected places.
The ambassador considered the broadcast to be untrue and intended to destabilize it. General Vong Pisen also reiterated the Cambodian Constitution, which does not allow any article to allow foreign military bases on Cambodian territory, nor to allow its military bases abroad. Except within the framework of the United Nations.
Svay Rieng University and Institute of Technology of Cambodia Sign MoU to Promote Engineering Training for Students
(Svay Rieng): Svay Rieng University and the Institute of Technology of Cambodia have signed a Memorandum of Understanding (MOA) for Cooperation to Promote Science, Technology, Engineering and Mathematics (STEM) Education Under the Higher Education Improvement Project in Cambodia. Supported by the Royal Government and the World Bank through the Ministry of Education, Youth and Sports.
The signing ceremony was held on the morning of December 3, 2019 in the presence of Mr. Dith Um Romney, Director of the Institute of Technology of Cambodia and Mr. Tum Saravuth, Rector of Svay Rieng University at Svay Rieng University.
The purpose of this agreement is that the Institute of Technology of Cambodia will provide technical support to Svay Rieng University in the development of two new engineering majors: mechanical engineering and electrical engineering and automation by sharing the knowledge of experts on software development. Study the training process and human resource training for Svay Rieng University.
According to Mr. Tum Saravuth, the signing of this agreement is very important to expand the construction of human resources for economic development, to respond to the policy of industrial development in Cambodia and to achieve the goals of the Royal Government. Set 2030 as a high middle income country and 2050 as a developed country.
Dr. Oum Romney is optimistic that through this agreement, he believes that it will be fruitful in the next 5 years by building human resources in a capable place and with sufficient quantity for the demand for jobs. The potential of the economic zone in Cambodia, especially the Bavet special economic zone, which has a great need for human resources.
Please be informed that Svay Rieng University will open the Mechanical Engineering major in the academic year 2020-2021 and the electrical engineering and automation major in the upcoming academic year 2021-2022 with the cooperation of the Institute of Technology of Cambodia, University of the Kingdom of Thailand and University of Japan as well.
