APSARA Authority tries to train people to take turns to repair the temple, believing that the damage to the ancient buildings will continue in the future
(Siem Reap): The construction of brick temples in the Angkor area has collapsed due to the age of the construction materials, poor quality, climate change, vegetation, lack of timely maintenance and the lack of experts to preserve the brick temples.
In order to save the ancient cultural heritage from serious risks and pass on the knowledge of the maintenance of the brick temple to the next generation, the APSARA Authority organized a training in November on the successor of the brick temple conservation techniques to the staff-staff. In Angkor Park.
This training course is taught by experts and workers who have many years of experience in repairing brick temples in the past in order to pass on the skills to new staff and less experienced workers to increase the joint capacity to repair, preserve and build brick temples. Continue to repair more because the damage to the ancient temples still exists in the future.
In the teaching, there are both general theory in repairing brick temples and practical application in the repair site (Prasat Lolay), which includes methods for laying bricks and formulas to use as cement to connect bricks to repair ancient temples. .
