Officials of Kampong Cham Provincial Department of Water Resources and Batheay District Authority pump water to save more than 1,000 hectares of people's dry rice fields
(Kampong Cham): Officials of Kampong Cham Provincial Department of Water Resources and Meteorology together with Batheay District Authority on December 3, 2019 are pumping water to save more than 1,000 hectares of dry rice fields.
Mr. Phen Sophal, Governor of Batheay District, said that the intervention to pump water to save rice of the people in Tang Krasang commune, the working group of the Provincial Department of Water Resources used more than 10 25-horsepower machines and nearly 10 in Mepring commune. In addition, to extract water to save rice, people about more than 1,000 hectares.
The district governor said that at the same time, there are some rice people who can not save because they are far from water sources.
(Siem Reap): On the morning of December 3, 2019, Mr. Mam Bunheng, Minister of Health and Mr. Tea Seiha, Governor of Siem Reap Province, visited the victims of the collapse of the building of Sala Chan at Wat Kork Chak. In Veal village, Kork Chak commune, Siem Reap city, who is being treated at Siem Reap Provincial Referral Hospital.
Please be informed that on the afternoon of December 2, 2019, there was an incident of collapse of the building of Sala Chan building at Wat Prasat Kork Chak in Veal village, Sangkat Kork Chak, Siem Reap city. This incident caused 13 monks and people to be seriously injured and 3 people to die.
Senior Minister Kun Kim, First Vice-Chairman of the National Committee for Disaster Management, confirmed to Fresh News that two of the dead were in Siem Reap and one was a resident of Prey Veng. The bodies of the victims were transported to their homes by the authorities and a traditional ceremony was held.
In this incident, Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia and Chairman of the National Committee for Disaster Management decided to provide about 20 million Riels for the dead and 3 million Riels for the injured in the collapse of the building at Wat Prasat. The wolf.
Svay Rieng CamControl Inspected Goods at Veal Yun Market, Svay Rieng City, Found 40kg of Dried Fish and 20 Canned Butter
(Svay Rieng): In order to ensure food safety for the people, CamControl Svay Rieng branch officials in the morning of December 3, 2019, in cooperation with the Provincial Department of Commerce, led a working group to inspect various items in Veal Yun Market. Svay Rieng City, Svay Rieng Province, found defective and expired goods displayed in this market.
Mr. Pheng Nil, President of CamControl Svay Rieng Branch, said that the responsibility for food safety is a joint responsibility of professional institutions, importers, producers, distributors and all consumers, because health is A key factor in the survival of human life.
He said that after inspecting various items in the field market, found defective goods, including 20 cans of butter and 40 kilograms of dried fish, while the seller also agreed to stop selling defective goods. Out of date because they all understand the impact on people's health.
Mr. Pheng Nil appealed to all people to be careful when eating food, to check the date label clearly before buying to eat. In particular, the food that children like to eat must be checked properly before eating to participate in promoting the well-being of all, and CamControl officials will continue to inspect the goods in the markets in Svay Rieng province in the future.
Samdech Krala Hom Sar Kheng also affirmed that people with disabilities in Cambodia are encouraged to participate in all activities in society, to receive respect and dignity, as well as to provide a working environment for people with disabilities in all fields, to disseminate awareness about the field of disability to all. Ministries, public and sub-national administrations, the private sector, civil society and development partners.
The remarks of Samdech Krala Hom Sar Kheng were made this morning, December 3, 2019, on the occasion that Samdech invited the representative of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia at the meeting to review the implementation of the National Strategic Plan on Disability 2014-2018 and Officially promulgated the National Strategic Plan on Disability 2019-2023, as well as the 21st Day of Persons with Disabilities and the 37th International Day of Persons with Disabilities.
Samdech Krala Hom Sar Kheng emphasized that the Royal Government has provided living support services, housing and other community services to people with disabilities and disabled veterans to help them get their basic rights, including Fully participate in the community.
In addition, the right to employment and livelihood opportunities based on the labor market, as well as an open work environment for people with disabilities, are recognized and cared for, and are encouraged by the Royal Government to strictly prohibit discrimination on the basis of disability. On all types of work, including conditions of recruitment, hiring, employment, resume, career development and safe and comfortable working conditions.
He stressed that the improvement of living standards ensures the reduction of poverty of the disabled, the promotion of employment and decent employment are taken care of by the Royal Government, while the state subsidy is implemented. Continuing through the provision of policy regimes. In addition to philanthropists and civil society, as well as development partners also contribute both financial and human resources to achieve greater benefits for people with disabilities in Cambodia.
