* Second: 102 private sector enterprises also recruited a total of 3,792 workers with disabilities.
He added that every year, about 28,000 people with disabilities receive free rehabilitation services of all kinds, along with policy subsidies for travel, food and shelter during the service. .
A bomb blast near Jakarta National Park injures several Indonesian military officials
JAKARTA: Two military officers were injured in an explosion Tuesday near a national park in the Indonesian capital, Jakarta. This is according to the release by CNA on Tuesday, December 3, 2019.
In front of reporters, Jakarta Police Chief Gatot Eddy confirmed that the blast occurred at 7:15 a.m. Tuesday (local time) in the north near the national park. . However, the Indonesian authorities immediately took control of the situation, and the two military officers who were injured in the arms and legs during the exercise were rushed to hospital.
The blast was believed to have been caused by a smoke bomb, but no motive has been identified for the blast. Indonesian authorities are investigating.
