37 Cambodian students receive master's degree scholarships in Australia and New Zealand
(Phnom Penh): Deputy Prime Minister Prak Sokhon, Minister of Foreign Affairs and International Cooperation of Cambodia, this morning (December 3, 2019) met with 37 undergraduate students who have received scholarships to study in Australia. And New Zealand.
Of the 37 students, 21 are Australian scholars and 16 are New Zealand scholars.
On that occasion, Deputy Prime Minister Prak Sokhon congratulated all students who have successfully passed the scholarship exam to study in these two countries. In addition, he instructed all students to make an effort to learn, absorb knowledge and good experiences from other countries to use in our country as well.
Koy Kuong, a spokesman for the Ministry of Foreign Affairs, said that the total number of Australian government scholarships offered to Cambodia from 1994 to 2019 was 853. He said that the New Zealand government provided scholarships to Cambodia from 2005 to 2019, about 285 people.
(Phnom Penh): Mr. Theam Chanpiseth, Investigating Judge of the Phnom Penh Municipal Court, on December 3, 2019, decided to detain the accused named Chut Chivoan, 27 years old, and put him in the Phnom Penh Municipal Prison (PJ) to wait for Later, according to the law, a case of robbery of a citizen's car due to gambling at a casino.
The accused is known to have a role as a serious criminal police officer of the Prey Veng Provincial Police, and the Phnom Penh Municipal Police investigated and arrested in connection with the robbery of a citizen's car.
According to the police report, in the early hours of November 12, 2019, the suspect, Chut Chivoan, left to gamble at NagaWorld Casino and rode a motorbike around Chbar Ampov to meet the victim, an acquaintance named Puth Rithyphet. A 33-year-old taxi driver lives in Trapeang Bon village, Prey Koki commune, Chantrea district, Svay Rieng province to rent a car to return to Prey Veng province.
Upon arrival in Prey Veng, the suspect stopped the victim at the entrance to the East Prey Veng Provincial Police to retrieve the AK rifle from the room, hid it in his backpack, and told the victim to return to Phnom Penh. .
Arriving at the Tiger Brewery, the suspect pulled out a gun from his backpack, threatened and robbed the car and the victim's money, then drove to sleep at a guesthouse in Phnom Penh and then drove into NagaWorld Casino to sell the victim's car for $ 14,000 and escaped.
Immediately after receiving the victim's complaint, on November 15, 2019, the police confiscated the car from Yan Sam Ol at a car wash in Boeung Trabek, Sangkat Boeung Trabek, Khan Chamkar Morn.
It was not until the night of November 27, 2019 that the police detained the suspect at his home in Phonsui Borey, Sangkat Choam Chao I, Khan Por Senchey, Phnom Penh, and finally the Phnom Penh Municipal Court decided to detain him (PJ). Samdech Pichey Sena Tea Banh Inspects the Site of Sala Chan Collapse in Wat Prasat Kork Chak, Siem Reap City
